&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, build, and maintain APIs, services, and large-scale systems that reliably and efficiently handle billions of money movement requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and solve critical production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers to help them grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the company to build new features at large-scale, while improving internal engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a distributed and hybrid team, maintaining open communication and strong connections with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-12+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships nor includes co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language &lt;em&gt;(we understand new languages can be learned on the job so our interview process is language agnostic)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, can work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers’ success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale financial tracking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding and practical knowledge in cloud based services (e.g. gRPC, GraphQL, Docker/Kubernetes, cloud services such as AWS, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UI Platform team, known as Sail, builds the foundations behind Stripe’s Dashboard and many other user interfaces. Sail Services owns the systems that evaluate feature flags and experiments, ingest frontend analytics, and improve Dashboard load times for Stripe’s largest merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build backend-for-frontend capabilities that connect Stripe’s backend systems to its UI platform. This gives product teams a consistent way to build and operate user experiences without recreating the same infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Backend Engineer on the Sail Services team, you’ll help build and evolve the systems that power Stripe’s user interfaces. You’ll independently drive software projects from problem definition through production, working closely with other UI Platform engineers, product teams, and infrastructure partners. Your work will range from APIs and GraphQL integrations to edge systems, architectural migrations, and the tooling needed to operate them safely at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of software projects, aligning on priorities and then independently scoping problems and carrying solutions through design, implementation, testing, rollout, and operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate reliable, scalable APIs and backend systems that support Stripe’s Dashboard, mobile applications, and other user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help modernize Stripe’s UI architecture through incremental migrations, automated validation, shadow traffic, and carefully controlled production rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, observability, performance, and operability of services on critical user paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with frontend, backend, and infrastructure engineers to understand their needs and turn recurring problems into reusable platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted and agentic development workflows to improve implementation, testing, validation, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute thoughtful code reviews, technical discussions, documentation, and runbooks that improve the quality of the team’s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in using AI-assisted and agentic development tools as part of day-to-day software engineering, including critically reviewing, validating, and improving generated code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software engineering experience, or equivalent practical experience, building, shipping, and operating production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of backend technologies and infrastructure, including the fundamentals of APIs, data storage, distributed systems, and production operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently scope and deliver open-ended software projects, making practical technical and product tradeoffs with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills, with attention to testing, maintainability, reliability, and user impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with frontend engineers, product engineers, and infrastructure partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building backend-for-frontend systems, UI platform services, developer platforms, or shared infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or integrating APIs, including GraphQL APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-throughput event ingestion, feature flag or experimentation systems, or other latency-sensitive platform services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with caching, asynchronous systems, configuration systems, or data-consistency tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience executing large migrations using automated validation, shadow traffic, feature flags, or staged rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data, developer feedback, or operational signals to improve a platform or developer-facing product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the gross domestic product of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits team is fundamental to the Stripe experience and directly supports our global workforce. The team ensures that our programs are competitive, clearly understood, and compliant with local regulations across 30 countries. We continually update our benefits strategy to meet the diverse needs of Stripe and Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits Program Manager plays a key role in shaping the strategy, execution, and user experience of our benefits programs. This role focuses primarily on benefits strategy and plan design, financial stewardship, vendor management, communications, the Stripe experience, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is suited to someone who can think strategically while supporting the successful execution of day-to-day operations and our broader benefits strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of our benefits programs, including market research, benchmarking, plan design, vendor selection and management, annual renewals and negotiations, communications, administration, security reviews, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends and regulatory changes, and recommend new or updated programs that align with Stripe’s business and Total Rewards strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert and develop clear communication plans that help Stripes understand our programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for benefits vendors, brokers, and third-party administrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and evaluate potential vendors, and manage the request for proposal process in partnership with Procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess vendor performance and manage contracts in partnership with Legal, ensuring that vendors meet their contractual commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compile, analyze, and report on key benefits metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with People Partners, People Consultants, Finance, Payroll, Employee Relations, and Legal to support a coordinated approach to our benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance to manage the benefits budget, prepare cost projections, and evaluate the return on investment of new and existing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Workday and our benefits administration platform to improve workflows and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems to deliver key initiatives and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you’re encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 to 7 years of experience in a benefits role with similar responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and improving employee benefits programs using data, Stripe feedback, and financial analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of government regulations related to employee benefits and time off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing pension and time-off plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using benefits administration platforms, such as Workday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing stakeholders and negotiating contracts with benefits vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, growing environment, preferably in a technology company or large-scale organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive projects independently, identify and raise issues, and seek feedback when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment, with the ability to make decisions that align with Stripe’s culture and benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing change initiatives related to benefits programs, including vendor or system implementations and transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced data analysis and financial forecasting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mergers and acquisitions and benefits integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Security Engineer to build and scale the Bridge security foundation. This is a rare opportunity to design a security program from the ground up, while also leveraging the infrastructure, best practices, and tooling of one of the most mature security organizations in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement the Bridge security roadmap from first principles to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and tackle the most important Bridge security risks quickly and pragmatically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with Stripe infrastructure where it makes sense, and find custom solutions where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead threat modeling and hardening efforts for the Bridge money movement systems in collaboration with crypto and infra teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build key security capabilities, including monitoring, secrets management, incident response, access controls, and CI/CD hardening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce engineering best practices around secure development and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Bridge meets compliance and audit expectations as we scale to more regulated markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product, and the Stripe security organization to move fast without compromising safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in Security engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling security programs at a startup or in an embedded role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced startup environments, building security practices from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup mindset—scrappy, pragmatic, and quick to solve the most critical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort writing and debugging backend application code, with Ruby experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and ability to ruthlessly prioritize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance security rigor with speed, especially in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication across technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in the potential of crypto and stablecoins to power global financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Accounting team at Stripe supports products across Stripe by providing guidance on accounting implications and enabling teams to make informed strategic decisions. The team records business transactions accurately and on time in the balance sheet and income statement, and partners with cross-functional and international teams in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an experienced accountant to join our world-class accounting team, focusing on products developed by our Bridge subsidiary. You’ll leverage your technical expertise with U.S. GAAP to identify accounting implications and customer impacts and advise cross-functional partners. You will be responsible for ensuring timely and accurate month-end close results for Bridge products, while also working on initiatives to create scalable accounting solutions..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly close activities, including journal entries, reconciliations, analytic reviews, and financial reporting deliverables for Bridge products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recommend and implement scalable accounting processes to support global growth at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our business and finance teams to understand new products, features, and contracts, and advise on accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Internal Systems and Engineering teams to improve financial systems and automate accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the effectiveness of internal controls and design processes and controls for emerging business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand data and system flows, analyzing financial results to identify and address anomalies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting and/or industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional accountancy qualification, such as CA, CPA, ACA, ACCA, or CIMA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP and experience with internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monthly or quarterly close processes, journal-entry preparation and posting, audits, regulatory reporting, financial-statement preparation, and accounting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous work and build systems and automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience accounting for cryptocurrencies, including stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Oracle Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data-querying and analysis tools, including SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to relevant US GAAP standards, e.g. ASC 860, ASC 606, or ASC 326, is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is responsible for driving organizational effectiveness and leading transformational programs across Marketing, Self-serve, Startup and Sales Development. We create the processes and conditions that enable high performance across teams and help Stripe scale with focus and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We partner closely with the CMO, Marketing and Sales Development leadership team to define strategy, lead operational planning, and steward execution across global programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work spans cross-functional efforts that are critical to Stripe’s growth. From delivering strategic insights and frameworks to leading complex initiatives, we focus on what moves the needle most for the business. We care about results, not activity, and we have fun doing it. If you like hard problems, are analytical, and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Campaign Strategy &amp;amp; Operations Manager, you&#39;ll own the operational foundation that powers Stripe&#39;s global demand engine — building the systems, processes, and workflows that enable our marketing teams to move faster and perform better at scale. You&#39;ll partner with the Global Campaigns, Demand, and Field Marketing teams to drive strategic planning, design operational processes such as budget management and resource planning, and collaborate across global, regional, and channel teams to execute the end-to-end campaign lifecycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility, high-impact role at the intersection of marketing strategy and operational execution — one where the work you build today shapes how the entire demand function operates for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Campaigns, Demand and Field Marketing leadership team on operating cadences and processes, including monthly and quarterly business reviews, annual planning, budget and resource allocation, org-wide goal setting, and communications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global, regional, and channel teams to architect and implement scalable operating models to support the end-to-end campaign &amp;amp; event lifecycle, from initial strategy and planning through execution, measurement, and optimization, ensuring seamless integration across various functions and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently monitor and analyze the campaign production &amp;amp; activation &quot;supply chain&quot; including tracking all key stages, handoffs, and friction points to drive meaningful efficiency gains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently scope and lead strategic programs to solve high-impact problems. This includes developing frameworks, aligning stakeholders, and ensuring execution drives measurable outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and report out on key operational metrics and team performance, clearly communicating the health of the campaign &amp;amp; event supply chain, the impact of operational improvements, and the overall effectiveness of campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage campaign and event analytics to do ad-hoc, deep-dives on user engagement patterns, conversion trends, and growth opportunities across the demand funnel. Use these insights to shape hypotheses, drive prioritization conversations, and identify areas to probe more deeply in partnership with Marketing, Finance and GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clarity to ambiguity. You’ll navigate complexity, distill insight from noise, resolve issues quickly, and empower teams to make smart, confident decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of demand generation, campaign &amp;amp; marketing operations, strategy and operations, business operations, or similar roles with exposure to both business and technical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in partnering with regional teams and channel partners to build scalable, end-to-end demand generation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deploy AI-powered solutions within campaigns or demand generation with specific, measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross-functional settings, and in a role that spans strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation, writing, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appetite and ability to work through ambiguity with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change management background and ability to influence diverse stakeholder groups across global, regional, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of marketing and how its varied disciplines work together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management tools such as Asana, Monday.com, or Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Marketing automation systems and tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, finance, fintech, or high-growth technology companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in management consulting or program management roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enhance all aspects of our global corporate cash investment program, including strategies, policies and systems/operations, performance and risk metrics;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and synthesize trends in global financial markets and macroeconomic developments;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with financial partners such as asset managers, custodians and service providers;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners, as well as external stakeholders, to unlock and manage global interest income opportunities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build observability tools and deliver data insights relating to investments and yield optimization;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify capital markets system needs and work with the respective teams to build the required infrastructure;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Capital Markets team in executing complex projects by assuming project and cross-functional coordination responsibilities; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the strategy and execution of the Capital Markets team long term roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Business, Math, Economics, Finance, Statistics, Engineering or related field, plus 7 years of experience in Capital Markets or Corporate Treasury of which, at least 5 years must be post bachelors, progressive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have 7 years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investments, interest rate risk management, and global cash management;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed income, interest rate derivatives, FX, hedging strategies, and analyzing macroeconomic trends;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating financial forecasts and models; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial markets, FX or Fixed Income, in G10 or emerging markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5 years of experience in running deadline-oriented deals or projects, including planning, stakeholder management, operational best practices, and tracking results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;2 years of experience in Bloomberg Terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $199,222 - $235,200/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. NY55&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a high potential candidate to join Stripe’s Alliances and Channels (A&amp;amp;C) team as a Channel Sales Executive. The Channel Sales Executive (CSE) is a key part of the Alliances and Channels team, supporting platform partners that embed Stripe technology into their solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic Channel Sales professional to drive business growth with a portfolio of SaaS Platforms. You will identify high-value opportunities, develop demand with these platforms, and foster new business within our partner ecosystem. Working closely with Partner Development Managers and Stripe Account Executives, you will be responsible for delivering incremental growth of new users and revenue through your portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint go-to-market and co-selling initiatives with a designated and diverse portfolio of SaaS platforms in a channel sales motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with platform counterparts to drive net new demand for partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the joint value proposition and lead account mapping workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sales strategies to expand Stripe’s revenue with strategic platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full deal cycle with partners, from sourcing new pipeline, opportunity progression to closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for partners within Stripe, representing Stripe within the partner&#39;s organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate sales and partner activities in Salesforce.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Who you are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technology sales experience with a proven track record of exceeding sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the payments, commerce, and/or Q2C landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience working in multi-party sales pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to speak to functional leadership both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and be a team player on cross-functional deal pursuit teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel (25%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute territory and opportunity-specific plans leveraging tools such as Salesforce and Crossbeam.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Alliances and Channels (A&amp;amp;C) team supports platform partners that embed Stripe technology in their solutions. As a Channel Sales Executive (CSE), you will help build demand and create growth opportunities across Stripe’s partner ecosystem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You will drive business growth across a portfolio of software-as-a-service (SaaS) platforms. You will identify high-value opportunities, develop demand with platform partners, and build new business within the partner ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Partner Development Managers and Stripe Account Executives, you will drive growth in new users and revenue across your portfolio. You will help Stripe and its partners establish joint value propositions, identify shared account opportunities, and move opportunities through the deal cycle.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint go-to-market and co-selling initiatives with a designated portfolio of SaaS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with platform counterparts to generate net-new demand for partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the joint value proposition, and lead account-mapping workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sales strategies to expand Stripe revenue with strategic platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full deal cycle with partners, from sourcing pipeline and advancing opportunities through closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for partners within Stripe, and represent Stripe within partner organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate sales and partner activity records in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technology sales experience, with a track record of exceeding sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, commerce, and/or the quote-to-cash (Q2C) landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in and leading cross-functional, multi-party sales pursuits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute territory and opportunity-specific plans, leveraging tools such as Salesforce and Crossbeam&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills, including the ability to communicate with functional leaders internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To avoid the worst effects of climate change, most climate models agree the world will need to dramatically reduce emissions &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; remove 5-10 billion tons of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere per year by 2050. The Climate team’s goal is to accelerate Stripe’s path to net zero in parallel with the world’s. We do this by reducing Stripe’s emissions and leading initiatives to increase the likelihood we build sufficient carbon removal capacity to reach global climate goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2019, we developed the first measurement of Stripe’s emissions. In 2021 we launched&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/climate&quot;&gt; Stripe Climate&lt;/a&gt;, enabling merchants to direct a fraction of their revenue to help scale emerging carbon removal technologies. In 2022 we launched &lt;a href=&quot;https://frontierclimate.com/&quot;&gt;Frontier&lt;/a&gt;, an advance market commitment to buy $1.8B+ of permanent carbon removal by 2040. In 2024, we entered our first multi-year offtake for clean energy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, Stripe’s corporate net zero program is entering a new phase. We are looking to streamline our emissions measurement, create a template for catalytic emission reductions, and champion buying removals on the path to net zero, all while meeting our expanding global ESG disclosure requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s Climate Program Manager, you will set the strategy and lead the execution and reporting for Stripe’s corporate net zero program. You’ll partner with a wide range of stakeholders within and outside of Stripe – Accounting, Finance, Legal, Procurement, Facilities, Sales, and carbon accounting and assurance providers – to refine our greenhouse gas inventory, deliver a reduction and removal roadmap that meets our climate targets, and provide inputs to global ESG disclosures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone with expertise in carbon accounting and reductions strategy, sharp program and process management, a track record of getting big things done fast, and excellent judgement to make the ‘right’ recommendations for Stripe’s program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Net Zero strategy (~15%): &lt;/strong&gt;Own and evolve Stripe’s corporate net zero strategy, including Stripe’s transition plan, priorities, budget, annual goals, emissions forecasts, removal retirements, and progress tracking. Stay current on evolving disclosure requirements, net zero guidance, and industry best practices to ensure Stripe’s program is high impact and best in class&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions measurement (~30%): &lt;/strong&gt;Build Stripe’s annual greenhouse gas inventory. Collect data inputs, evolve methodology, manage Stripe’s footprint vendors, run a rigorous and auditable process with cross-functional stakeholders, and identify opportunities to use AI to improve the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions reporting (~30%):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Serve as Stripe’s subject-matter expert to deliver inputs to ESG controllership for regulatory disclosures and to customers for RFPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduction program (~25%):&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and manage emissions reduction initiatives across Stripe. This will include efforts like securing renewable electricity for Stripe’s scope 2 emissions, as well as supporting the creative and high-impact interventions like carbon removal or lower-emission data centers that we need to reach global net zero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA or BS degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in corporate sustainability, climate strategy, carbon accounting, environmental consulting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills – especially adept at translating complexity into clear recommendations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of generating and implementing ambitious emissions reduction initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative skills and expertise in emissions accounting and Greenhouse Gas Protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led a corporate climate program in a sector with a significant Scope 3 footprint, ideally technology or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a self-starter, and has a proven track record of producing measurable reductions through clean energy, cloud usage, and other supplier engagement initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a working knowledge of major emissions accounting and climate reporting standards and requirements (e.g., CSRD, California SB 253, GHG protocol), and experience with Watershed or similar enterprise carbon management&amp;nbsp; platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience partnering with cross functional controllership partners to manage a greenhouse gas inventory process that meets requirements for limited or reasonable assurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is an exceptionally fast learner. Enjoys (and has experience) quickly ramping on new reduction technologies and sustainability standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe powers businesses all over the world. We process payments, run marketplaces, detect fraud, help entrepreneurs start a business from anywhere in the world, build world-class developer-friendly APIs, and more. Nearly every system we operate interacts with sensitive financial or personal data—making security a top priority for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe will succeed at our mission of increasing the GDP of the internet only if we prove ourselves worthy of our users&#39; trust. As an engineer on the Security team, you&#39;ll design and develop frameworks, systems, and solutions to ensure the security of Stripe&#39;s engineering infrastructure and, most importantly, privacy of our users&#39; data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Cloud Security team accelerates Stripe&#39;s business priorities by building core security controls and services that empower teams to build quickly and securely on top of a well-governed cloud platform and partnering with infrastructure teams to advance select critical business priorities using novel infrastructure or integrations as that platform expands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate the core security infrastructure used by all of Stripe&#39;s engineering teams in close collaboration with other stakeholders and our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold our high engineering standards and bring consistency to the many codebases and processes you&#39;ll encounter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team learning by improving engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build durable solutions that will advance Stripe&#39;s security beyond the state of the art&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help expand Stripe&#39;s cloud footprint on top of secure, paved roads and guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize for security controls that have delightful user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with infrastructure and engineering teams building integrations with our cloud infrastructure or adopting new cloud managed services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make impactful decisions about systems and security—their edge cases, failure modes, and life cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to determine appropriate baselines against which to measure security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define infrastructure that reliably feeds signals to threat teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and prototype new security tools and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may work on&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing controls that support security invariants and enforce our security principles while providing a surprisingly great user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing a migration path for newly acquired companies onto the Stripe Secure Platform, embedding with their engineers and biasing for action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI tooling for platform-related configuration, including IAM roles, SCPs, and associated components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guardrails and security controls for both commonly used and newer cloud technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding our cloud identity infrastructure to provide paved paths for AI and agentic access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation tooling for continually driving down permissions and access across our cloud services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, strong communication skills, and a deep respect for the power of collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A learning mindset, regardless of level or experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive clear next steps when encountering ambiguous spaces without clear lines of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards for code quality and a constructive attitude to help others raise the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering experience in a high-stakes production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for considering how systems can fail and how to fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security on one or more of AWS, Azure, or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting threat modeling of software or infrastructure in cloud-native environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux systems, Kubernetes, and container-based platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior usage of security monitoring tools (e.g., CSPM, CNAAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a multi-cloud or complex cloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for considering how systems can fail and how to fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Commercial Sales team is responsible for the acquisition, growth, retention, and expansion of mid-market customers. As a Grower Commercial Account Executive, you’ll set strategy for your territory, identify opportunities for existing customers to get the most out of Stripe, execute scaled sales strategies to grow revenue and drive end-to-end campaigns to nurture relationships and increase adoption of Stripe products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth and expanding revenue from Stripe’s existing mid-market customers. In this role, you will also help build out a new team touching more of our install base and GTM motion at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate upsell opportunities to drive revenue growth in your territory&lt;/li&gt;
