&lt;li&gt;Passion for learning new functions and features of technical products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Accounting Team is responsible for supporting all products at Stripe, consulting on accounting implications, and supporting teams&#39; ability to make informed strategic decisions. We are responsible for the accurate and timely recording of all business-generated transactions on our balance sheet and income statement. We operate in a fast-paced environment and collaborate significantly with cross-functional and international teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an experienced accountant to join our world-class accounting team. In this role, you will support revenue and cost accounting for products developed by our Bridge subsidiary, leveraging your technical expertise with U.S. GAAP, specifically ASC 606, to quickly identify accounting implications and impacts on customers while advising and collaborating with team members cross-functionally to develop operational processes that help us scale. Ideally, you will have both public accounting and industry experience in tech or financial services, as well as experience working for companies with a high volume of complex transactions and issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own P&amp;amp;L accounting for Bridge&#39;s products, including journal entries, reconciliations, variance analyses, financial reporting deliverables, and analytical reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Bridge&#39;s product, go-to-market, and finance partners to thoroughly understand new products, features, and contracts, and advise on accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal systems and engineering teams to support internal financial systems and automation of accounting processes, and identify, recommend, and implement scalable accounting processes to support global growth at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and prepare technical accounting analyses, assess the effectiveness of internal controls, and design new processes and controls for emerging and growing business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand data and system flows, analyze financial results to identify and address anomalies, and support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting or industry experience, with a B.A. or B.S. degree in Accounting or Finance (CPA strongly preferred), experience accounting for cryptocurrencies including stablecoins, and experience with SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in U.S. GAAP and ability to research complex accounting issues, with a proven track record of managing high volumes of complex transactions and financial issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences, and demonstrated success working collaboratively and influencing cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on challenging projects and producing results with excellent attention to detail, and a solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices and challenging existing processes to identify improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of or experience in the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Go-to-Market Enablement develops the capabilities that help Stripe’s customer-facing teams deliver greater value to users. We align expectations for role excellence, build practical learning experiences, and equip managers to reinforce new skills and behaviors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Customer Success Managers are ongoing partners to some of our largest users after they begin using Stripe. They help users understand the health of their business on Stripe, address challenges, and identify opportunities to get more value from our products. Through regular business reviews and account engagement, they connect users’ priorities with how Stripe can support their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success Enablement Business Partner will support these teams from onboarding through ongoing development, connecting global enablement programs with the priorities of Customer Success leaders, managers, and teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll serve as the strategic enablement partner to Customer Success leadership, helping identify the skills, knowledge, and practices that Customer Success Managers need to support their users effectively. You’ll translate those needs into a focused enablement roadmap and work with global program owners, Customer Success Operations, and subject matter experts to deliver it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring an understanding of customer success work and combine strategic partnership with hands-on execution. That includes shaping role-specific learning offerings, equipping managers to reinforce skills, and using data and feedback to evaluate what’s working. You’ll also make clear tradeoffs about priorities, protect the team’s time, and connect stakeholders with the right expertise across enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Success leadership to define and execute an enablement strategy aligned with business priorities, role expectations, and performance needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape onboarding and ongoing development for CSMs, building role-specific offerings and coordinating handoffs for ongoing administration and management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the governance, roadmaps, and operating rhythms needed to prioritize requests, manage dependencies, and deliver complex programs with consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Customer Success Operations, technical enablement, Product, and Marketing to prepare teams for evolving products, processes, tools, and user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an enablement roadmap, manage cross-functional dependencies, and communicate priorities, progress, and tradeoffs to leaders and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use conversation intelligence, learning and competency data, business indicators, and field feedback to identify needs and evaluate enablement effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead learning sessions and equip managers to reinforce skills through practice, coaching, assessment, and feedback&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in customer success, professional services, enablement, program management, or a related field supporting post-sales or customer-facing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the customer success role, demonstrated through direct experience or close partnership with customer success teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, cross-functional programs, including setting priorities, managing dependencies, and coordinating execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with senior stakeholders, communicating recommendations and tradeoffs, and translating business needs into practical programs, resources, or guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data and stakeholder feedback to identify performance needs, evaluate results, and improve programs or ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or delivering onboarding, training, or ongoing enablement for customer-facing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting customer success teams serving large enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving an enablement program, service model, or governance framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across regions and time zones within a global, matrixed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with conversation intelligence, learning platforms, workflow automation, or applications of artificial intelligence in enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Customer Success Managers (CSM) oversee the post-sales lifecycle for Stripe users, ensuring they realize the maximum value of their investment. This partnership drives user success, increases retention and expansion, and supports mutually beneficial renewal outcomes. Few roles provide such a direct impact on the growth of the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a motivated and curious professional to manage a book of enterprise customers. The CSM will deliver proactive workshops, business reviews, payments insights, and thought leadership to help users grow their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is detail-oriented and meticulous, and enjoys engaging customers to investigate issues and deliver insights. This role involves working closely with sales, technical account managers, and operations teams to engage customers in product, payment, and technical conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner closely with account executives and technical account managers to support post-sale engagements focused on the optimization, retention, and growth of Stripe&#39;s enterprise customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Manage a book of customers to drive overall account health including performance, product adoption, usage velocity, account renewals and growth, referrals, and customer satisfaction&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Serve as a trusted payments and product advisor to managed customers by delivering payment performance and industry insights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Perform business reviews to align on user priorities, review payments performance metrics, share Stripe product roadmap, and provide guidance on how to optimize the value from Stripe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Advocate for the customer to internal stakeholders. Share customer feedback and insights to Product Management, Engineering, Support, Marketing, and Sales on the innovation and improvement needed to optimize the Stripe user experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• In coordination with an account team, support book expansion—identifying and surfacing opportunities to ensure customers are successful&lt;/p&gt;
