&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue and Financial Automation (RFA) teams create solutions that empower businesses to optimize their revenue operations. A significant component of RFA is the Revenue team, which is one of our fastest-growing product areas and helps businesses manage and scale their revenue effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Orchestration team builds the foundational execution engines, background job processing frameworks, and asynchronous event platforms that power Stripe’s global billing infrastructure. We own the core execution primitives and platform systems that orchestrate the end-to-end financial lifecycle for millions of businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe’s scale, the Orchestration team sits at the intersection of high-throughput distributed systems and mission-critical financial reliability. Our job processing and event scheduling platforms execute millions of scheduled workloads and asynchronous tasks daily with extreme precision, handling everything from global recurring billing cycles to complex time-dependent execution workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe expands to support complex monetization models and enterprise scale, our team is architecting the next generation of core platform infrastructure. We build highly leveraged primitives and foundational frameworks that enable product teams across Stripe to innovate rapidly while operating on an uncompromising foundation of reliability, fault tolerance, and global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Stripe, you will play a pivotal role in driving the success of your team and the broader organization. Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading engineering and design processes, coaching, mentoring, and supporting your team as they build innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with stakeholders across product, design, infrastructure, and operations to ensure alignment on projects and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning problems from end-to-end by managing diverse systems, processes, and technologies, while continuously seeking opportunities to optimize efficiency and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upholding high engineering standards, ensuring consistency across codebases, and implementing best practices throughout your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiting top engineering talent in partnership with Stripe’s recruiting team to build a diverse and high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting your team members&#39; career growth by providing insights and development opportunities tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications below, with preferred qualifications that would be advantageous but are not required. If you meet the minimum requirement, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing and growing teams of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record managing a team of 5+ software engineers focused on building and shipping products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, with a history of creatively tackling complex challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in cross-functional environments, demonstrating rigorous thinking and effective decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in dealing with ambiguity and executing on multiple high-impact work streams simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to fostering a supportive, feedback-driven, and challenging work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency to engage thoughtfully with engineers about architecture and product design, offering valuable insights when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset of autonomy and entrepreneurship, where you&#39;re excited to take responsibility and drive initiatives forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignment with Stripe’s Operating Principles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will embody our &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/jobs/culture&quot;&gt;operating principles&lt;/a&gt; by maintaining a focus on user outcomes, fostering open communication and cross-team collaboration, and embracing an iterative approach to both product development and team management. You will make decisions that reflect our commitment to integrity, excellence, and the long-term success of our users and the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about empowering engineers and driving impactful projects in a dynamic environment, we would love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testability has long been a priority for Stripe. Before users trust code with their money, they need to verify that it’s safe and correct. This need drove Stripe to build test mode and, more recently, Sandboxes, which enables safe, isolated, and scalable testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As businesses build with AI and agents, their testing needs are evolving. Stripe customers use claimable sandboxes to add Stripe capabilities to prototypes before business registration. Once onboarded, they provision isolated test environments to support agents’ exploration. These capabilities help developers and agents build and test their integrations with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sandboxes team defines, builds, and operates these testing capabilities. We work across Stripe to make our products testable, helping businesses develop with confidence and shaping the future of Stripe’s developer platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead and grow the Sandboxes engineering team, setting technical direction and operating critical systems. You’ll build a culture of operational excellence and thoughtful product development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work directly with users to understand their needs and partner with Product, Design, and Data Science to shape and deliver the team’s strategy. The role combines building reusable testing capabilities across Stripe with attention to the details that make developer tools effective and easy to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering planning and execution, partnering with Design to build clear, useful testing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the team’s strategy and roadmap, aligning partners across Product, Design, Infrastructure, Marketing, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery from problem definition through rollout and ongoing operation, improving both system performance and the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold high engineering standards across the team’s codebases and development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Recruiting to hire engineers and build a diverse, high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor engineers, provide candid feedback, and support career development tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers building and shipping products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full-time software development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building reusable, extensible software that supports a range of user needs, with strong user empathy and a commitment to high-quality user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, with a track record of finding practical solutions to complex challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning ambiguous goals into clear priorities and delivering multiple high-impact workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building a supportive environment with candid feedback and high expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to guide architecture and product design discussions and help engineers make informed tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking ownership of initiatives and moving work forward independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product and design judgment, including the ability to simplify complex user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making decisions and building strong working relationships across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading a distributed team across multiple locations and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer tools or platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building testing tools or capabilities that help users test within a product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI agent systems or tools that support agent-driven development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Self Serve Direct Onboarding helps businesses start using Stripe’s products quickly and confidently. The team builds self-service experiences that guide users through providing business information and completing required checks. We turn complex financial, regulatory, and verification requirements into clear steps, shaping both how quickly businesses can get started and the trust they place in Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of this work is a shared product activation experience: a consistent way for businesses to start using new financial capabilities as they grow. This foundation helps users avoid repeating information and makes it simpler for product teams to integrate onboarding into their offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI creates an opportunity to rethink how businesses get started on Stripe. The team is designing onboarding journeys for users who interact directly through a user interface, work with AI agents, or delegate onboarding to agents entirely. We’re improving today’s experience while building the foundations for agent-led onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll set engineering direction in partnership with Product and Design and develop the team delivering it. The role combines improving activation today with shaping how onboarding works for people and AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll use strong product judgment to decide where to experiment, where to build reusable foundations, and how to measure progress through faster activation, fewer repeated steps, and reliable outcomes. You’ll work across Stripe to align teams and resolve dependencies, while coaching engineers and giving them meaningful ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering planning and execution, partnering closely with Product and Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the team’s strategy and roadmap, aligning partners across product engineering, Risk, Compliance, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery from problem definition through rollout and ongoing operation, using experimentation to improve activation while maintaining risk controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold high engineering standards across the team’s codebases and development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguous goals into focused plans, resolve dependencies, and balance new capabilities with operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor engineers, provide candid feedback, and support career development tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Recruiting to hire engineers and build a diverse, high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers building and shipping products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full-time software development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user-facing products, with strong user empathy and product judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning ambiguous goals into clear priorities and delivering work that depends on multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of coaching engineers, supporting their growth, and building an environment of candid feedback, inclusion, and shared ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to guide architecture and make pragmatic tradeoffs across user interfaces, APIs, backend workflows, and production reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to align technical and nontechnical partners with different priorities and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience simplifying complex customer journeys and using data, user feedback, and experimentation to evaluate outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience modernizing an established product or architecture while continuing to ship improvements and maintain production reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI-assisted workflows or agent-facing APIs, with clear approaches to evaluating quality and correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Premium Support Experience team builds products to enable, support, and grow businesses in their usage of Stripe. Our Dublin-based team is a startup within Stripe, building a greenfield product to provide a high-quality, differentiated support experience for our largest, most complex, and most engaged users. Besides building directly for Stripe&#39;s users, we&#39;re responsible for improving internal tooling and processes that set the foundations for their end-to-end experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is part of the Support Experience engineering organization, which builds and improves Stripe&#39;s user support from end to end: how users get help within our products, how they get in touch with us when they have questions, and how our teams use internal tools to answer those questions. Providing great support to users of all sizes is culturally important to everyone at Stripe. We partner closely with Stripe&#39;s design, product, and operational teams, and we&#39;re using the latest generative AI technologies to re-imagine support experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of a new engineering team, your role is closer to a founding engineering manager at a startup within Stripe. You&#39;ll build and grow the team, set its technical direction, and establish a culture of technical excellence and fast, sustained product delivery. You&#39;ll partner with Product and other cross-functional leaders across the company to define and drive the long-term vision for how Stripe serves its users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your team will design, build, and operate production systems with an emphasis on extensibility, reliability, and usability. It will deliver high-quality end-to-end product experiences built around a deep understanding of user needs. You&#39;ll lead your team to use the best tools for each job, whether that means AI-enabled product experiences or proven techniques for building scalable distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, lead, and manage a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the team&#39;s culture from the ground up, fostering a collaborative and inclusive environment that promotes innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Management, Design, and key leaders across the company to understand user needs and translate them into a technical vision and roadmap aligned with business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects across the full development lifecycle, from planning to delivery, while upholding high standards of quality and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make effective tradeoffs across short- and long-term roadmaps, balancing business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable technical foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders to integrate internal tooling and processes into differentiated workflows, navigating organizational complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with stakeholders, providing regular updates on progress, risks, and challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing teams that build and operate full-stack web applications at scale, and 10+ years of overall industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited and built great teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize competing requirements and stakeholders to iteratively ship new product features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User empathy and a customer-centric approach to problem solving and product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The desire to encourage a healthy, inclusive work environment that&#39;s both supportive and challenging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication with technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new team or product from an early stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with full-stack development, particularly using React and Ruby&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, deploying, and owning agentic LLM solutions (e.g., multi-step orchestrators, tool use/function calling) for complex customer support or workflow automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable planning in quarters while setting a vision for several years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe&#39;s organization to provide a wonderful experience to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a platform company powering businesses all over the world, Stripe processes payments, runs marketplaces, detects fraud, helps entrepreneurs start internet businesses from anywhere in the world, builds world-class developer-friendly APIs, and more. The engineering teams at Stripe work on the business logic for all of that. As a software engineering manager at Stripe, you&#39;ll lead teams that build and expand APIs, services, and experiences. You&#39;ll also work with partners to launch new markets and vertical capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps our users extend their online presence to the physical world. The mission of the Terminal team is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has done for online payments—building for Unified Commerce. With Terminal, businesses can unify their in-person and online experiences, unlocking payments use cases that are right for their business model—whether it&#39;s creating a modern retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling a mobile point-of-sale at their next event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Terminal, the Commerce team focuses on the following to help make Unified Commerce a reality for businesses across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise features—on-reader forms, tipping, gift cards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payment features—DCC, surcharge, multi-capture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Point-of-sale integrations—enterprise-focused integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-code and no-code—solutions that will enable our users to onboard quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on the Terminal Commerce Experience team, you&#39;ll launch and scale Unified Commerce experiences within Stripe Terminal, drive new end-customer and merchant features, and build POS integrations from the ground up to support large-scale enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across Stripe to create and drive toward the vision of Unified Commerce, bringing in-person and online payments together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the roadmap and priorities for your team, and work with dependencies across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the engineering team in achieving a high level of technical excellence and stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage processes to help the team do its best work and interface effectively with the rest of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit excellent engineers in collaboration with the Stripe recruiting team and develop engineers on the team, helping them advance in their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand core Stripe APIs, influence design to interplay with card-present payments, and build a platform for Unified Commerce with your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower and guide your team to build and scale integrations and core abstractions across payment methods, gift cards, and point-of-sale connectors for large-scale enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive table stakes features like surcharging and tipping across Enterprise and SaaS platform merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical background with 5+ years of experience in engineering leadership across &lt;strong&gt;mobile&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;API&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;strong&gt;backend&lt;/strong&gt; development teams and demonstrated broad technical leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building diverse teams to tackle challenging technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the impact of AI and a strong product mindset to turn emerging capabilities into clear customer and business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in a collaborative environment involving different stakeholders and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how to build and manage scalable, resilient, and observable systems across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to listen well and internalize the best ideas from all over the organization while also setting a vision that others are excited to get behind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to put yourself in the shoes of our merchants and users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large technical projects with internal and external dependencies and impact across many teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience building or managing teams who have built in-person checkout experiences or payment method integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with in-person payments hardware and software such as card readers and firmware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the payments industry as a whole&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a platform company powering businesses around the world, Stripe processes payments, runs marketplaces, detects fraud, helps entrepreneurs start internet businesses from anywhere, builds world-class, developer-friendly APIs, and more. Stripe’s engineering teams build the business logic that powers all of this. As a software engineering manager at Stripe, you’ll lead teams that build and expand APIs, services, and experiences. You’ll also work with partners to launch new markets and vertical capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps our users extend their online presence into the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make accepting in-person payments as easy as the Stripe API has made accepting online payments—enabling unified commerce. With Terminal, businesses can unify their in-person and online experiences, unlocking payment use cases that fit their business models—whether they’re creating a modern retail experience, extending a website to a pop-up store, or enabling mobile point-of-sale payments at an event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Terminal, the Enterprise team enables our largest and most influential merchants to scale their businesses globally through:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise features, including in-person refunds, loyalty, and DCC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise-focused point-of-sale integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vertical-specific payment methods, including SNAP EBT, Link integrations, merchant-specific QR payments, private-label credit cards and gift cards, and fleet fuel cards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on the Terminal Enterprise Features team, you’ll launch and scale merchant-specific features, build shared tooling for Terminal’s largest merchants, and partner with cross-functional teams across Stripe, including Go-to-Market, Legal, Design, and Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Stripe leaders across the company to create and advance the vision for Stripe’s unified commerce offering, bringing in-person and online payments together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the roadmap and priorities for your team and coordinate dependencies across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the engineering team in achieving a high level of technical excellence and stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop processes that help the team do its best work and collaborate effectively with the rest of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit excellent engineers in partnership with Stripe’s Recruiting team and develop engineers on the team, helping them advance in their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of core Stripe APIs and influence their design to work effectively with card-present payments while building a platform for unified commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower and guide your team to build and scale integrations and core abstractions across payment methods, gift cards, and point-of-sale connectors for large enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver essential enterprise features such as DCC and in-person refunds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in engineering leadership across mobile, API, and backend development teams, with demonstrated broad technical leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building diverse teams to tackle challenging technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of AI’s impact and a strong product mindset, with the ability to turn emerging capabilities into clear customer and business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in a collaborative environment involving different stakeholders and subject-matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and managing scalable, resilient, and observable systems across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to listen well, internalize the best ideas from across the organization, and set a vision that others are excited to support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to put yourself in the shoes of Stripe’s merchants and users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large technical projects with internal and external dependencies and impact across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience building, or managing teams that have built, in-person checkout experiences or payment-method integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with in-person payment hardware and software, such as card readers and firmware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on the Enterprise team at Stripe, you&#39;ll drive future growth at Stripe by building new relationships with prospective companies, turning them into happy Stripe users. You&#39;ll manage and elevate relationships with a named account list within a key vertical while identifying new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations. This role will be dedicated to accounts focused in ANZ&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, you will own a portfolio of established enterprise customers and drive their continued growth with Stripe. This is a hunting role within existing accounts: you will identify new opportunities to increase payment volume, activate additional products, expand Stripe’s footprint across business units and subsidiaries, and build long-term customer stickiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will create and execute account strategies for complex technology customers, engaging both executive and technical stakeholders to understand their priorities and translate Stripe’s platform into clear commercial and operational value. The role spans the full expansion cycle, from account planning and opportunity creation through commercial negotiation, activation, and post-launch growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially ambitious and highly autonomous seller who can balance near-term revenue delivery with the long-term relationship building required to grow a strategic book of business. You should be comfortable navigating technical and business conversations with leaders across the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named portfolio of existing enterprise customers and develop strategic account plans to grow Stripe’s revenue, product adoption, and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, create, and progress expansion opportunities across customer business units, subsidiaries, geographies, and product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute outbound strategies within existing accounts to develop new executive relationships and create qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full expansion sales cycle, from opportunity identification and discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customers’ complex business and technical challenges, and position Stripe’s core platform and products as solutions to those needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product workshops, business case development, and financial analyses that help customers quantify the value of investing further in Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with internal teams including Product, Engineering, Partnerships, and Post-Sales to coordinate migrations, activations, and strategic customer initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales experience, with at least 2 years working with enterprise customers, preferably in a technology company, with a demonstrated record of exceeding commercial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and expanding existing upper-middle-market or enterprise customer relationships, including identifying new opportunities within a portfolio rather than relying solely on renewals or inbound demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute strategic account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units, stakeholders, or subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value and engage confidently with senior business and technical stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Finance, and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage internet or software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech or payments is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position details&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer: Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employment type: Full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: 383 Kent Street, Sydney, NSW 2000, Australia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applications open: 30th October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
