&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Risk/Fraud Operations Team Lead, you will operate in a player-coach capacity, directly leading a team of Operations Associates while maintaining hands-on involvement in complex casework. You will be accountable for driving operational excellence, developing talent, and delivering strategic initiatives that shape the future of our Risk Operations function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of Operations Associates through regular 1:1s, performance conversations, and structured goal-setting aligned with organizational priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and report on team performance against KPIs, managing capacity, scheduling, and workload distribution across queues and channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicate approximately 40% of your time to core casework, including handling complex, high-risk escalations and conducting quality reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert in Risk and Fraud Operations, guiding thorough investigations to protect Stripe&#39;s business, brand, and mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root cause analyses on complex operational challenges, leveraging data to identify trends, surface gaps, and drive actionable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sustainable solutions to systemic issues and present data-backed recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong cross-functional relationships across the Risk vertical, representing your team&#39;s priorities in strategic forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recruitment, hiring, and onboarding initiatives while fostering an inclusive, high-performing team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for meaningful product and process improvements that deliver lasting operational impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion company-building initiatives, mentor future leaders, and consistently model Stripe&#39;s core principles in all decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in Fraud Operations, Fraud Strategy, or Financial Crime Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coaching and leading operations teams with a track record of managing and improving performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring others and delivering constructive, growth-oriented feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to use data to drive operational decisions and deliver weekly and monthly business metrics and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated subject matter expertise in Risk Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work cross-functionally to deliver results and build strong partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary planning, prioritization, and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and Spanish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of risk reviews, policy/compliance operations, and fraud detection tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing risk events and identifying at-risk scenarios within operational systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or contributing to cross-departmental or transformational initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with operational tools such as Jira and incident management workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leading player in the internet economy, Stripe has a responsibility to protect itself, our users, end customers, and the broader financial ecosystem from harm. Fraud Operations proactively reduces fraud, making it difficult and unprofitable for fraudsters to carry out attacks through Stripe. We build scalable, high-judgement investigation and review operations while minimizing user friction. We work across products, customer segments, and markets and serve as a core pillar of Stripe’s risk strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is hiring a Team Lead to develop a team of Operations Associates (OAs) within Fraud Operations in Bangalore. You will be responsible for the day-to-day operational execution and performance of your workflow(s), including queue health, SLA attainment, and decision quality. This role requires staying close to the work, remaining hands-on in complex casework (QA and targeted production), modeling high-quality decisioning, providing real-time coaching, and serving as the first-line escalation owner. You will also drive unit-level operational excellence. To be a fit, you will have a coaching mindset, proven ability to communicate at different levels, a track record of driving operational performance, and a passion for inspiring a team to deliver outstanding results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of Operations Associates; set clear expectations, coach performance, and build a high-judgement culture rooted in strong decisioning and customer empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own individual performance metrics of Operations Associates and ensure the team consistently meets throughput, SLA, and quality targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform specific unit-level execution, including: defining, clarifying, and evolving core processes, leading team meetings, and performing root cause analyses for defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support team operations including hiring, onboarding, scheduling, and intra-day coverage planning to meet SLAs; provide interview feedback and help maintain a high hiring bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain hands-on casework at a level that enables effective coaching and escalation coverage, without compromising core people-lead responsibilities and team performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve SOPs and decision frameworks for your workflow(s); drive process adherence and consistency through clear guidance, change management, and reinforcement mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent your workflow(s) in cross-team forums, surface operational pain points, propose improvements, support rollouts, and drive adoption within your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary escalation point for complex or time-sensitive cases within your unit, in partnership with global fraud stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process adherence and consistency across your team through robust quality programs and calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in leader development and represent Bangalore workflows in global enablement sessions/onsites as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on people leader and operational owner who thrives in a fast-paced fraud investigation environment. You run a strong performance cadence through clear metrics, coaching, and rigorous decision quality. You can take ambiguous operational problems, use data to diagnose root causes, and drive changes that stick, through influence, alignment, and follow-through, not just instruction. You bring sound judgment, calm execution under pressure, and a bias toward data-backed solutions and measurable improvements in both fraud outcomes and user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading fraud, risk, trust &amp;amp; safety, or investigations operations in a high-scale environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a team of frontline operations associates and own their individual performance/productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, risk, compliance, or financial industry operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define and operationalize team-level metrics (e.g., accuracy/quality, SLAs, throughput) and use data to drive team priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational background in new process launches, service delivery, and building operating models at the unit/team level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including presenting operational updates and representing the team in escalations in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill and credibility doing the core work of a user facing team with a high bar for quality, and a willingness to lead by example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3+ years of direct people management experience; this includes handling performance management and proactively coach/mentor individuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fraud domain depth across investigation workflows, risk vectors, and decision frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in optimizing unit-level fraud review operations through process redesign and tooling improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments risk (CNP/card testing, ATO, merchant fraud, transaction fraud) and familiarity with how upstream detection and downstream enforcement interact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytics proficiency (comfort with data to track team performance) and comfort partnering with data science/engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud Strategy is responsible for building scaled fraud mitigation systems that prevent fraud and protect the financial ecosystem, while minimizing disruption to good users. The fraud team’s mission is to protect Stripe, our users, and the broader financial ecosystem from actors who abuse Stripe accounts for financial gain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Fraud Strategist, you will be responsible for building strategies to mitigate fraud (buyer fraud, seller fraud and account fraud) on new and existing Stripe products. You will enable safer money movement for our users and help Stripe manage fraud risks intelligently. The stakes are high, and you will be up against ever-evolving challenges. You will face some of the most complex and dynamic problems at the company, and the nature of your work will evolve rapidly to combat new and more sophisticated challenges to Stripe&#39;s integrity in the financial ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations and other Risk Strategy functions to ensure fraud controls are embedded in every Stripe product. Beyond protecting against fraud risk, you&#39;ll drive innovation in how Stripe approaches fraud management— staying ahead of emerging fraud trends and pushing the boundaries of what effective, scalable fraud risk management looks like at a global payments company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor portfolio to identify, mitigate and predict risky behavior that could result in losses for Stripe, our users, and the financial ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal partners like Product, Engineering, Data Science, Risk Partnerships, and Operations, to tailor fraud risk management techniques to various products and payment methods across the globe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually evaluate products for gaps and propose risk controls to enhance the product while enabling growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale risk processes to cover a large and complex landscape of fraud risks. Effectively design, outsource and automate manual/repetitive workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe users to educate them and guide them on how to prevent potential fraud risks to their business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively and clearly communicate with other Stripes, Stripe&#39;s users, and Stripe&#39;s financial and regulatory partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; 6+ years of relevant experience, preferably in Financial Services, Payments or FinTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Curiosity and passion for risk management - you dig into anomalies and solve root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Decisiveness and openness to learning, with comfort making high-impact calls daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Data-driven judgment - skilled at using quantitative analysis to drive and defend decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Empathy for early-stage businesses and the ability to balance enforcement with user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Strong analytical skills, including the ability to frame complex tradeoffs through data and visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Advanced SQL skills with hands-on experience in business environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Proven ability to collaborate and execute cross-functionally with Engineering, Product, Data Science, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to convey complex ideas clearly across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Holistic thinking and the ability to build scaled processes that bridge systemic gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Track record of deriving actionable insights from complex problem spaces and influencing product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Ownership mentality and the ability to lead without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Proficient with AI tools to accelerate productivity and process automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with quantitative tools such as Python, R, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, risk, or trust &amp;amp; safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with machine learning teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced and rapidly changing start-up environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and pursue new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have significant work ahead, which gives you the opportunity to do important work that expands access to the global economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the APAC Risk team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The APAC Risk team helps Stripe launch and grow products responsibly across a diverse and rapidly evolving region. We work closely with global and regional partners across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations, Partnerships, and Risk to identify emerging risks, define practical controls, and make risk decisions easier to execute at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team supports Stripe’s growth in APAC by combining deep regional context with strong analytical judgment. We assess how fraud patterns, payment methods, user behavior, market structures, and regulatory expectations vary across countries. We use those insights to build strategies that protect Stripe and the broader payments ecosystem while preserving a strong experience for legitimate users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Fraud Strategist on the APAC Risk team, you will be responsible for identifying and reducing transaction and merchant fraud across Stripe’s products and markets in the region. You will monitor the health of Stripe’s APAC portfolio, investigate emerging threats, and build scalable strategies that reduce losses without creating unnecessary friction for legitimate businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on complex and fast moving problems where the available information is often incomplete and fraud patterns evolve quickly. Your work may range from investigating an anomalous fraud trend to designing a regional control, defining a model feature, improving a manual review workflow, or shaping the risk approach for a new product, payment method, or country launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor transaction and merchant fraud trends across APAC and investigate anomalous behavior at the merchant, account, and transaction level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, build, and maintain regional fraud health metrics. Set targets, identify material changes, and communicate the drivers of performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop short and long term fraud strategies for APAC markets, products, and payment methods. Translate investigations into clear controls, product requirements, model improvements, and operational actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations, Partnerships, and other Risk teams to scope, prioritize, and deliver fraud mitigation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess fraud risks for new country, product, and local payment method launches. Define mitigations before launch and monitor outcomes after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance fraud loss, user experience, operational cost, conversion, and growth when recommending or implementing controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and automate fraud risk workflows through data, internal tools, and agent based solutions where these can increase consistency, speed, or coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with users and external partners when needed to explain fraud risks, improve controls, and support a healthy payments ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear regional reporting for senior stakeholders, risk governance forums, and other internal audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is naturally curious, analytically strong, and comfortable making decisions in ambiguous situations. You investigate unusual patterns until you understand the underlying mechanism. You can turn data and domain context into a clear risk decision, then work across teams to make that decision operational.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand that effective fraud strategy is not simply about reducing losses. It requires thoughtful tradeoffs between protection, growth, user experience, and operational complexity. You communicate those tradeoffs clearly and remain open to new evidence and feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 - 8 years of relevant experience in fraud strategy, payments risk, financial services, fintech, trust and safety, data, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience investigating fraud or other risk patterns using account and transaction data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment and the ability to frame business decisions and tradeoffs through quantitative analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate SQL skills and experience applying SQL in a business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining metrics, assessing performance, and translating analysis into practical recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with technical and operational teams such as Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations, or Partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex risk issues to technical and nontechnical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management skills and the ability to drive execution across teams with different priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound decision making in ambiguous or time sensitive situations, with a willingness to learn and iterate as new evidence emerges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy for legitimate users and an ability to balance scaled risk controls with user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with transaction fraud, merchant fraud, account takeover, or abuse in an online payments environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across APAC markets or with regional payment methods and local market structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL skills or experience with quantitative tools such as Python, R, or Stata.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with machine learning or Data Science teams on model features, rules, detection, or measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assessing fraud risk for new products, payment methods, or country launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing risk controls, monitoring frameworks, operational workflows, or policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using automation, AI tools, or agent based workflows to improve risk processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast moving environment where threats, products, and priorities change quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Web Presence and Platform (WPP) designs, builds, and operates Stripe’s public web presence, including stripe.com and other sites that may be the first impression of Stripe for many. We create industry-leading experiences that help customers understand the power of Stripe’s platform, share Stripe’s ideas and expertise, and drive adoption. We also build the systems and operational foundations behind those experiences, making our websites fast, stable, and easy to evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work brings together design craft, engineering, operations, and business strategy. We want to make every pixel count, create experiences that are both useful and compelling, and help other Stripes benefit from the systems and capabilities we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP’s Design Systems pod builds and stewards Helm, the shared design system behind stripe.com. We create the components, patterns, tools, and guidance that help WPP teams deliver expressive, consistent, and high-quality web experiences at scale. We work across design and engineering to keep design intent, production code, and real-world usage aligned as the system evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an engineer on the Design Systems pod, you will turn Stripe’s visual direction into reusable, production-ready capabilities. You’ll shape components from early design through implementation, testing, documentation, adoption, and ongoing iteration. You’ll combine strong design judgment with frontend expertise to ensure Helm works across responsive layouts, interaction states, accessibility needs, performance constraints, content models, and locales. You’ll also partner with teams building on Helm, helping them use the system effectively, identify reusable patterns, and contribute improvements back to it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build polished, accessible, and performant React components and patterns that express Stripe’s visual language across stripe.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with designers and engineers to shape component behavior, APIs, responsive states, interaction details, and design-token architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for design–code parity and component quality through documentation, accessibility and visual-regression testing, production validation, and in-context review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help workstream teams decide when to compose existing capabilities, extend the system, or keep an implementation local, and lead the upstreaming of broadly reusable work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how designers, engineers, content authors, and agents discover, understand, and adopt Helm through clear guidance, examples, tooling, and responsive collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant frontend or design engineering experience building production web experiences or the shared systems and tooling behind them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining a production design system or shared component library, including evolving it through real-world use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with React, TypeScript, HTML, and CSS, with experience taking interactive, responsive work from design through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted development tools as a regular part of software engineering work, with sound judgment about validating their output and maintaining code, product, and security quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing flexible component APIs, primitives, tokens, and composition models that give skilled practitioners meaningful control while preserving accessibility and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual and interaction-design judgment, along with the communication skills to collaborate with experienced designers and engineers on ambiguous system-level tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building expressive, brand-forward web experiences where consistency must coexist with differentiated art direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CMS-driven experiences, structured content, localization, or other constraints involved in supporting a large global website&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tools and practices that connect design and code, such as Figma libraries, design tokens, Code Connect, component documentation, or visual-regression testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating consumers between design systems or evolving shared components while maintaining compatibility across existing production surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UI Platform team, known as Sail, builds the foundations that support Stripe’s Dashboard and many of Stripe’s other user interfaces. The Sail UI team owns Stripe’s design system, helping Stripe engineers create consistent, accessible, performant, and high-quality experiences at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build and maintain reusable components, design tokens, theming capabilities, documentation, and developer tooling used by engineers and designers across Stripe. We are currently focused on two major projects. First, we are building Sail for Agents: the generation infrastructure, documentation systems, agent integrations, and automated quality checks that help AI coding agents build high-quality Stripe interfaces safely and consistently at scale. Second, we are evolving the visual language of the Dashboard, one of Stripe’s largest UI surfaces, while modernizing its underlying codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Frontend Engineer on the Sail UI team, you’ll help build and evolve Stripe’s design system and the tools that enable engineers and AI coding agents to create high-quality user interfaces. You’ll independently drive frontend projects from problem definition through rollout, working closely with designers, product engineers, and other Sail engineers. Your work will range from reusable components, themes, and documentation to agentic tooling, automated quality checks, and modernizing the foundations of Stripe’s Dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of software projects, independently scoping problems and carrying solutions through design, implementation, testing, and rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain accessible, performant, and well-tested components, themes, and frontend APIs used across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling, documentation, and automated quality checks that help engineers and AI coding agents use Sail effectively and meet Stripe’s UI quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product designers and engineers to understand their needs and turn recurring UI patterns into reusable design-system capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve the visual language of Stripe’s Dashboard while modernizing its underlying codebase and migrating legacy UI patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the accessibility, internationalization, observability, performance, reliability, and developer experience of the design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute thoughtful code reviews, technical discussions, and documentation that improve the quality of the team’s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in using AI-assisted and agentic development tools as part of day-to-day software engineering, including critically reviewing, validating, and improving generated code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional frontend engineering experience, or equivalent practical experience, building, shipping, and debugging web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of modern frontend technologies and frameworks, including browser fundamentals, responsive design, and accessibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently scope and deliver open-ended frontend projects, making practical technical and product tradeoffs with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills, with attention to testing, maintainability, and the quality of the resulting user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with designers, product engineers, and other partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a design system, frontend platform, or shared component library&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer tooling such as build tools, package managers, codemods, lint rules, or large monorepos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building tools, integrations, or automated evaluation and quality systems for AI coding agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using documentation, developer feedback, or adoption data to improve a developer-facing product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team to drive financial insight and strategy at Stripe. The Finance &amp;amp; Strategy team brings understanding and predictability to Stripe’s financials, and we work together with our key business partners to accelerate long term growth for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with F&amp;amp;S and Business Leaders to drive the long-term success of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, mentor, and oversee a team of small analysts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally to identify important strategy questions and answer them with data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial forecasts and targets, track performance, and understand deviations from actuals to drive strategy and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain deep knowledge and understanding of Stripe&#39;s business performance across geographies and user segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define metrics and leading indicators of business performance and partner with the Analytics team to develop tools and dashboards to make these metrics widely accessible across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, or business-finance experience with 2+ years managing a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning planning and forecasting processes across headcount, operating expenses, and/or revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial-analysis fundamentals, including budgeting and forecasting, month-end close support, and budget-versus-actual variance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage and develop a small team of analysts, including setting priorities, reviewing work, coaching, and creating clear accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to retain a defined individual-contributor portfolio alongside people-management responsibilities. ~50% IC work, 50% Manager responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and/or Python skills, with demonstrated ability to automate recurring analyses and improve finance workflows through AI-enabled tools and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous problems, independently develop a point of view, and drive cross-functional projects to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder-management and communication skills, with a track record of acting as a trusted, objective finance partner to business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively across regions, time zones, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience in a strategic finance function at a high-growth tech company, preferably in the payments/fintech space&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of SQL or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of data visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge is building a new payments platform powered by stablecoins to make global money movement simpler, faster, and more accessible. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders, give customers access to dollars through virtual accounts, and disburse USD globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe stablecoin rails will become a foundational part of financial infrastructure, moving and settling trillions of dollars worldwide. Bridge is helping bring that future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team has built financial infrastructure at companies including Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, and Airbnb. We are united by the conviction that stablecoins can materially improve how money moves around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and ship end-to-end product experiences across frontend applications, backend services, APIs, and data systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design reliable, performant, and intuitive interfaces for developers, operations teams, and end users interacting with Bridge products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain the APIs and backend systems that power global payments, virtual accounts, and payouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects from technical design through launch and iteration, often operating with substantial autonomy and without dedicated product management support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and resolve production issues across the stack, with a focus on reliability, performance, and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful tradeoffs among business priorities, user experience, speed of execution, and long-term technical quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional software-engineering experience. We are open to candidates across a range of seniority, from experienced individual contributors through senior technical leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and shipping production software across both frontend and backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with backend services, SQL databases, and API design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building polished, maintainable web applications and collaborating closely on product and user-experience decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership, with the ability to lead technical projects and influence product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write modular, well-tested, maintainable code while remaining pragmatic and moving quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment and diving into unfamiliar problem spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to produce clear technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity, sound judgment, and a commitment to continuously improving the product for partners and end users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer-facing API products or platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial infrastructure, payments, money movement, or other regulated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in or experience with stablecoins, blockchain systems, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing systems that require high reliability, strong security controls, and careful operational discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Builder Experience Team makes it easier for Stripe’s product teams to build the right products, ship them with confidence, and help users realize value from them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order to build a great product, product teams must develop a deep understanding of users, shape and test ideas, coordinate across functions, navigate launch requirements, identify risks, gather feedback, and manage products after launch. Today, many of these workflows are fragmented, manual, or built around processes and tools that predate recent advances in AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a small, AI-native team reimagining how Stripe builds, ships, and ramps products. We experiment with new approaches across AI agents, automation, and process—and scale the ones that work. Our initial areas of focus include reinventing launch readiness from gates into guidelines, giving product teams richer and more timely context, and shortening the feedback loops between builders, users, Sales, and Support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are Stripe’s product managers, engineers, designers, researchers – and we help to simplify the interactions with the cross-functional teams that help bring products to market. We work closely with teams including all of our business unit PMs, Product Operations, and Kai, Stripe’s internal AI platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for product-minded engineers who want to rethink how products get built—not simply digitize existing processes. You’ll identify high-friction parts of Stripe’s product-development lifecycle, rapidly prototype new approaches, put them in the hands of real teams, and turn the strongest experiments into scaled solutions used by every product team at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role with broad product and technical scope. You’ll work across the stack, combining traditional software engineering with emerging AI capabilities. You’ll operate in ambiguous problem spaces where the right product, interface, and technical architecture must be discovered together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build tools that help Stripe teams shape better products, ship with greater speed and confidence, and learn from users more quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop AI-native workflows and agents that synthesize context, automate repetitive work, surface risks, and help builders make better decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end to end: identify high-value problems, develop prototypes, test them with users, measure their impact, and scale the approaches that work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across backend systems, data sources, internal platforms, and polished user-facing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with product managers, engineers, designers, researchers, and cross-functional teams to understand how work happens in practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with platforms such as Kai and Compass while identifying where new foundational capabilities are needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong judgment to the use of sensitive internal context, including appropriate attention to security, privacy, permissions, and user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define how the team operates, including its technical foundations, product-development practices, and standards for experimentation and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the team’s roadmap by identifying systemic sources of friction and opportunities to improve Stripe’s product-development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of backend and/or full-stack software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical experience leading the design and delivery of new product experiences from prototype to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in high-ambiguity environments: framing problems, experimenting &amp;amp; adjusting, making right-sized technical decisions, and creating an actionable path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional and cross-organizational collaboration skills, with the ability to align teams with different systems, priorities, and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering judgment around system reliability, operational excellence, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded approach to engineering, with a focus on delivering meaningful outcomes for users and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Java, Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering user facing products at Stripe (Payments, MM, RevSuite, etc), or experience delivering user facing products pre-dating Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on 0→1 products or taking new capabilities from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Developer &amp;amp; End-user Experience Platform (DEEP) organization empowers all of Stripe&#39;s products with a shared product platform that helps with rapidly delivering high-quality, cross-product experiences across our UI and API surfaces. It focuses on providing a consistent and scalable developer experience that any developer (both internal and external) can leverage to accelerate a merchant&#39;s ability to create value using Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team matching — exact team matching for one of the subteams will begin during final stages. Please note we may also consider you for different orgs based on your experience, location, etc. More information on our team matching process can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zvJkO2c7GzukHG-_oqc5wbOLajpuh5FjbmZPcZPU1o0/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for full-stack engineers who are interested in building software services and platforms that impact thousands of employees and millions of Stripe users, regardless of whether they&#39;re an end user, developer, or partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure our platforms are reliable, scalable, secure, and extensible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape future-proof interfaces that are easy to build with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make effective tradeoffs that consider business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable technical foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive sound technical decision-making and lead technical conversations with other teams across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug production issues across services and various levels of the tech stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–12+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language (you can learn new languages on the job, and our interview process is language agnostic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy and responsibility, with an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Enterprise and Ecosystem team is focused on enhancing migration, activation, and cross-product experiences for enterprises. This position will be integral to a growing team, collaborating closely with product and customer-facing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team Matching: exact team matching for one of the subteams will begin during final stages. Please note we may also consider you for different orgs based on your experience, location, etc. More information on our team matching process can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zvJkO2c7GzukHG-_oqc5wbOLajpuh5FjbmZPcZPU1o0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.ahb3b6nrktv1&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Full-Stack Engineer on the Enterprise and Ecosystem team, you will be a key contributor in building and scaling the next generation of Stripe&#39;s connectivity with global commerce systems. This role is crucial to building and managing integrations with leading Ecommerce, CRM, and ERP systems to help our users activate faster and realize greater value from Stripe. You will focus on developing the infrastructure that powers unified connectors for various partners, ensuring seamless and rapid integration of Stripe&#39;s products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining a set of connectors and integrations for partners like Shopify, and Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out Stripe services and infrastructure to facilitate transactional flows and data migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launching specific, high-impact projects in the first six months, such as a new payments-agnostic billing connector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as a self-starter and driving technical ownership for projects, given the nature of the role requires a highly self-sufficient contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with other engineering teams, particularly those focused on underlying infrastructure, to ensure cohesion and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships nor includes co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack capabilities; comfortable writing code on core Stripe systems while also understanding external partner systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in a modern web stack and have shipped production level code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding and ability to read the code/interfaces of partner systems (e.g., Salesforce, Oracle, Netsuite) to facilitate complex integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable, intuitive, and capable of quickly solving complex, multi-system problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivating and thrive in an environment where you are expected to take full ownership of your projects and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building connectors, or deep integrations with major Ecommerce, CRM, or ERP platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments or subscriptions systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background that demonstrates an ability to rapidly learn new systems and navigate unfamiliar technical domains effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about building cutting-edge solutions that empower businesses worldwide, we would love to hear from you! Please submit your application detailing your experience and why you believe you would be a great fit for the team.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Enterprise Product team, the Enterprise Engineering team is responsible for bridging the gap between Stripe&#39;s core capabilities and the bespoke needs of the world&#39;s largest organizations. Our mission is to improve Stripe&#39;s product-market fit with enterprise users to win more deals and grow revenue, while giving every enterprise user an excellent experience as they onboard, activate, and grow their business with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
