&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Professional Services team works with our most strategic users. You will work on the highest visibility projects to provide technical expertise to our customers to help accelerate their knowledge, solution design and integrations with Stripe. This role is responsible for leading strategic conversations and developing plans that will transform the payments and financial infrastructure for leading enterprises.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales, Solution Architecture and Implementation teams to drive client engagement, customer wins, and revenue on behalf of the Professional Services team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute integration engineering end-to-end, from high-level architecture down to code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think on your feet and comfortable talking about technical concepts, and explaining how Stripe works, both from a product feature and API architecture perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate our users and the developer community about Stripe&#39;s value proposition, best practices and new technical developments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the primary, ongoing technical point of contact for our largest users&#39; and partners&#39; technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep abreast of new Stripe technologies and software products and showcases technical thought leadership in whitepapers, conferences and other industry events&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing recommendations, feedback and best practices to the product and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years + experience in a Software Engineering / Integration Engineering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with various code-level debugging (Stripe code and user code)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be comfortable talking about technical concepts, and explaining how Stripe works, both from a product features and API architecture perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user first approach &amp;amp; empathy with our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident and comfortable with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong generalist technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy the puzzle of solving open-ended problems, both individually and as a member of our team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn and teach others&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, communicative, consultative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually curious, with great problem solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metronome is a usage-based billing platform and a Stripe product. It helps modern software companies launch products faster, offer flexible pricing models, and streamline finance workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Metronome Integration Engineering team sits at the intersection of sales, growth, product, and research and development. We own the technical aspects of the customer lifecycle after a sale and before the customer transitions to our post-implementation teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Integration Engineer, you’ll help customers implement Metronome successfully and realize value quickly. You’ll lead technical work across requirements gathering, solution and integration design, configuration, testing, data migration, launch, and handoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct discovery and scoping to understand customers’ challenges across billing, product launches, pricing and packaging, quote-to-cash, customer experience, and related areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support customers throughout the implementation lifecycle, including requirements gathering, technical design, integration design, testing, data migration, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert guidance on usage-based pricing and consumption-based business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure Metronome’s platform on behalf of customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design integrations between Metronome’s APIs and customers’ business systems—including CRM and CPQ platforms, payment and tax systems, ERP and billing providers, and reporting and analytics tools—in alignment with Metronome best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison between customers and Metronome’s research and development teams, advocating for customer needs and feature requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with implementation managers and other project-team members to provide visibility into progress and proactively identify risks and issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across customer organizations, from day-to-day operators to C-suite executives. Meet customers in person when doing so will improve the engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise customers on integrating Metronome into their systems and help shape their pricing and packaging strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure an effective handoff to Customer Success and Technical Support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with some of Metronome’s most strategic customers. These engagements will be complex, deep, and highly technical. Metronome directly influences how modern software companies monetize their products, and this team is on the front lines of that work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metronome operates with a startup mindset within Stripe. There is a significant opportunity for people with initiative to influence our direction, build processes from zero to one, and make a meaningful impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are helpful but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in technical or customer-facing roles involving SaaS products, such as sales engineering, solutions architecture, technical account management, or deployment strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex implementations for enterprise technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-moving environments that value initiative and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn and communicate technical concepts to technical, go-to-market, and finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in building and improving go-to-market playbooks, processes, and reusable assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel approximately 30% of the time, depending on customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of quote-to-cash processes, including experience integrating with or working alongside platforms such as Salesforce, NetSuite, CPQ systems, and the Stripe ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a software engineer, product manager, or in another technical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of project- and program-management fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with stakeholders in finance, engineering, product, sales operations, or billing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with logs, metrics, billing, finance, infrastructure, or financial tooling and concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

