&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience using React Native&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience in ensuring great user experience and ease of use of features for products you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with financial product companies and interest in financial products and markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team is Stripe’s global backbone, dedicated to delivering and continuously improving essential business services—billing and collections, procurement, monetization, payroll, and travel and expenses. We drive company value through data-driven insights, operational rigor, and a relentless focus on excellence. As strategic partners, we shape business decisions, champion technology-enabled solutions, own operational strategy, and collaborate across global functions to enable Stripe’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Monetization and Contract Success (MACS) team sits within Monetization Services and helps Stripe execute complex commercial agreements efficiently and accurately. The team partners across the deal and contract lifecycle to reduce friction, improve deal velocity, support scalable commercial constructs, and deliver a seamless user experience after contract execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Monetization and Contract Success (MACS) Specialist to join our growing team. In this high-impact role, you will guide complex commercial agreements through pre-signature review from a supportability lens - helping ensure that contractual terms are clear, operationally feasible, and can be accurately implemented in Stripe’s systems. You will work closely with cross-functional partners to resolve issues, strengthen controls, improve workflows, and develop scalable solutions that increase deal-cycle efficiency and reduce downstream user friction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject-matter expert across the commercial contract lifecycle, answering questions and advising deal owners on the supportability elements of sales contract reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and interpret commercial and legal terms, identify operational requirements and potential risks, and prepare agreements or deal inputs for review under established guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Deal Pricing, Deal Strategy, Commercial Legal, Business Practices, Accounting, Billing, Tax, Sales Operations, Engineering, and account teams to align commercial objectives with operational capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and, where appropriate, advise on commercial terms, balancing user needs, Stripe’s objectives, operational feasibility, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the feedback loop with Pricing Activation for accurate and timely onboarding of custom contracts and pricing terms into Stripe’s billing and financial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contract and deal workflows in relevant systems, maintain clear documentation, and provide proactive communication on status, dependencies, and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the end-to-end contract lifecycle, including inquiries, escalations, implementation troubleshooting, billing-related issues, and post-execution corrections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable, auditable processes and controls that balance and improve contract quality, activation accuracy, deal velocity, and the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze operational data and recurring issues to identify root causes, measure performance, and recommend process or system improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and internal systems teams to translate operational needs into durable tooling, automation, and workflow enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits, key programs, and other cross-functional initiatives as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to building a high-performing team culture grounded in sound judgment, continuous improvement, accountability, and excellent stakeholder service.&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in commercial contracting, deal management, legal operations, monetization operations, pricing activation, billing operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to interpret commercial and legal language and translate complex contract terms into clear operational and system requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing commercial agreements and partnering effectively with Legal or other risk and control functions; experience supporting commercial negotiations is strongly valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to synthesize information from multiple sources, investigate complex issues, and make sound, well-reasoned decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a high volume of work with meticulous attention to detail, strong organization, and consistent follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain complex requirements clearly, earn trust quickly, and represent Stripe effectively with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering across functions and balancing commercial objectives, operational constraints, user experience, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solution-oriented mindset and a track record of establishing best practices, improving processes, and delivering results in ambiguous or rapidly changing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and escalate thoughtfully when established frameworks do not fully address a situation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, SaaS, or another technology-driven industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with custom pricing, contract activation, billing implementation, or post-signature contract operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or improving contract lifecycle management, deal management, or pricing activation workflows and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with audit requirements, operational controls, and performance metrics in a financial or regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder’s mindset, a willingness to question assumptions and conventional wisdom, and a passion for solving problems through infrastructure and automation.&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team provides and enhances core business services that are the backbone of Stripe. FinOps uses data and operational excellence to deliver technology solutions, payroll services, operational excellence, and monetization services to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Monetization Operations Analyst to join our growing team. You&#39;ll help us improve user experience through accurate and timely onboarding of contracts and workflows, and deliver improvements in our integrated financial systems with business partners, financial colleagues, and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard sold custom contracts into our billing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with legal contracts with strong attention to detail and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage scalable billing and collection processes for complex user agreements and new business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable and auditable onboarding processes for new and existing users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal systems, global deal management, legal, sales ops, internal audit, go-to-market, engineering, and accounting teams to develop and improve processes for contract reviews and to anticipate changing business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account managers to resolve user inquiries related to onboarding implementation, billing, and collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for the customer to internal stakeholders. Share system feedback and insights with Sales, Product Management, Engineering, Support, and Legal on innovation and improvements needed to optimize the Stripe user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scope, build, and deliver continuous process improvements that enhance operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a client-facing role, ideally in customer success, consulting, financial services, account management, or sales, preferably working with technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading technical conversations and persuading others to take action based on requirements and value provided by solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be detail-oriented while visualizing the larger impact of a series of transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to navigate data and people to find answers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operating rigor, including organizational and time management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well with a wide range of people, both internally and externally, including working with a team of sales and services peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation and flexibility to work well in a high-growth environment where things change quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to trace process impacts from situation to end customers and business financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of or experience in the payments industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated professional experience using GSuite, Excel, and working with large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management or consulting experience and the ability to work cross-functionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s mindset and a willingness to question assumptions and conventional wisdom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and solving problems through infrastructure and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-8886b3bc-7fff-4ce3-aab2-99b5392589d8&quot;&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AMER Product Demand Generation is a team of marketers that drive strategies to engage prospects and customers, generating demand for Stripe&#39;s priority products in the Americas. We partner closely with Campaigns, Product Marketing, Sales Development, and Sales to bring full-funnel campaigns to life and optimize performance and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced marketer to lead Money Management marketing across the US, Canada, and Latin America. Money Management brings together products that help businesses hold funds, move money globally, create and manage cards, and access financing. You’ll set the regional strategy and turn it into programs that build demand, grow pipeline, and help increase market share in partnership with teams across Stripe’s go-to-market organization. You’ll also help Stripe strengthen its approach to marketing Money Management and evolve demand generation for this high-priority area for Stripe. Money Management is still in an early stage of its marketing journey, with a strong opportunity to shape the strategy, build the programs that bring it to market, and establish how we create demand across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will have a meaningful impact across Stripe’s go-to-market organization. Money Management is a rapidly growing, high-priority product and an important part of Stripe’s strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll build and improve the engine that reaches key decision-makers and create a consistent experience across customer journeys, channels, and campaigns. You’ll set regional priorities, allocate budget across channels, and connect global campaign strategy with regional execution for Money Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional multi-channel strategy for Money Management marketing campaigns that drive demand. Channels can include paid media, content syndication, digital events, account based marketing (ABM), etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build region-specific marketing activations with channel leads to unlock local opportunities for Money Management audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a cross-GTM coalition including Global Campaigns, Events, Product Sales, Sales Development, and Sales Operations to jointly grow the Money Management pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics for Money Management across the sales funnel — investigating conversion, channel mix effectiveness, and pipeline health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to define regional requirements as Stripe refines marketing capabilities, MarTech stack, and lead management for scaled motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify innovative new ways to reach and engage the Money Management audience — there is broad leeway in this role to pursue creative marketing ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a thought leader representing the Americas as Stripe grows its Money Management go-to-market across campaigns and broader strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience running scaled digital demand generation programs (e.g., demand generation, growth marketing, or regional marketing)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GTM direct ownership of an audience or product segment at a B2B company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building multi-channel demand generation strategies and owning integrated digital activations across paid media, content marketing, email marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience assessing business health and managing marketing performance metrics. You can turn go-to-market data on lead generation, funnel conversion, pipeline progress, and channel performance into clear insights and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple complex programs simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building and delivering programs with partners across Sales, Sales Development, Product Marketing, Content, and Event Marketing. Be prepared to discuss programs you owned directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity: The ability to build, adapt, and maintain positive momentum is key for this role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI including leveraging native AI tooling and integrating LLM / agentic capabilities into everyday work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling net new programs with an eye toward repeatability and efficiency. You’ve built 0 to 1 and have scaled from 1 to 10&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event or field marketing experience or exposure (prior event ownership not required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or or adjacent industries or marketing FinTech solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adjacent business experience (e.g., strategy consulting, paid media, etc) that brings well-rounded GTM perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Brand Studio is a multi-disciplinary team that accelerates the awareness and trajectory of our brand. We craft the creative vision and strategy for different types of projects and audiences, and amplify them across various mediums, channels, objects to environments, and digital and physical experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe brand identity team is responsible for defining and evolving Stripe’s visual identity, and bringing the Stripe brand to life in new and impactful ways across surfaces. Our goal is to enable the creation of a coherent, high quality brand experience across the user journey, building recognition and trust in Stripe at every turn. We collaborate with other design systems teams to translate our brand for Stripe.com and Dashboard, and partner with teams across the company on high impact user-facing projects to create work that feels authentic to Stripe at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3d illustrator/animators at Stripe demonstrate passion for great design and for expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible illustration systems that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency for the brand at scale. The ideal candidate excels at delivering on brand 3d illustration from conception, to 3d modeling, and all the way to motion. They have a deep understanding of visual storytelling, iterate quickly, and collaborate seamlessly with marketers, product managers, leaders, other designers, and agency partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the Stripe brand ecosystem to develop, establish and create illustration and motion styles in close partnership with brand, product design, and marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create photo-realistic 3d compositions that tell editorial stories in static and motion and a variety of advertising surfaces from billboards to video.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion and influence how the Stripe brands expresses itself through image and motion and develop guidelines, systems, and processes to ensure quality and consistency at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with non-motion designers, elevating and informing each others’ work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee quality and consistency of 3d illustration/motion and how it is used to express our brand—from product, to advertising campaigns and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the work of external teams in creative strategy, execution, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with designers, researchers, product managers, marketers, and other cross-functional partners to serve a global audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, create and sustain a culture of excellence by expanding and evolving our best practices, design process, and ideation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay curious and experimental as an avid maker, obsessed with tinkering and tool building with AI to create beautiful things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape a strategic vision that pushes brand boundaries and builds internal awareness of design’s impact at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant design and art direction experience for technical and product-driven companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in art, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong strategic acumen for building leading brands in a fast-paced, global facing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a systems-thinker and excel at extrapolating and extending shared patterns and behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven excellence in effective art direction, and building and extending 3d illustration systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have proven track record of using and building AI tools to create exceptional work in new ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to express and communicate a brand through distinct graphics, patterns, motion, interaction, and video.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can effectively communicate concepts, direction and decisions with the team and with external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record independently delivering work as well as collaborating with and influencing the work of other designers, contractors, and agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find a meaningful balance between optimizing for speed, quality, and doing risky, interesting, pixel-perfect work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions and crave feedback to help you design at your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and have them help you learn and grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Proactive Threat team is responsible for identifying vulnerabilities and security weaknesses across Stripe&#39;s systems, applications, networks, and cloud infrastructure — before adversaries do. We operate as a hybrid offensive function: conducting penetration testing, emulating real-world threat actors through red team operations, and partnering closely with our defensive security teams to validate detection capabilities and improve Stripe&#39;s overall security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are builders first. Our team develops custom tooling, automation frameworks, and internal platforms that scale our offensive capabilities and enable repeatable, high-fidelity assessments. We believe the best offensive security engineers are equal parts hacker and engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is distributed across the United States, primarily operating in Eastern and Pacific time zones, and collaborates regularly with security, engineering, and product stakeholders across Stripe — including teams in Europe and Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Offensive Security Engineer on the Proactive Threat team, you will simulate the tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) of real-world adversaries to uncover security risks across Stripe&#39;s products and infrastructure. You&#39;ll conduct hands-on penetration testing, lead red team engagements, and collaborate with blue team counterparts to validate and improve detection and response capabilities. Your work will directly influence how Stripe builds, ships, and secures financial infrastructure used by millions of businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond assessments, you&#39;ll design and build offensive tooling and automation that amplifies the team&#39;s impact. You&#39;ll leverage threat intelligence to prioritize testing efforts, contribute to incident investigations when needed, and act as a subject-matter expert for security initiatives across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct comprehensive penetration tests across web applications, APIs, cloud environments (AWS/GCP/Azure), mobile applications, and internal infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute red team engagements that emulate the TTPs of cyber and criminal threat actors targeting financial services, including initial access, lateral movement, persistence, and data exfiltration scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform assumed-breach and objective-based assessments to test detection and response capabilities in coordination with defensive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with detection engineering, threat intelligence, and incident response teams to validate security controls, identify coverage gaps, and improve detection fidelity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute adversary tradecraft insights to inform detection rule development, threat hunting hypotheses, and incident response playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support incident investigations by providing offensive expertise, log analysis, and root cause analysis when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain custom offensive tools, scripts, and automation frameworks to enhance assessment efficiency and coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal platforms and workflows that enable scalable, repeatable offensive operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal security tooling repositories and champion engineering best practices within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate repetitive testing tasks, payload generation, and reporting workflows using modern development practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear, actionable reports that communicate technical findings, business risk, and remediation guidance to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject-matter expert and primary point of contact for stakeholder teams engaged in offensive security programs and Stripe-wide security initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead offensive security projects end-to-end, mentor junior team members, and foster a culture of continuous learning and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and attack techniques; share research internally and contribute to the broader security community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in offensive security, penetration testing, red teaming, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python, Go, or similar languages, with demonstrated experience building tools, automation, or custom exploits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of web application security, including OWASP Top 10, ASVS, and common vulnerability classes (injection, auth flaws, business logic, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP), including cloud-native attack techniques and misconfigurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with offensive tooling such as Burp Suite, Cobalt Strike, Mythic, Sliver, BloodHound, or similar frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with adversary tradecraft and frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, including TTPs for initial access, privilege escalation, lateral movement, and exfiltration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex technical findings into clear, risk-based recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think like an adversary — creative, persistent, and able to holistically assess risk in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting offensive security in fintech, financial services, or other highly regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in vulnerability research, exploit development, or CVE discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with threat intelligence, detection engineering, or incident response teams (purple team operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with big data and log analysis tools (Splunk, Databricks, PySpark, osquery, etc.) for threat hunting or investigative support&lt;/li&gt;
