&lt;li&gt;The ability to prioritize effectively and make sound decisions in a fast-moving, structured environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A process-oriented mindset and a track record of improving workflows, reducing manual effort, or improving user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first mindset and interest in learning technical products, systems, and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work from the Bengaluru office in night shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational data to manage performance, identify trends, and prioritize improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hiring, onboarding, workforce planning, or scheduling for an operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global teams across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Litigation team at Stripe works on complex technical and legal matters involving disputes, insolvency, litigation, arbitration, regulatory investigations, and other escalated issues. The team supports products and services that help businesses around the world grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Litigation Paralegal, you&#39;ll support the team on pre-litigation, litigation, investigations, and insolvency matters across a range of issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll support the Litigation team in managing disputes, insolvency, litigation, arbitration, and other escalated matters. You&#39;ll prioritize competing requests, build effective relationships with internal partners, and help the team respond to matters in a fast-paced environment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage bankruptcy and insolvency matters involving Stripe merchants in Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia-Pacific, including filing proofs of claim, responding to requests from insolvency practitioners, and escalating matters that require attorney support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide paralegal support for litigation and regulatory investigations, including fact investigations, issue analysis, discovery, and matter management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with all aspects of discovery, including implementing legal holds and collecting and producing documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle and respond to small claims matters globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support overall matter management for the Litigation team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize and maintain knowledge-management resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to special projects and adapt to changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paralegal certificate or bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant litigation paralegal experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated judgment and ability to drive matters to resolution in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize work, and meet deadlines independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with individuals across organizational levels and contribute to a supportive team environment&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior in-house experience as a litigation paralegal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payment Methods and Expansion Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with payment methods and financial partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy, and delivers new capabilities in new and existing markets to Stripe users.&amp;nbsp; This is not a traditional sales, channel, merchant-partnership, or account-management role. You will build product and infrastructure partnerships with banks, acquirers, payment providers, and other financial institutions that enable Stripe’s products and market launches. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a new member to join our team to develop and execute on high-impact initiatives with both payment method partners and expansion partners in new and existing markets, focussing on EMEA. These partnerships form the basis of Stripe’s product. As part of these efforts, you will be responsible for deal negotiation and execution for our EMEA payment methods and expansion business. This is an exciting opportunity to make a significant impact and contribute to the growth and success of Stripe&#39;s payment method partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will require close coordination with product and engineering teams, as well as cross-functional stakeholders including go to market teams, Marketing, Legal, Finance, Risk, etc., and with external partners’ senior executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities and craft partnership and product strategies for market expansion and payment method partners in existing markets in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute deals, manage partner onboarding and partnership development for new and existing financial partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand our partners’ strategic priorities, challenges, and internal roadmaps; regularly communicate insights and recommendations to Stripe product stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow Stripe’s relationships with partners, identifying&amp;nbsp; partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, and building alignment between Stripe and our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish key performance indicators (KPIs) and metrics to measure the effectiveness of both deal&amp;nbsp; processes and ongoing partner management and&amp;nbsp; distribution initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience related to payments and/or ecommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep EMEA market knowledge, and a thorough understanding of payment method dynamics and business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple stakeholders with varying priorities and drive creative solutions and commitment to a shared goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a product centric environments with significant internal and external dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders internally and externally across a wide variety of functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Alliances and Channels (A&amp;amp;C) team builds and scales the partner ecosystem that powers Stripe&#39;s growth. We work with SaaS platforms, technology partners, and services partners to drive merchant acquisition and expand Stripe&#39;s reach across markets. In LATAM, partners are a the primary growth engine — and this role sits at the center of that motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of partner development and channel sales. You&#39;ll own the full lifecycle of SaaS platform partnerships across LATAM — recruiting and developing vertical platforms that embed Stripe into their products, then activating and growing those relationships into meaningful contributors to regional revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Stripe Account Executives, you&#39;ll drive joint go-to-market motions, identify high-value opportunities within your partner portfolio, and own the co-sell pipeline from sourcing through to close. Expect a mix of partner engagement (enablement, solution development, business reviews), sales engagement (opportunity qualification and pipeline progression), and direct user engagement (prospecting, activation).This role requires a high level of dynamism and the ability to adapt to evolving business strategies and changing conditions. We are looking for someone who feels comfortable working in ambiguity and who can quickly adjust to new priorities, changes, and strategic shifts as the business evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recruit, and develop a portfolio of SaaS platform partners and community services partners across LATAM, with a primary focus on Mexico and support for Brazilian partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full partner lifecycle — from first contact through onboarding, enablement, activation, and long-term growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint go-to-market and co-selling initiatives with your partner portfolio; own forecasting across Partner Sourced Opportunities, Co-Sell, and Product Live metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly alongside Stripe AEs on co-sell opportunities, supporting the full deal cycle from pipeline sourcing through to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable Stripe and partner sales teams on the joint value proposition; lead partner business reviews, account mapping workshops, and enablement sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for partners within Stripe and represent Stripe within partner organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support LATAM&#39;s Retail, Insurance, Travel and Hospitality strategy through active engagement with relevant services, platform, and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in partner management, channel sales, or a combination of both at a technology company, with a demonstrated track record of building and scaling SaaS platform partnerships in Mexico&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with vertical SaaS platforms and Technology companies in Financial services, Travel and Hospitality, Retail, or adjacent industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in multi-party sales cycles, including co-sell and channel motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the payments, commerce, or fintech landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills, able to engage partner and customer leadership internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Brazilian market, alongside strong written and verbal proficiency in English and Portuguese&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ISVs or platform ecosystems such as Oracle, Salesforce, or SAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated comfort with AI tools in day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead&lt;/strong&gt; based in Singapore to own Stripe’s Global Partnerships strategy and execution across SE Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the regional Global Partnerships Lead, you will own Stripe’s most important in-market relationships across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners. You will set the partnership strategy for the region; identify, prioritize, and develop new opportunities; lead complex negotiations; and ensure partnerships deliver durable commercial, product, and expansion outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role at the intersection of product strategy, market expansion, and commercial execution. You will serve as Stripe’s senior partnership representative for the region, build trusted executive relationships with ecosystem partners, and lead alignment across Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, Legal, Risk, Compliance, Finance, Treasury, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Stripe’s &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead for SE Asia Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;, with end-to-end accountability for the regional partnership portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the regional strategy across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Stripe’s senior external relationships in the region, building alignment and representing Stripe’s strategic priorities with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partnership opportunities from market assessment and strategy through negotiation, contracting, onboarding, launch, governance, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional expansion-partnership strategy and execution, coordinating the partnerships required to establish, operate, and scale Stripe in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market intelligence, partner priorities, and ecosystem developments into clear recommendations for Stripe’s product and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional decision-making on commercial, product, operational, regulatory, and technical dependencies related to regional partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage partner-performance metrics, including commercial outcomes, product adoption, operational health, and strategic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and manage partnership risks, escalations, and trade-offs, ensuring sustained executive alignment internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategy, financial services, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in payments, fintech, e-commerce, banking, card networks, local payment methods, or adjacent financial-services sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex, strategic commercial negotiations with senior external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the payments and financial-partnership landscape in SE Asia, including relevant market dynamics and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and English executive communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to develop a clear point of view amid ambiguity, influence without authority, and drive decisions across complex internal and external stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with product and engineering organizations on partnerships with meaningful technical, operational, and regulatory dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate autonomously while balancing multiple high-priority initiatives and long-term strategic relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a regional or multi-market portfolio of payments or financial-infrastructure partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting market-entry, expansion, licensing, or ecosystem-development initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing senior relationships across banks, networks, payment-method providers, fintechs, or other relevant ecosystem partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, global technology company with cross-functional product, commercial, and regulatory stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Worldwide Alliances and Channels team develops and manages partnerships that help businesses adopt Stripe’s payments and financial infrastructure. These partnerships create new routes to customers, extend the reach of Stripe’s Sales teams, and help Stripe and its partners serve shared customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits on the Americas Alliances and Channels Tech Partnerships team. The team builds and executes joint go-to-market initiatives with major technology companies, with the goal of accelerating Stripe’s commercial growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of this team, you’ll lead global partnerships across the artificial intelligence ecosystem, with an initial emphasis on leading AI labs. You’ll work across Sales, Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, and regional partnerships teams to develop shared opportunities and turn them into scalable global partner strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Development Manager, you’ll define and build Stripe’s global partnerships across the artificial intelligence ecosystem, initially focusing on leading AI labs. Although the role sits on the Americas Alliances and Channels Tech Partnerships team, its mandate is global. You’ll establish relationships across partner organizations, develop shared value propositions, and translate early opportunities into joint commercial and product initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to build a new partnership motion from the ground up. You’ll start with focused opportunities, determine what works, and create a playbook that Stripe’s regional teams can apply around the world. Your work will span co-selling, co-marketing, and co-building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build senior relationships across the commercial, partnerships, product, and technical organizations of Stripe’s priority AI partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute global partner strategies, including shared value propositions, joint business plans, success measures, and operating cadences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and launch co-selling, co-marketing, and co-building initiatives that create value for Stripe, its partners, and shared customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional teams across Sales, Marketing, Product, Solutions Architecture, Legal, Finance, and regional partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and technical teams to identify opportunities for product collaboration and support productive technical conversations with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create repeatable partnership playbooks that regional teams can adapt for local markets and AI ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess partnership performance, identify opportunities and risks, and communicate progress clearly to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 or more years of experience in strategic partnerships, partner development, business development, or a related commercial role within technology or another complex business-to-business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a strategic technology partnership from its early stages and translating the relationship into joint commercial, go-to-market, or product outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing joint go-to-market plans with external partners and cross-functional Sales, Marketing, Product, or technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building relationships with senior external stakeholders and leading global or distributed teams through influence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and willingness to travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing partnerships with artificial intelligence companies, cloud providers, data platforms, developer platforms, or other global technology ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the artificial intelligence and data value chain, including the commercial and technical considerations involved in building partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across co-selling, co-marketing, and product or technical collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a partnership framework or playbook that was adopted across multiple regions or teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial infrastructure, financial services, or commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Worldwide Alliances and Channels team is responsible for developing and managing a global community of partners that helps ambitious businesses with industry-leading payments and financial infrastructure solutions and services. These partnerships help Stripe unlock market opportunities and accelerate user growth across segments, from startups to enterprise companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an enthusiastic Partner Development Manager (PDM) to join the Americas Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team. This is a partner relationship and revenue-generating role, reporting to Americas Alliances &amp;amp; Channels leadership. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll cultivate and maintain relationships with executives and sales teams at Stripe and partner organizations. You’ll secure new business, negotiate and close strategic partnerships, and help accelerate Stripe’s business across the region with systems integrators, consulting firms, and development agencies. You’ll also execute Stripe’s global partner programs, marketing, enablement, and co-selling initiatives across the region, driving partner participation and engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep relationships across sales, and marketing, and partner leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a revenue-generating joint go-to-market plan for assigned partners, including joint activities such as events and webinars, engagement with partner account executives through enablement and co-selling plans, and solution development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Stripe’s partner strategy with assigned partners, aligned with Stripe’s regional business and global partner strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for partners and identify partnership growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report weekly, monthly, and quarterly to key stakeholders, using a strong analytical approach and clear communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with program, marketing, and sales teams to execute partner programs, events, and sales engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build playbooks and collateral that help partners sell effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of partnerships or sales experience in technology, financial services, or a similarly complex B2B environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning and growing strategic partnerships that generated measurable commercial outcomes, such as sourced pipeline, closed revenue, partner engaged revenue, partner-sourced opportunities, or joint go-to-market activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing joint go-to-market plans with external partners and internal sales, marketing, and program stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating commercial agreements and influencing senior executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as required for partner meetings, events, and internal collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or advanced degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial infrastructure, or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with systems integrators, consulting firms, development agencies, or other ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building partner enablement programs, co-selling motions, events, playbooks, or sales collateral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data to assess partner performance, identify growth opportunities, and communicate results to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound business judgment, strong analytical skills, and a proven track record of taking ownership, leading data-driven analyses, and influencing results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Partnerships team sits within the Global Partnerships organization and is foundational to Stripe’s success. Our team is responsible for developing and managing Stripe’s relationships with global and regional banks, card networks, and money movement product partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team executes high-impact, cross-functional product partnership initiatives across existing products and early-stage financial products further up the stack. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and are essential to offering products used by millions of Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone to develop and execute high-impact initiatives and strategies with new and existing AMER bank partners. You’ll work closely with Product to support Stripe’s Treasury, Issuing, Capital, and Crypto businesses. This includes product development, defining and aligning on partner requirements, leading partner relationships to execute on those requirements, and negotiating, signing, and managing relationships with global partners to support Stripe’s growing MaaS product line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role requires close coordination with cross-functional teams, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, and Risk, as well as with partners’ senior executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Stripe’s critical bank partner relationships, with a focus on executing joint initiatives and launching new offerings that benefit Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure best-in-class, methodical partner and deal management rooted in milestone definition, a thoughtful and documented negotiation approach, and alignment on opportunities of mutual interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use industry knowledge to craft partnership and product strategies, and execute deals and initiatives that support Stripe’s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from and coordinate with internal cross-functional stakeholders, including Risk, Compliance, Product, Engineering, and Treasury, to create and execute partner and related product strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, educate them about Stripe’s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and partners’ executive teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage strategic planning, negotiation, and expansion activities with key partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple stakeholders with varying priorities, and drive creative solutions and commitment to shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use strategic and product creativity to design and develop new models for money movement, as well as extensions of Treasury, Issuing, Capital, and Crypto use cases for Stripe’s direct and platform users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit an operationally focused mindset, with the ability to lead teams through complex relationship-management activities by setting a clear vision and running tight processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;requirements&quot;&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, or a related field, including experience in partner management or business development with banking institutions at payment service providers or fintech companies enabling pay-in, pay-out, stored-value, or cross-border money movement experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of the banking and clearing landscape across multiple geographies, with a specific focus on transaction banking, e-money, safeguarding, multi-currency, and cross-border payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building proprietary global issuing, collection, and payout networks is ideal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating complex commercial deals with bank partners, including scaling those deals across multiple partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of fintech business models and associated best practices for compliance and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of working in a product-centric environment with significant internal and external dependencies across Product, Engineering, Legal, Sales, Risk, and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience executing industry-wide partnership strategies to build innovative product experiences and go-to-market models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills and ambition about what Stripe should pursue with partners, and how Stripe creates value and differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An operationally focused mindset, with the ability to see challenging deals through to success well beyond signing. Experience leading teams through execution using planning, metrics, and organizational structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset focused on contributing to the success of the team and company beyond individual goals and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at fintech companies that build payment and card-issuing programs or stablecoin-linked card programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategy across multiple markets or partner types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a company with industry groups, at conferences, or with senior external executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or guiding peers on partnership strategy, complex negotiations, or cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge is building financial infrastructure that makes money more programmable and global. The Financial Partnerships team develops the ecosystem that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across Bridge and Stripe to develop strategic relationships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners. These partnerships support reserve management, liquidity, distribution, and card-related products for both businesses and their shared customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior Partnership Development Manager, you will define and execute the financial-partnership strategy that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a strategic ecosystem of financial-partner relationships across markets. You will turn market insight into durable, high-impact partnerships, from strategy and negotiation through launch, expansion, and ongoing performance management. You will work directly with senior Stripe leaders and external executives to make investment tradeoffs, align priorities, and shape long-term product and partnership strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead multi-year partnership strategy across reserves, liquidity, distribution, card-related products, and the stablecoin ecosystem, using market and commercial insight to shape Bridge and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a strategic financial-partner ecosystem across markets, including partnership health, commercial performance, executive alignment, escalations, and expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, evaluate, structure, negotiate, and lead high-impact partnerships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set end-to-end deal strategy for complex, novel, or multi-market partnerships with material financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead company-level tradeoffs across partner economics, customer needs, product requirements, operational readiness, risk, and long-term strategic value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Treasury, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Finance, Engineering, and go-to-market teams to set requirements, align senior stakeholders, and execute shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a differentiated point of view on financial services and digital assets, represent Stripe and Bridge with senior external stakeholders, and share expertise that strengthens the broader Partnerships organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategic finance, treasury, or a related field, including ownership of complex, high-impact external partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently set partnership strategy, influence senior executives, and drive cross-functional alignment on ambiguous, high-stakes company priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of structuring, negotiating, and managing high-value, multi-year partnerships with material strategic, financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience working with financial institutions or infrastructure providers, such as banks, exchanges, asset managers, market makers, liquidity providers, payments companies, or stablecoin ecosystem participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and experience leading both commercial and technical partnership conversations with senior internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in stablecoins, crypto, card issuing, or stablecoin-linked card programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategy across multiple markets or partner types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a company with industry groups, at conferences, or with senior external executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or guiding peers on partnership strategy, complex negotiations, or cross-functional execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Partnerships team sources, develops, and manages relationships with the payments ecosystem partners that power Link, Stripe&#39;s consumer wallet. Our team drives the growth and utility of Link by building partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, crypto providers, and emerging commerce platforms. We execute on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives that expand Link&#39;s acceptance, improve performance, and enable new payment experiences—including agentic commerce. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager who builds and manages Link&#39;s payments partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment method providers, and crypto and stablecoin providers. You&#39;ll own the strategy and execution of partnerships that expand Link&#39;s payment capabilities, improve transaction performance, and position Link as the default payments layer for agentic commerce. You&#39;ll negotiate commercial agreements, drive technical integrations, and shape Link&#39;s payments roadmap in collaboration with these partners. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, and others. You&#39;ll also lead relationship management and partner closely with external partners&#39; executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute Link&#39;s payments partnership strategy across card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, and crypto and stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage commercial agreements with payment partners that expand Link&#39;s acceptance footprint, improve authorization rates, and unlock new payment capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the card network and issuer landscape—including scheme rules, tokenization frameworks, authentication protocols, and competitive dynamics—to inform partnership strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partnerships that enable Link to serve as the payments layer for agentic commerce, working with networks and issuers to establish rules, liability frameworks, and technical standards for agent-initiated transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather inputs from and coordinate with internal cross-functional stakeholders (including product, risk, compliance, engineering, and security) to drive creation and execution of partner strategy including our global LPM roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to define requirements and shape Link&#39;s payments product roadmap based on partner capabilities and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, educate them about Link&#39;s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and our partners&#39; executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and effectively analyze new partnership opportunities, ultimately making recommendations to relevant decision makers and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit an operationally focused mindset, with an ability to lead teams through complex relationship management activities by setting a clear vision and running tight processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re a skilled dealmaker and a strategist by nature. You understand how to work closely with Product and Engineering teams and can formulate partner strategies that drive tangible and measurable results. You&#39;re energized by the intersection of payments infrastructure and emerging commerce models, and you see the opportunity to define how payments work in an agentic world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in or working closely with card networks, card issuers, digital wallets, or payments infrastructure providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with partners, including scaling such deals across multiple partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, in both verbal and written form, and ability to influence stakeholders across a wide variety of functions, including at executive levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, especially an ability to understand product strategy and use this understanding to define requirements for scaling products through partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategies and identifying, sourcing, and analyzing new partnership opportunities in greenfield segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with card scheme rules, tokenization (network tokens, device tokens), authentication frameworks (3DS, SCA), and issuer-side authorization optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with emerging payment models such as agentic commerce, embedded payments, or programmable payment flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new partnership category or vertical from zero—defining the strategy, establishing first partnerships, and scaling the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Payments Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with large payment method and ecosystem partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow priority payment-method partnerships, with a focus on strategic wallets, buy now, pay later (BNPL) providers, and related payment partners. You will manage day-to-day partner relationships, lead defined commercial and product initiatives, and work across Stripe to increase payment-method adoption and deliver better experiences for users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires sound commercial judgment, a structured approach to execution, and the ability to bring together internal and external stakeholders with different priorities. You will develop deep expertise in your partners and the payment-method ecosystem, using that context to identify opportunities, inform Stripe’s decisions, and execute initiatives that support Stripe’s product and business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage one or more priority payment-method partnerships, driving the execution of joint initiatives and launching new offerings that benefit Stripe users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage internal and external stakeholders with varying priorities, driving alignment on shared goals and ensuring structured partner and deal management rooted in clear milestones, performance metrics, and opportunities of mutual interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow Stripe’s relationships with partners, including their senior executives and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from and coordinate with cross-functional stakeholders, including Risk, Legal, Product, and Engineering, to execute deals and related partner product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring an operationally focused mindset to relationship management, setting clear goals, running tight processes, and proactively identifying opportunities to improve execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategic partnerships or business development, including 3+ years working in payments, fintech, or financial institutions, and 3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with financial and technology institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading commercial discussions or negotiations using established deal strategies and frameworks, with sound judgment about trade-offs and when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning partner relationships, channel or distribution initiatives, and/or cross-functional commercial programs from planning through execution, and working in a product-centric environment with meaningful internal and external dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take initiative, handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility; strong verbal and written communication skills; and the ability to influence internal and external stakeholders across a wide variety of functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, including the ability to understand Stripe’s product portfolio and strategy and use this understanding to define requirements with partners and evaluate new partnership opportunities, along with interest in and intellectual curiosity about payments, economic infrastructure, and Stripe’s partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, payment methods, wallets, BNPL, or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Worldwide Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team is responsible for developing and managing a global community of partners that helps ambitious businesses with industry-leading payments and financial infrastructure solutions and services. These partnerships provide Stripe with the opportunity to unlock our market opportunity, supporting us in accelerating our users growth across all market segments from Startup to Enterprise companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow existing, mature, strategic systems integrator (SI) partnerships across EMEA. The focus is on deepening established relationships and improving joint commercial outcomes, rather than incubating or building new partnerships.&amp;nbsp;You’ll manage a defined portfolio of large SI organizations, owning each partnership end to end. You’ll engage senior commercial and technical stakeholders, align on shared priorities, and turn joint partner plans into measurable pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a partner relationship and revenue-generating role. You’ll work closely with regional sales teams and partner stakeholders on joint account planning and customer engagements. You’ll also coordinate with partner solution engineering, marketing, and program teams to strengthen partner capabilities and grow their Stripe practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a defined portfolio of existing, mature, strategic SI partnerships end to end, from joint planning and stakeholder alignment through execution and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with senior commercial and technical stakeholders across large partner organizations, including alliance, sales, practice, and delivery leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute joint partner plans with clear commercial priorities, owners, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe’s enterprise sales teams and partner account teams on account mapping, opportunity identification, and co-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, track progress, and coordinate the teams needed to move joint opportunities forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partner Solution Engineering to deepen partners’ technical capabilities, support training and certification, and strengthen their ability to deliver Stripe solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate targeted campaigns, events, and enablement with marketing and program teams to support joint commercial priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular partner business reviews, agree on actions with senior stakeholders, and follow through on delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand established partnerships across accounts, practices, and EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report clearly on partnership performance, pipeline, risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 years+ Experience in partnerships, sales, or business development within a technology or financial services organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing established SI or consulting partnerships, with an understanding of how these organizations sell and deliver services to enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing existing partnerships and progressing commercial opportunities against defined goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own partner relationships end to end, coordinating internal and partner teams to deliver agreed outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging senior commercial and technical stakeholders within large, complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in joint account planning, pipeline development, or enterprise sales engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand customer needs and explain how a joint solution addresses them, working with technical specialists when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple partner initiatives and work through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for partner and customer engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
