&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Partner Marketing team extends Stripe’s marketing reach to customers and prospects by educating, engaging and enabling partners, globally, to build market awareness and generate demand for their Stripe solutions and services. We recruit prospective partners and support the on-boarding and growth of existing partners as they build, launch, market, and scale business through the Stripe Partner Ecosystem and the Stripe platform. We partner closely with our global partnerships, GTM partners, marketing, and product teams and serve many different partner types.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced, strategic, and results-oriented marketing leader to own Stripe’s global partner marketing strategy for Services partners—including GSIs—and Technology/ISV partners. You’ll lead a global team, define the multi-year operating and investment model, build influential relationships with partner and Stripe leaders, and scale programs that drive partner-sourced and partner-attached pipeline, customer activation, and product adoption. This role requires setting a clear long-term direction while leading through others and using performance insights to focus the organization on its highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the multi-year vision and global strategy for Services, GSI, and Technology/ISV partner marketing, translating Stripe’s company, marketing, and partnerships priorities into an operating model, investment strategy, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing global team of four Partner Marketing professionals across APAC, AMER, and EMEA. Establish clear accountability, build organizational capability, evolve the team as business needs change, and ensure agencies and vendors extend the team effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with partner CMOs and senior Stripe leaders. Develop joint strategies with priority partners and align global and regional teams around shared priorities, investments, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of differentiated programs for strategic partners and scalable programs for the broader ecosystem. Integrate partners into Stripe campaigns, regional initiatives, co-sell motions, events, content, and enablement to drive pipeline, activation, and product adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape joint value propositions, messaging, and customer evidence, and turn successful programs into reusable playbooks that can scale across partners and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance for market development funds and other investments, alongside the performance framework, dashboards, and business-review cadence. Use data and financial insight to assess impact, address underperformance, and reallocate resources toward the strongest opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience, including substantial experience in partner, ecosystem, channel, or alliances marketing and a strong understanding of partner business models and indirect GTM motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting and leading global marketing strategy across regions, translating company priorities into long-term plans, scalable operating models, and measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, leading, and developing a distributed team of experienced marketers, including setting direction and accountability, coaching talent, and evolving organizational capabilities through change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex cross-functional initiatives with a high degree of autonomy, build trusted relationships with partner and internal executives, and align senior stakeholders without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success delivering measurable partner-marketing outcomes and using analytical and financial judgment to manage significant budgets or market development funds, evaluate ROI, and make portfolio trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the judgment to simplify complex issues, articulate a compelling vision, and turn strategy and performance insights into clear executive recommendations and action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing marketing strategies for Services, GSI, Technology, or ISV partners in a global, high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, enterprise software, or an adjacent industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breadth across partner marketing and adjacent disciplines such as demand generation, product marketing, field marketing, or integrated campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies or vendors across markets and holding them accountable for quality and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Global Partner Marketing team drives growth by developing and scaling go-to-market programs with Stripe&#39;s most strategic channel, technology, and alliance partners. Working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, and GTM teams, the team builds the infrastructure, enablement, and co-marketing programs that extend Stripe&#39;s reach across the partner ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Online &amp;amp; Regional Events Program Manager, you will build the operating foundation behind Partner Marketing’s online and in-person event portfolio. You’ll turn priorities into repeatable programs, capacity and investment plans, and measurable business outcomes. Working closely with Marketing Operations, regional and global marketing teams, and agency partners, you’ll improve how events are selected, planned, delivered, and evaluated—helping the team scale its impact while making thoughtful trade-offs across resources, timing, and budget.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale repeatable event motions across Partner Marketing’s online and in-person portfolio, including partner-led pre-sales and post-sales workshops, partner enablement programs, and co-sell events. Partner with Marketing Operations to use existing infrastructure and processes where possible, improving efficiency and consistency across programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the measurement and analytical framework for partner events. Identify and quantify high-value opportunities, establish event selection criteria and performance benchmarks, and assess results against defined business outcomes. Diagnose the root causes of underperformance and recommend changes that improve impact, efficiency, and return on investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a capacity model and integrated editorial calendar for Partner Marketing events. Translate priorities and available resources into a clear execution plan, identify capacity constraints and tradeoffs, and recommend where the team should invest, defer, or scale..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the Partner Marketing events budget and forecasting process, tracking commitments and actual spend, identifying risks early, and maintaining forecast accuracy within 1% accuracy .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate Partner Marketing-led events into regional and global marketing calendars. Coordinate with regional, field, partner, and global marketing teams to align timing, audiences, messaging, and resources; identify conflicts or gaps; and recommend solutions that maximize collective impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and launch a shared-services model for Partner Marketing events. Define the service offering, operating model, intake process, roles, and success measures; support the selection and onboarding of a global agency partner; and drive adoption of the service across the Partner Marketing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage agency performance and service quality by setting clear briefs, milestones, service-level agreements, and escalation paths. Monitor delivery against agreed standards and recommend process or resourcing improvements when performance falls short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for an analytical and highly organized program manager who can independently lead complex, cross-functional event programs from planning through measurement. You are comfortable operating through ambiguity, managing several workstreams at once, and using data to identify opportunities, anticipate risks, and recommend improvements. You build trusted relationships across teams, communicate clearly, and balance attention to executional detail with a focus on business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant experience in B2B event marketing, partner marketing, field marketing, or marketing program management, including online and in-person programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently managing complex, cross-functional programs, including defining timelines, deliverables, dependencies, roles, and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with experience establishing performance benchmarks, evaluating program impact and ROI, diagnosing underperformance, and translating findings into recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing program budgets and forecasts, tracking commitments and actual spend, and identifying financial risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build repeatable processes, capacity plans, calendars, or operating models that improve efficiency and execution across multiple programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies or vendors, including developing briefs, setting expectations and milestones, monitoring performance, and resolving delivery issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to align stakeholders across regions, functions, and levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing events or programs for technology, channel, alliance, or ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating a shared-services model across multiple teams or regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting global and regional marketing calendars and coordinating programs across AMER, EMEA, and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing operations, pipeline measurement, event attribution, and CRM or marketing-automation systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As a member of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team, you will be responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe’s partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education and enablement with our partner organization. The right candidate will be a critical technical liaison to the Stripe Partner Development Manager. This will involve creating comprehensive technical business plans for Partners, including identifying, incubating and bringing to market service/solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solution Architect is someone who is intellectually curious, motivated to win, open and entrepreneurial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, PSAs build highly consultative trusted relationships with executives and technical decision makers in the customer’s organisation to provide business and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges. We architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with key partners to build out their Stripe capabilities and solutions to grow their business and drive non-linear growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute enablement plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be at the forefront of technical discussions &amp;amp; solution deep-dives with partners on the value Stripe can provide to their clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with CTOs, engineering &amp;amp; other technical leads at key partners to share technology roadmaps, demonstrate the latest innovations, and define a solution strategy to expand the partnership revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate success internally through QBRs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight, guidance, and assistance during the partners sales process to ensure mutual success in joint opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate the Stripe sales team on key partner solutions and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for key partners within specific sales regions and identify areas for sales partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on technical content (sample code, demos, etc.) to show partners how to implement specific use cases or best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Partner-focused guidance on Stripe’s product through feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role such as solution consultant, solutions architect, sales engineer, for a global software enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical acumen in API integrations, SaaS platforms, and enterprise architectures, with particular emphasis on order-to-cash processes and billing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with subscription, billing, and payment solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of financial infrastructure industry trends and emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience co-selling and co-solutioning with go-to-market partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer meetings to gain strategic footing and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle and API architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills, presentation skills, and confidence in explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn Stripe solutions such as Payments, Billing, Connect, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand how a wide variety of applications such as ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax and legacy systems interact with each other in an enterprise technology ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple strategic opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and creative thinker who can proactively identify challenges and maintain a positive approach when facing difficult obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Partner Solutions Architect, Consulting Partners&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Partner Solutions Architecture team, you will provide technical guidance to Stripe’s partners. Our goal is to drive growth through joint solution development, education, and enablement in collaboration with our partner organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as a critical technical counterpart to Stripe’s Partner Development Managers. This includes creating technical business plans with partners and identifying, developing, and bringing to market service and solution offerings built on or with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A successful Partner Solutions Architect is intellectually curious, motivated to win, and comfortable operating with an open and entrepreneurial mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Solutions Architect, you will build trusted relationships with C-level executives and technical decision-makers across partner organizations and their customers. You will provide business and technical thought leadership, serve as a trusted advisor, and help solve mission-critical business challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also help partners design business models that create new monetization opportunities and drive growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with strategic consulting partners, including systems integrators (SIs) and global systems integrators (GSIs), to build their Stripe capabilities, develop solutions, and grow joint business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable horizontal and industry-specific solutions with partners. (&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.partners/solutions&quot;&gt;https://stripe.partners/solutions&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic pre-sales opportunities and help secure joint technical wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and execute technical enablement plans for priority partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discussions and solution deep dives that demonstrate the value Stripe can provide to partners and their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage partner CTOs, engineering leaders, and other technical decision-makers to share product roadmaps, demonstrate new capabilities, and define joint solution strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide partners through the sales and solution-design process to support mutual success in joint opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate Stripe’s sales teams on key partner capabilities, solutions, and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for strategic partners within assigned sales regions and identify opportunities for greater sales collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop technical content, including sample code and demonstrations, that shows partners how to implement specific use cases and follow best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent partner needs internally by providing structured feedback on Stripe’s products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe at partner and industry forums and contribute to joint thought leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Stripe Partner Advocates to drive innovation and adoption of Stripe products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and communicate progress, outcomes, risks, and opportunities through quarterly business reviews and other established forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements for the role. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in solutions architecture, sales engineering, technical consulting, or a comparable customer-facing technical role within a global software company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working within partner ecosystems, including SIs, GSIs, or independent software vendors (ISVs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated executive engagement skills and presence, with the ability to establish strong relationships with key decision-makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer and partner meetings to establish strategic alignment and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle, APIs, and enterprise integration patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication and presentation skills, with the ability to explain complex concepts to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to learn and advise on Stripe products, including Payments, Billing, Connect, and others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of how ERP, CRM, billing, tax, and legacy systems interact within enterprise technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities across multiple strategic partners, customers, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a customer-facing domain expert in payments, including presenting and architecting solutions for enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Stripe or other RESTful APIs into web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system design and building and deploying complex applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting global enterprise technical sales at a leading enterprise software company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping customers adopt and expand their use of cloud-based software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and actively seeking new knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work independently and confidently develop a path forward with customers under ambiguous circumstances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and creative thinking, with the ability to identify challenges proactively and maintain a constructive approach when facing difficult obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work effectively with cross-functional teams to support Stripe’s users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Hybrid work at Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is available either in an office or a remote location (35+ miles or 56+ km from a Stripe office).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;In-office expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office-assigned Stripes spend at least 50% of the time in a given month in their local office or with users. This hits a balance between bringing people together for in-person collaboration and learning from each other, while supporting flexibility about how to do this in a way that makes sense for individuals and their teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Working remotely at Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A remote location is defined as being 35 miles (56 kilometers) or more from one of our offices. While you would be welcome to come into the office for team/business meetings, on-sites, meet-ups, and events, our expectation is you would regularly work from home rather than a Stripe office. Stripe does not cover the cost of relocating to a remote location. We encourage you to apply for roles that match the location where you currently live or plan to live.&lt;/p&gt;

