&lt;li&gt;A creative and process-oriented mindset, with an interest in improving workflows and the candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with internal stakeholders in a collaborative, service-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the key drivers to our success is a committed and rigorous emphasis on our people. We believe that our competitive advantage lies in our talent and that we can build a sustainable advantage by attracting, enabling and cultivating the world’s most exceptional people to do the very best work of their careers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;People Operations Specialist, HR Compliance&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Global People Operations team. This role is a critical pillar of our People Operations function, focusing on complex operational challenges and continuous improvement across the employee lifecycle. You will serve as a critical operational stakeholder enabling HR transformation by ensuring seamless support, optimizing processes with data-driven insights, and collaborating closely with our Centers of Excellence (COEs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audits and controls Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Own Global People Operations participation in recurring compliance audits including SOX, HR security controls, and external audits. Coordinate evidence gathering, manage timelines, and serve as the People Operations point of contact for audit teams across multiple concurrent cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Optimization and Data-Driven Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;: Bring innovative, data-driven ideas and recommend enhancements to existing HR processes and workflows. Interpret data and formulate insights to proactively drive continuous operational improvements that enhance the overall employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory filing management:&lt;/strong&gt;Track and execute Stripe&#39;s recurring compliance filings as required. Maintain filing calendars and monitor global regulatory changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder and COE Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams and Centers of Excellence (COEs), including Procurement, Employment Legal, and Employee Relations, to ensure cross-functional compliance obligations are met, processes align, and smooth handoffs occur across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HRIS Management and Integrity: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain the accuracy and integrity of our HR Information System (Workday) by accurately entering employee change transactions manually and through bulk data uploads, ensuring a robust and reliable foundation for all HR data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOP Development and Documentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Create and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) that document workflows from end to end, encompassing all system interactions and cross-functional handoffs for clarity and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor management: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage compliance vendor relationships — background check providers, labor law poster services, employment verification platforms — including contract renewals, SLA oversight, and service transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigating Ambiguity: &lt;/strong&gt;Operate effectively in ambiguous situations using your expertise, Stripe’s operating principles, and stakeholder perspectives to determine the best course of action and communicate clearly about systemic blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in HR compliance, People Operations, or employment law support, with direct ownership of compliance obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of HR processes, policies, and best practices across the employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or supporting external audits, including evidence gathering and cross-functional coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical aptitude and proficiency with Workday (specifically data accuracy and management) and experience with Salesforce or a similar ticketing system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US employment compliance requirements: I-9/E-Verify, EEO-1 filing, state pay equity reporting, labor law posting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving operational improvements and contributing to significant program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience collaborating effectively with COEs (e.g., Legal, ER, People Partners) to resolve complex employee issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Written and verbal English communication skills including translating regulatory requirements into plain-language SOPs and stakeholder updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally and cross-culturally in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, with a focus on accuracy, quality, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency with the ability to interpret data and formulate insights to drive improvements and measure program success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency, including the ability to use AI tools effectively, assess output quality, and recognize when human review or escalation is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SOX controls, internal audit processes, or global compliance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with international employment compliance — GDPR/ROPA, Right to Work checks outside the US, or EMEA/APAC regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving global HR compliance program infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recruiting depends on systems that work reliably for recruiters, hiring managers, interviewers, and candidates. The Recruiting Systems Operations Administrator helps keep those systems running and improves the support experience around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with Recruiting Operations, Global People Operations, and People Systems. This role supports a clear division of work between routine service delivery and the system governance, integrations, complex configuration, and strategic work owned by Recruiting Systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working CDMX business hours while partnering across Americas time zones, you’ll manage a defined Tier 2 Recruiting Systems portfolio. You’ll troubleshoot tool issues, resolve requests, track recurring problems, and partner with People Systems on improvements. This hands-on role is well suited to someone who enjoys working across systems, applying sound judgment within established processes, and making complex operations easier for others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and resolve Tier 2 support requests through established channels, maintaining clear requester updates, case records, and handoff notes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot recruiting systems, including DocuSign, Gem, LinkedIn Talent Insights, HackerRank, Harver, BrightHire, Qualtrics, Eightfold, Greenhouse, and related platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process recruiting workflow requests, including assessment updates, job-posting changes, candidate-record updates, approved offer amendments, requisition pooling and unpooling, and requests to keep jobs open temporarily or close inactive jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor request volume, aging, service-level expectations, and recurring issues to identify risks and opportunities to improve support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and improve runbooks, templates, knowledge-base content, intake forms, and self-service guidance based on common request patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in release testing, validation, quality reviews, recurring Recruiting operations cycles, and reviews of queue trends, documentation gaps, and operational risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems administrators on releases and support priorities, providing complete handoffs when requests require expertise in areas such as complex configuration, integrations, reporting, privacy, security, policy interpretation, or permissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in recruiting operations, People operations, service delivery, systems support, customer support, or a similar operations environment, including managing a request queue, ticketing system, or case-management process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot system issues, follow defined processes, document work clearly, and identify when escalation is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, organization, follow-through, and the ability to prioritize competing requests while providing clear, timely updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling confidential candidate, recruiting, or employee information with discretion, and comfort learning enterprise systems and working across multiple tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Jira, Salesforce, or a comparable ticketing or case-management tool, and professional fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Greenhouse or another applicant tracking system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting recruiting technology such as BrightHire, LinkedIn Recruiter, LinkedIn Talent Insights, GoodTime, Gem, HackerRank, DocuSign, Qualtrics, Harver, or Eightfold&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Recruiting Operations, Talent Acquisition Coordination, People Systems, or software-as-a-service administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting offer processes, job-posting management, interview operations, or recruiter onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating or maintaining standard operating procedures, runbooks, and knowledge articles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic spreadsheet, reporting, or data-quality skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with service-level agreements, queue metrics, audit controls, or release testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-success-looks-like-in-your-first-six-months&quot;&gt;What success looks like in your first six months&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage your Tier 2 support portfolio with prompt resolutions and clear status updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide reliable coverage across Americas time zones and set transparent escalation expectations for recruiters and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve standard issues across DocuSign, Gem, LinkedIn Talent Insights, HackerRank, Harver, and Greenhouse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate Tier 3 requests to the correct People Systems owner with complete context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate ticket records, handoffs, runbooks, and knowledge-base guides that improve self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability of recruiting technology for recruiters, hiring managers, interviewers, and candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the platform knowledge needed to take on additional approved support responsibilities over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. Stripe’s People &amp;amp; Places Operations team will sit within the SDC and is a highly collaborative, cross-functional team that drives key support for the People and Places function. We work with many different teams at Stripe. We are nimble and flexible individuals that can wear many different hats. We don’t mind working through ambiguity and love adding organization to chaos. We believe that success is not defined by any one individual, but rather by the collective work of the entire team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic and operational leadership for the newly-formed People Support team in CDMX, translating the global Core Ops strategy into an effective local operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a small team People Support specialists through clear expectations, regular coaching, actionable feedback, and quality calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish local team practices, coverage, escalation paths, and ways of working that integrate effectively with the global People Support organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily operations, including queue health, workload allocation, service levels, and escalations, while contributing directly during the team’s ramp or periods of high volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use service metrics, case trends, and feedback to set priorities, identify root causes, and improve workflows, documentation, and the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People, People Systems, and specialist teams to clarify ownership, improve handoffs, and implement global initiatives locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards for case handling, written responses, documentation, data accuracy, privacy, and operational controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand the CDMX team’s capabilities and use AI tools thoughtfully to improve service quality, operational efficiency, and the team’s ability to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and operational leadership, including the ability to establish new team practices while contributing directly to service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership, coaching, communication, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and attention to detail when handling complex or ambiguous People matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze operational data, identify patterns, set priorities, and turn insights into practical improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency, including the ability to use AI tools appropriately, assess output quality, protect sensitive data, and recognize when human review is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6-8 years of experience in People operations, shared services, support operations, or a related field, including 2+ years leading or managing others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A graduate or postgraduate qualification in human resources or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing or developing a new team, service, location, or operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing case queues, escalations, service levels, and operational quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading operational improvements or implementing global initiatives within a local team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with People systems and case-management tools, such as Workday or comparable platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of core People processes, including worker data, benefits, talent mobility, equity, compensation, and exits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance immediate operational needs with longer-term team development and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the key drivers of our success is a committed and rigorous emphasis on our people. We believe that our competitive advantage lies in our talent and that we can build a sustainable advantage by attracting, enabling, and cultivating the world’s most exceptional people to do the very best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for an experienced People Partner to drive that effort across our Finance organization. This includes enabling leaders and managers to build successful teams, aligning business strategy with our people strategy, creating an environment where Stripes of all backgrounds can thrive, and using research and insights to develop best practices and programs to promote meaningful career experiences at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Partner for our Finance organization, you’ll play a direct role in shaping the organization and career experiences of the Stripes within it. You’ll partner directly with our Chief Financial Officer and Finance leadership team to develop and deliver on our people strategy and enable leaders to build high-impact, healthy teams that deliver outstanding results for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support the Finance leadership team and the organization through continued growth and evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic consultant to Finance leaders, partnering to align business and people strategies, with an understanding of the function’s priorities, operating rhythms, and talent needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across People teams to develop and deliver programs that address Finance’s needs and advance Stripe’s broader people strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, insights, and People expertise to inform organizational strategy, structure, and programs that improve team health and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and coach leaders and managers on organizational design, change management, and ways of working that balance efficiency, accountability, and effective cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support leaders as they execute on global talent and organizational planning, building the Finance capabilities and leadership capacity needed for future business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leaders on succession planning and the development and retention of critical Finance talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a culture guided by our Operating Principles that combines high standards, kindness, and a commitment to improving how teams work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience as a People Partner or in an equivalent people business partnering role, preferably with a mix of experience in fast-growing technology companies and more established organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with and influencing executive and senior leaders to align people strategy with business priorities and improve organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and project management skills, with the ability to translate people data and business context into practical recommendations, design clear processes, and take a detail-oriented yet flexible approach to problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner with and influence diverse groups and experience levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and discretion when working with sensitive people and business information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a Finance organization, with an understanding of its talent markets, specialist career paths, and leadership needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategist and scaler who can connect Finance’s business priorities with the organizational capabilities, structures, and talent needed to deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A partner and connector who builds trusted relationships with managers and leaders by providing practical insights, anticipating challenges, and offering constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A business partner who can develop a deep understanding of Stripe’s strategy and Finance’s role in it, then translate that understanding into people priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborator who enjoys working with leaders to create effective teams and organizational structures across a global function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic thinker whose decisions are informed by data, experience, and Stripe’s Operating Principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A coach who loves building and developing high-impact teams and helping leaders manage growth and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach. Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSA) are domain experts aligned to specific Stripe solutions and customer buying centers. We have in-depth knowledge of specific solution offerings and a deep understanding of customer challenges. We align with specialist product sellers on deals, advise the broader pre-sales team on complex opportunities, support pipeline development and revenue attainment, serve as an advisor on go-to-market sales plays, and provide critical insights to our product and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Specialist Solution Architect, you will lead in-depth product discussions with our top users and prospects and execute against our go-to-market strategy for our Money Management products, including Stripe Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite. You will educate our product and engineering teams on market trends and strongly influence the product roadmap for the Money Management product suite at Stripe, helping us become the primary way merchants run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert on Stripe’s Money Management products (including Capital, Issuing, Treasury, and our global Payouts suite) to accelerate opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a deep understanding of embedded finance applications that leverage Stripe’s products, articulating how they combine to create a compounding platform for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with users on a broad range of embedded finance use cases, from charge card programs and global payouts to a comprehensive suite of financing options including revenue-based financing, loans, and lines of credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the compliance requirements of solutions built with Stripe products, especially as we expand our offerings into new markets and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, share, and learn best practices and reusable assets with the broader GTM organization to enhance the quality and efficiency of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reference architectures to uplevel the team and refine reference solutions based on product enhancements and feedback from customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Money Management product sales team and be an active part of the opportunity team for Stripe’s largest customers to lead strategy and own key relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a “Voice of the Customer” internally, providing actionable insights to product stakeholders to influence the Money Management product roadmap and feature prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide critical insights on emerging technologies, including the application of stablecoins for money movement, lending, and global financial access, to influence the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the sales process for the product and provide the Sales team with tools and training to qualify potential leads, including simplifying our distribution for faster onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on competitive analysis and market differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing events including executive briefings, conferences, user groups, and trade shows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
