&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Procurement team provides services to the businesses that are the backbone of Stripe. Stripe’s broader Procurement organization consists of Third Party Risk, Strategic Sourcing, Supplier Deal Management (Procurement Contracting), Procurement Enablement, Accounts Payable, and Travel and Expense.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Procurement Contracting function, Supplier Deal Management (SDM), builds an efficient supplier contracting process, reduces friction for business leaders, works in partnership with Third Party Risk and Legal to minimize risk, and increases the speed at which Stripe can engage key suppliers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SDM’s mission is to drive agreements efficiently through appropriate channels, bringing structure to the overall contracting process in partnership with stakeholders while providing a customized and guided user experience and effectively managing value and risk for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of SDM and working closely with SDM Leads, you’ll support the supplier contracting process, from answering initial questions and reviewing use cases to negotiating commercial terms and supporting contract lifecycle management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer initial questions and educate directly responsible individuals (DRIs) on the overall risk assessment and supplier contracting process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct an initial review of DRI-provided use cases and appropriate contractual terms, or assemble appropriate Stripe templates, and prepare agreements for legal review according to defined guidelines when necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and negotiate commercial terms in supplier agreements when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor productivity and communication with DRIs using our procurement tool, Zip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage internal stakeholders, including Legal, Sourcing, Third Party Risk, and Stripe DRIs, to understand their needs and translate them into a risk-balanced approach to preparing contracts using training and existing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage engagements within our procurement system, Zip, and contract lifecycle management system, Ironclad, and support end-to-end contract lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with respective internal teams to resolve business inquiries and troubleshoot issues related to contracting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
