&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk Operations Enablement team sits within the Risk Operations org and is responsible for building and operating the core business and strategic programs that are critical to Risk Operations. These programs range from operational excellence initiatives to high-priority, cross-functional initiatives that typically require partnering across broader Risk (e.g., Risk Product) and risk-adjacent (e.g., Policy) teams. More specifically, we both lead initiatives to make step changes in the Risk User Experience and devise and execute strategies to ensure that a wide range of missing-critical business processes are effective at achieving our dual goals of preventing bad actors from exploiting our systems and delivering an exceptional user experience for legitimate users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner cross-functionally across Risk (e.g., Risk Product) and Risk-adjacent (e.g., Policy) teams to lead ambiguous, high-priority problem spaces that change the trajectory of Risk Operations. You&#39;ll also partner across Risk Operations to deliver and measure processes that enable operational excellence at scale within the Risk Operations org.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex global programs, from initial scoping to design and execution and work on high-impact strategic initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with multiple stakeholders across Risk Operations, Risk Product, Risk Eng, and other stakeholder teams (e.g., Policy, Data Science) to prioritize and maximize the impact of your projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and launch programs that lead to step-change improvements in our operational processes and business outcomes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the Risk Operations expert and partner closely with our cross-functional stakeholders to scope and execute large projects to create operational efficiencies and ensure operational readiness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embody our Operating Principles and foster our values and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in risk program management, strategy, management consulting, business operations, or operations program management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to dig deep into the data and think from first principles while delivering the best results&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple stakeholders with varying priorities and drive creative solutions and commitment to a shared goal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills with experience managing end-to-end execution of projects and programs that have transformed your company&#39;s operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys solving complex and hard problems and can turn incomplete, conflicting, or ambiguous inputs into solid action plans and deliver quantifiable business impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify repeated user and specialist-facing issues and build scalable solutions and processes to address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years in consulting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL or willingness to learn&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or other graduate degree&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience partnering with Product, Eng, and Operations teams preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Total Rewards Strategy &amp;amp; Enablement (TR S&amp;amp;E) team translates people strategy into business impact, building the infrastructure, programs, and systems that make Total Rewards work at scale. We&#39;re a small, high-leverage team that bridges strategy and execution, partnering with People leadership and cross-functional teams across Finance, Legal, and the business to turn ambiguous problems into durable programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Total Rewards programs span compensation, benefits, equity, internal mobility/immigration, and mergers and acquisitions (M&amp;amp;A), each with cross-functional dependencies, regulatory stakes, and direct impact on the Stripes they affect. Delivering these programs well takes a Project Manager who develops real subject matter depth, engages with pillar leads as a strategic partner, and brings structure to decisions that aren&#39;t always clear-cut.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Project Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own high-priority Total Rewards projects and programs end to end. You&#39;ll work closely with our Benefits, Compensation, Equity, Talent Mobility, and M&amp;amp;A pillars, building expertise in how these programs work and what it takes to land them well. Some programs have established playbooks you&#39;ll sharpen; others are less defined and will need you to help shape the approach before you execute it. Across all of them, you&#39;ll identify dependencies early, proactively surface and mitigate risks, and keep complex, multi-stakeholder work moving toward clear outcomes. This is a high-leverage individual contributor role for someone who brings both rigor and judgment to every project they own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end project management for high-profile cyclical and transformational Total Rewards projects, from intake and scoping through go-live and handoff to program owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and embed with project teams across the Total Rewards and People portfolio, raising the quality bar and building PM capability across the extended team, not just doing the work yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build subject matter expertise across Benefits, Compensation, Equity, Talent Mobility, and M&amp;amp;A — becoming a reliable strategic thought partner to pillar teams on program decisions, not just a tracker of status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, automate, and continuously improve the infrastructure that makes program management repeatable and scalable: intake frameworks, project plan templates, SOPs, playbooks, and handoff checklists for common program types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools in your daily work and the team&#39;s workflows, using them to accelerate synthesis, drafting, stakeholder communications, and documentation, and actively identifying new opportunities to work faster and better&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional alignment across People and key partner functions (Legal, Finance, Corporate Technology, and others), creating shared visibility into priorities, dependencies, and blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex, ambiguous program questions with rigor and independence, owning work from problem definition through final recommendation — including defining the approach, monitoring progress, identifying risks early, and putting mitigation in place before issues land&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface patterns and gaps across the program portfolio, translating observations into structured analysis and recommendations for People leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of People project, program, or operations management experience, including at least 3 years driving multi-stakeholder, cross-functional programs end to end, ideally at a scaling or global company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building from scratch: you&#39;ve created processes, playbooks, or program infrastructure where none existed before, not just improved what was already in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication: you can produce an executive update, a stakeholder decision memo, and a practitioner playbook with equal fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management across senior cross-functional partners: you drive results with a balance of urgency and thoughtfulness, and know when to push, when to align, and when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI expertise: you default to AI tools for synthesis, drafting, analysis, and communications, and you proactively design workflows that help the team move faster and operate at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical fluency: you can work with data to build a credible narrative, identify patterns across a program portfolio, and make recommendations grounded in evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A users-first mindset: you obsess over the Stripe employee experience and the operator experience, not just the project/program artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with change management frameworks (such as Prosci ADKAR) and judgment about when to apply structured change management vs. lighter-touch approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying enablement materials or training resources for cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Total Rewards, People Operations, or an adjacent HR domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PM and collaboration tools (Asana, Jira, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Total Rewards or HR systems (such as Workday, equity administration platforms, or benefits administration tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, Lean/Six Sigma, or comparable structured-program training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Value Consulting and Proposals team supports long-term growth and value creation for Stripe’s largest and most strategic users. We translate Stripe&#39;s technical capabilities into measurable business outcomes and create value-led proposals that help secure and expand relationships with leading organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Proposal Lead, you’ll manage requests for proposals and requests for information (RFPs and RFIs) for Stripe’s largest pursuits. You’ll develop proposal strategy and narratives, coordinate contributors across Stripe, and deliver high-quality submissions that address customer requirements. You’ll also improve the processes, templates, and tools that help Stripe manage proposals consistently and at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring structure to complex pursuits, build trusted relationships, and communicate clearly with contributors and leaders. This role is a good fit for someone who can balance strategic thinking with detailed execution while managing multiple deadlines and priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end bid management process, including reviewing bid invitations, supporting bid or no-bid analysis, defining the response strategy, and establishing timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customers’ business and technical requirements into clear, persuasive proposals that communicate Stripe’s value and competitive advantages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop proposal content, including executive summaries, value propositions, and recommendations related to pricing and commercial structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate contributors across sales, solutions architecture, legal, privacy, security, and other functions to produce complete and accurate responses to bid components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proposal reviews, resolve blockers, and keep contributors aligned to deliver high-quality submissions within required timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop proposals that connect customer requirements with Stripe’s long-term goals, products, and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve proposal processes, templates, tools, and performance reporting, using win and loss data to identify opportunities for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in bid management, deal management, procurement, pricing strategy, financial consulting, legal services, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, large-scale bids from initial evaluation through submission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proposal writing and project management skills, with a clear understanding of the bid and deal lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating cross-functional contributors and communicating effectively with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with payments or software-as-a-service (SaaS) products and improving processes in an ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with bid management software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of pricing and commercial strategies used in proposal development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating the value of complex payments products and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Management Professional (PgMP) or Project Management Professional (PMP) certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building economic infrastructure for the internet. We help organizations of every size move money, manage revenue, and build global financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Public Sector team builds Stripe’s presence in markets where organizations deliver essential services to millions of people. In the UK, public sector organizations collect taxes and tuition, enable transit, distribute funds, support charitable giving, and modernize citizen services. The team helps these organizations improve how they collect, manage, and disburse funds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the UK Public Sector Lead, you will build and lead Stripe’s public sector go-to-market motion in the UK. You will define how Stripe serves central government, local government, devolved administrations, public bodies, higher education, utilities, transport, charities and not-for-profit organizations, and adjacent regulated organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine market knowledge, commercial judgment, and operational leadership to build trusted relationships, win meaningful business, and establish the operating model needed to serve public sector customers. This role reports to the Global Head of Public Sector and will help launch Stripe’s UK public sector motion in 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Stripe’s UK public sector strategy, including priority segments, customer problems,&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; routes to market, commercial opportunities, and the capabilities needed to succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across government, public bodies, procurement ecosystems, industry associations, systems integrators, and advisory partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior customer decision-makers to understand their payment, revenue, digital service, and financial infrastructure needs, and develop solutions with Stripe teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide strategic opportunities through public sector procurement, contracting, security, compliance, and stakeholder alignment requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Compliance, Risk, Go-to-Market, Alliances and Channels, Product, Engineering, Finance, and Operations to prepare Stripe to support public sector customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring market requirements into priorities for onboarding, risk, contracting, procurement, implementation, support, and product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the positioning, account strategy, partner ecosystem, sales plays, internal processes, and success metrics that support growth in the UK and inform Stripe’s global public sector strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in or selling to the UK public sector, including government, public bodies, education, transport, utilities, charities and not-for-profit organizations, or other regulated institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established senior relationships across the UK public sector, its partner ecosystem, and relevant procurement or policy communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering complex outcomes across multiple stakeholders and working through public sector procurement, contracting, compliance, risk, and implementation requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading senior cross-functional stakeholders across Legal, Compliance, Risk, Product, Sales, Partnerships, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, strategic judgment, and experience working directly on market-building initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching a product, organization, market, vertical, or strategic go-to-market motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial services, enterprise software, digital transformation, or platform technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with UK public procurement frameworks and common contracting vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with systems integrators, consulting firms, implementation partners, or public sector technology ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning customer and regulatory requirements into scalable products, processes, or commercial models&lt;/li&gt;
