&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our EMEA Marketing team is a dynamic, fast-growing group that loves turning customers into enthusiastic Stripe advocates. We work hand-in-hand with our Sales team to build demand, help users get the most out of our products, and craft marketing plans that truly resonate with local audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the DACH region, our team partners with some of the most ambitious innovators across Germany, Austria, and Switzerland—brands like DeepL, refurbed, N26, and Nestlé. We help them use Stripe’s financial infrastructure to unlock new revenue, navigate local complexities, and scale globally. What we learn from these relationships directly influences how Stripe builds its products. The opportunity in this region is massive. We’re tackling it as a diverse, international team that thrives on collaboration, bold innovation, and genuine curiosity. If you love to learn and want to make a meaningful impact, we&#39;d love to have you join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead marketing strategy and plan execution for the DACH region and serve as the primary Marketing partner on the DACH Leadership Team. You’ll set the regional strategy and investment plan, with Germany as the main market, and shape priorities across Austria and Switzerland. You’ll be accountable for demand, pipeline, customer advocacy, and Stripe’s long-term market position in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor, you will align regional and global cross-functional teams around shared priorities, secure the necessary resources, and navigate trade-offs between global strategies and local market needs. You will directly lead high-priority initiatives across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leveraging deep market and account insights, you will identify key growth opportunities across target industries and audiences. In close partnership with Sales, you will build tailored programs for strategic accounts and high-potential prospects aligned with their business models, technical environments, and commercial objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the integrated DACH marketing strategy, turning business goals, market dynamics, and competitive context into clear priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with DACH GTM leadership, Sales, Sales Development, and Partnerships to set shared priorities, join business and pipeline reviews, and focus investment on the highest-value opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and oversee a full-funnel DACH marketing plan across brand, demand generation, account-based marketing, pipeline acceleration, executive engagement, and customer advocacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop industry and account programs for strategic customers and high-potential prospects, helping Sales engage the right stakeholders with relevant messages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring together EMEA and global teams, including Demand Generation and Product Marketing, to deliver the DACH plan, working with Sales, Product, Solutions Engineering, Partnerships, and Communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Stripe’s brand and local presence in DACH through regional customer stories, partner programs, and executive, industry, and ecosystem engagement, including activation around Stripe flagship and third-party events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own metrics across demand, pipeline, opportunity progression, priority-account engagement, and return on investment. Use results to improve programs and stop or change those that aren’t delivering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent DACH across EMEA and global marketing teams, bringing market insight into planning and sharing successful programs across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an experienced B2B marketer who has owned a country, regional, or similarly broad marketing strategy. You can set direction, make investment trade-offs, and work credibly with senior Sales and GTM leaders. You stay close enough to execution to turn the strategy into commercial results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you meet them, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, including ownership of planning and investment for a country, region, or comparably broad portfolio in enterprise technology or another complex B2B environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the German and wider DACH business and technology markets, including enterprise buying dynamics and local ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of partnering with senior Sales and GTM leaders and aligning cross-functional teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading integrated programs across several marketing disciplines, drawing on regional and global specialist teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of annual budgets and multi-program portfolios, with evidence of using commercial results to prioritize investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German and English, with the ability to explain technical concepts and present complex strategies to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and comfort making decisions when priorities compete or information is incomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, commerce, B2B cloud services, or another complex and highly competitive technology category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging enterprise executives and buying groups across Finance, Treasury, Technology, Product, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building local brand relevance, thought leadership, customer advocacy, or influence strategies—not only demand-generation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a marketing approach where the playbook, resources, or route to impact was still taking shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe provides regulated payments and financial services products, and also has a number of regulated subsidiaries, including in the United States (Money Transmitter and lending licenses). These licenses have programs of periodic and ad hoc regulatory reporting stemming from license requirements, and are critical aspects of the supervisory mechanisms for these entities. The Global Regulatory Reporting team leads the process by which we report regulatory data externally to regulators in support of our payments licenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll support the Global Regulatory Reporting team by partnering with Legal, Compliance, Accounting, Business and Product, and Data Analytics teams across Stripe to maintain the Stripe North American regulatory reporting program. This includes understanding and documenting the applicable regulatory reporting requirements in the region, implementing systems and processes for comprehensively tracking those requirements for each of the Stripe North American entities, maintaining the end-to-end processes for the collation of data, production of reports, and continuously monitoring compliance to meet the expectations of regulators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is both a technology company and a financial services company, and you&#39;ll need to be comfortable straddling both of those worlds every day. You&#39;ll enjoy dealing with that puzzle, seeking creative solutions and moving quickly, often in the face of ambiguity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end U.S. regulatory reporting program for digital assets including stablecoin-related financial activities, including defining reporting scope, governance, timelines, and accountability across required regulatory filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret U.S. regulatory reporting requirements applicable to stablecoins, digital assets, payments, and custody, and translate them into clear reporting specifications, data definitions, and execution plans in partnership with Legal and Compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full regulatory reporting lifecycle, from data sourcing and aggregation through validation, internal review, sign-off, and timely submission to regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory reports accurately reflect stablecoin-specific activities and risks, including issuance, redemption, circulation, reserves, custody arrangements, and transaction flows across on-chain and off-chain systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain a robust regulatory reporting control framework, including data quality checks, reconciliations, documentation, and issue remediation to support audit and exam readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Data, Finance, Compliance, and Legal to improve data lineage, transparency, and automation across regulatory reporting processes as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regulatory reporting change management, including assessing the impact of new or evolving stablecoin regulations, product launches, and system changes on reporting scope, data requirements, and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain regulator-ready documentation, including reporting methodologies, assumptions, data lineage, and process documentation to support supervisory reviews and examinations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for regulatory reporting matters during U.S. regulatory exams, audits, and regulatory inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field; equivalent practical experience in financial services regulatory reporting will be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience leading the delivery of an ongoing regulatory reporting program within a regulated financial services environment, ideally supporting stablecoin issuance, payments, or custody-related activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of U.S. compliance and regulatory obligations applicable to stablecoins, including evolving federal and state frameworks (including, but not limited to, the GENIUS Act and related Treasury, banking, and payments guidance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent working knowledge of the U.S. payment stablecoin regulatory landscape, with experience engaging directly with U.S. federal regulators (e.g., OCC, Treasury) and state regulators on regulatory reporting, data submissions, or supervisory requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work across complex data environments, including navigating on-chain and off-chain data sources, internal ledgers, and third-party systems to produce accurate, cohesive, and regulator-ready reporting deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading, analyzing, and compiling financial statements, reserve-related data, transaction-level reporting, and other financial regulatory reports relevant to stablecoin and payments activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in financial services with direct exposure to stablecoins, digital assets, payments, e-money, or other money services business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success executing complex, cross-functional programs in fast-growing organizations, with an emphasis on building scalable, repeatable regulatory reporting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and judgment, with the ability to quickly understand novel or ambiguous regulatory and data challenges and drive balanced, risk-aware solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently and efficiently in a fast-paced, high-volume, and evolving regulatory environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate effectively across Compliance, Legal, Finance, Engineering, Data, Product, and Accounting teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong “culture of compliance” mindset, with the ability to translate regulatory expectations into practical, business-aligned execution without impeding responsible growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with stablecoins, digital assets, payments, or fintech platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory reporting for banks, trust companies, payment institutions, or money services businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on Call Reports FFIEC041 and FFIEC031&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting regulatory exams, audits, or supervisory reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to reporting automation, data pipelines, or reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe has a growing focus on our Renewals business and opportunity to drive growth. Our team provides strategic &amp;amp; operational partnership to those specialized sellers, cross-functional product partners, and leadership. Partnership is provided across three pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy and planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Operations organization, our team, the renewals team of our GTM Post Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations is focused on driving business changes across business operations, insights, process, and tooling. We facilitate incremental Stripe productivity improvements to help our specialized sellers deliver key revenue results for their remit and drive Stripe Revenue. &amp;nbsp;We are a global team with resources in the Americas, Europe and Asia Pacific.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is still very nascent, with the majority of our near term focus on building business foundations, which necessarily entails a focus on operational projects (process design, business cadences, systems work). This analyst is a critical person to the foundations and scale of the Renewals business. Their role includes: measuring and providing insights on performance, forecasting, and process improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set annual and quarterly SOKRs and track performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build actionable reports and insights for leadership reporting forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for QBRs and other leadership meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Examine operational or financial data to uncover trends and guide decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System and operational workflow management analysis and investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve business processes through data driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of operations experience in a software solutions or technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years working with a GTM or Sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong comfort with LLM and AI tooling (e.g. Cursor, Claude Code or Open AI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Analytics (Google Sheets/Excel data manipulation, SQL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business and operational SLA reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly, proactively, and concisely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and comfortable dealing with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tableau or SFDC report development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a User and Report developer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Renewals Team is a strategic partner to Stripe&#39;s Sales organization, helping Stripe retain and expand revenue from its portfolio of existing users. We bring analytical rigor, commercial judgment, and operational discipline to the renewal process so account teams can navigate complex decisions with clarity, accuracy, and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work closely with Sales, Deal Pricing, Deal Strategy, Customer Success and other cross-functional partners throughout the renewal lifecycle. The team analyzes account performance and contractual history, builds renewal scenarios, and develops recommendations that inform deal strategy and negotiation planning led by Account Executives. We also improve the systems and processes that enable Stripe to manage renewals at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Renewals Specialist, you will partner with account teams and cross-functional stakeholders to protect and grow Stripe&#39;s revenue. This is an analytical role at its core. You will combine quantitative analysis and financial modeling with user context to assess renewal options, identify risks and opportunities, and help teams make well-supported commercial decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on large, complex renewals, balancing the needs of Stripe and our users while helping account teams move deals forward on schedule. Success requires strong judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to build trusted relationships across teams. You should be comfortable operating in ambiguity, respectfully challenging assumptions, and engaging in constructive debate to reach better outcomes. You will also help design scalable processes so the team can handle fluctuating volumes while maintaining a high standard of operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives to develop and execute strategies for retaining and expanding revenue from existing users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a portfolio of upcoming renewals, tracking milestones, risks, dependencies, and stakeholder actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze historical pricing, product usage, account performance, and contractual terms to develop renewal recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial models and renewal scenarios that clarify commercial tradeoffs and support data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
