&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supportability Decisions is a Dublin-based engineering team within Supportability Engineering, part of Risk Engineering. We own the “how a business sells” side of Supportability: determining whether a user’s declared business, web presence, account configuration, and observed transaction behaviour align with Stripe’s standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our core domain includes transaction-laundering detection and decisioning, web-presence and URL-policy controls, and low-quality e-commerce detection. We consume the signals and evaluations that support decisions in these spaces and convert them into evidence-based and auditable determinations that can be shared with the rest of the Supportability platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pitch is: join a high-ownership team solving some of Stripe’s hardest risk problems. We build technology that helps Stripe distinguish legitimate businesses from bad actors at scale, combining sophisticated engineering, AI-assisted investigation, and meaningful real-world impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a meaningful part of a risk-decisioning problem from investigation and design through implementation, rollout, measurement, and iteration. You will help build both the domain capabilities and the modern agentic infrastructure required to make Supportability decisions consistent, stateful, explainable, and appropriate to the business, product, and moment in time. Depending on team priorities and the candidate’s experience, this may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building the Supportability Decision Layer: a durable service and API through which automated systems, agents, and human reviewers can request, produce, retrieve, and understand canonical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing the infrastructure that enables agentic investigations to synthesize policy, business identity and history, product context, risk appetite, and multiple assessment signals into explainable, confidence-calibrated decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the transaction-laundering agent’s policy grounding, evidence quality, risk tiering, precision and recall, and use of behavioural, dispute, and other relevant signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing durable decision state and history, including traceability from supporting evidence through reasoning and applied consequence, and validity and refresh policies that prevent stale outcomes from persisting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building governed, reusable configuration and integration patterns that adapt decision capabilities across products, partners, countries, and permitted risk appetites without creating bespoke systems for each use case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building reliable backend workflows on shared Supportability and Risk Platform infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making complex risk decisions explainable to reviewers and affected users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using data and feedback from outcomes, appeals, and corrections to improve decision quality while balancing the identification of bad actors against avoiding unnecessary harm to legitimate businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernising URL enforcement, including when and how URL checks run, reducing unnecessary review volume and user friction, and supporting migration away from legacy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding shared SAE/SPO decisioning foundations, including due-diligence support and product-scoped remediation and appeal capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the Process Orchestration Framework and moving workflow code into more maintainable platform packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to future work in automated LPM URL screening, low-quality e-commerce detection, wider web intelligence, and active test charges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 - 7 years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work effectively across the stack from top to bottom, comfortably navigating codebases with different languages and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re equally comfortable shipping user-facing experiences as you are writing custom queries to analyze experiment results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language (we understand new languages can be learned on the job, so our interview process is language-agnostic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, with the ability to work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy and responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a generalist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth teams similar to Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building financial systems or tools for financial experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you would join Stripe&#39;s Vulnerability Management team, whose mission is to &quot;Surface vulnerabilities at scale across Stripe.&quot; Our vision is to create a culture of continuous excellence in managing vulnerabilities. We want to enhance customer trust by giving users context about threats and vulnerabilities affecting Stripe&#39;s systems. We aim to be a key partner in Stripe&#39;s risk management by providing visibility into vulnerabilities across Stripe&#39;s products and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer focused on Vulnerability Management at Stripe, you will use your software engineering expertise to find and prioritize vulnerabilities in our systems. Working closely with engineers across the company, you will drive the timely remediation of discovered vulnerabilities, playing a key role in Stripe&#39;s overall security and risk strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, you will continuously improve Stripe&#39;s security defenses by enhancing our vulnerability management processes and selecting effective scanning tools to uncover weaknesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your core responsibilities as a Vulnerability Management Software Engineer will involve building data- and agent-backed systems to surface vulnerabilities across Stripe. In addition, you will coordinate fixes to prevent exploits that could impact Stripe or our users and serve as an advisor on security risks. All of this requires collaborating cross-functionally to advocate for practices that strengthen the safety of Stripe&#39;s systems and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify vulnerabilities using automated tools and triage them appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other teams to drive remediation of vulnerabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our overall security and risk management strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve our security posture, processes, and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering experience within the security domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, strong communication skills and a deep respect for the power of collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards for code quality and a constructive attitude to help others raise the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automated vulnerability identification tools and triage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery of successful projects using agents to automate human review processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you will have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach, securely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps Stripe users extend their online presence into the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has done for online payments. With Terminal, businesses can unlock in-person payments use cases that are right for their business model, whether it’s creating a flagship retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling a mobile point of sale at their next event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp; Software Quality Assurance Engineer to join the Stripe Terminal Device Software Quality Assurance team. In this role, you will own the quality assurance process and results for firmware and device operating system components across our payment terminal devices. You&#39;ll work closely with software development teams to define quality standards, develop test strategies, and drive software quality improvements through technical expertise and process enhancements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own software quality for Terminal device software components, including firmware and the device operating system, and ensure software quality targets are met for customers. Collaborate with developers during software planning, change review, and release meetings to understand new features, specifications, expected behaviors, and the impact and risks of changes. Create spot tests before branch cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand customer use cases, Product Requirements Documents, and Software Design Documents. Work with developers to create test plans that improve coverage across configurations, user scenarios, and reliability testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Bluetooth validation across multiple devices, edge cases, and recovery scenarios. Validate devices with enterprise network configurations and security types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute testing for power performance, battery behavior, sleep and wake reliability, and resilience under extended or degraded operating conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain lab setups and test environments that reflect production-like usage conditions and support repeatable validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-lead software quality incident remediation with engineering teams, including root cause analysis and solution development. Establish and maintain software quality assurance processes, and influence cross-functional teams at Stripe and drive quality and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and optimize test cases. Collaborate with automation engineers to expand automated test coverage, guide manual software quality assurance team members in high-quality software testing, and mentor junior software quality engineers on technical skills, test design, work quality, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, software engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of software quality assurance experience for embedded systems or firmware, including analyzing software changes and assessing their impact on test coverage by reviewing release notes and software design documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing test strategies, test plans, and test cases based on product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify the root causes of software defects and proactively identify and mitigate risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, communication, ownership, and influencing skills to drive quality improvements across teams, along with excellent verbal and written English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment terminal devices, EMV certification, or Payment Card Industry compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of embedded systems, real-time operating systems, and firmware development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment processing systems or financial technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of mentoring junior team members on technical skills and test design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s SMB Solutions Architecture (SA) team works with technical and business leaders (CTO/ CIO/ CEO/ Founders etc.), payments leaders and product engineering teams in the mid-market segment to evangelize Stripe’s solutions in the market. A solutions architect’s role is to build relationships with decision makers and think strategically about the business needs of Stripe’s customers. Solution Architects identify and propose Stripe solutions to solve complex business challenges and drive growth for our customers. SAs establish and prescribe best practices around a customer’s strategy, provide business and technical thought leadership and are viewed as a trusted advisor. They work on scaling business processes aligned to maximizing account coverage while working closely with customer and partner resources to deliver a solution that can be adopted quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, the Solutions Architect will build highly consultative trusted relationships with c-level executives and technical decision makers in the customer’s organization to provide business and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges. She/he will architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth for both the user and Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive thought leadership and build executive relationships with key business and technical stakeholders including CIO, CTO, COO, CRO, CDO &amp;amp; Head of Payments. Strive to become their trusted advisor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work to deeply understand the customer’s business objectives and apply Stripe’s payments, SaaS, Banking-as-a-Service and Link Network solutions to customer challenges&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure the technical win for Stripe’s products by delivering demos, responding to RFPs, evangelizing Stripe’s products, and collaborating internally on narratives that align with the customer’s goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emphasis on creating scalable processes (1:M customer engagements, Webinars, office hours etc), partnerships (with external and internal partners) and scaled assets (reusable videos/ templates, playbooks) in order to act as a force-multiplier in the sales process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand Stripe’s footprint within existing accounts to new global markets and business units by introducing new capabilities and local payment methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with multiple internal stakeholders including go-to-market, product and marketing to deliver impactful EBC briefings for SMB accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer to inform our product team on insights, trends, and opportunities across our SMB accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with professional services and partners to accelerate activations and time to live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with partners to help Stripe scale and reach its Total Addressable Market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 25% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way with users and collaborate internally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An ideal candidate should have experience working for medium to large software companies (preferably in In payment-tech), focused on identifying business priorities, technology strategy, and solution design.&amp;nbsp;They will have demonstrated the ability to become a trusted advisor to senior executives and facilitate customer success including business value identification(discovery/ demo cycles), road mapping, as well as advising and defining successful execution strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates have external customer-facing experience, have payment expertise (preferred but not required) who can present and architect Stripe’s solutions, and persuade decision makers to leverage Stripe technology to drive business value. Candidates have previous experience in web architecture, enterprise architecture or experience defining and optimizing financial business processes.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role (e.g. solutions architect, sales engineer, customer success, professional services delivery) for a fin-tech/payment-tech / global software enterprise or 3+ years of total relevant experience (software development, enterprise sales/ architecture, business development etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presenting and architecting solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding or background in writing code in at least 2 of Stripe’s primary deployment languages (Ruby, Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding oral and written communication skills, presentation skills, and comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able and willing to learn Stripe solutions (Payments, Billing, Connect, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability&amp;nbsp; to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact with each other (ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax, Legacy)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational/time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills to work seamlessly with the broader GTM team to support our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving open ended business problems with a combination of technology and creative thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel per business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI Solutions Architecture team is a group of specialists with a deep understanding of Stripe&#39;s products that partners with AI users to realize their full potential through the adoption of prescriptive solutions that drive their growth and success. SAs on this team leverage their expertise in the broader subscription, billing, and payments industry to influence revenue growth across Stripe’s product portfolio, and collaborate with sales, support, product management, and Stripe’s executive team to provide the best experience to our most valued customers.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an AI Solutions Architect, you&#39;ll be a key technical advisor driving the adoption of Stripe&#39;s product solutions among top AI companies. You&#39;ll collaborate with cross-functional teams to craft successful solution plans and shape our product roadmap to meet the unique needs of AI businesses. Your role will involve developing and advising on innovative billing strategies, engaging with AI founders and technical stakeholders, and positioning Stripe as the go-to monetization partner in the AI ecosystem. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to influence the future of AI commerce, tackling complex challenges at a global scale in a dynamic, collaborative environment. Your work will be instrumental in establishing Stripe as the leader in AI monetization infrastructure, driving innovation in the rapidly evolving AI industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Specific Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Become the go-to expert on global payments and monetization strategies for AI companies, including real-time metering for APIs, agents, and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Solution Development&lt;/strong&gt;: Architect innovative solutions that address the unique needs of AI businesses, often working with experimental products and evolving pricing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Influence&lt;/strong&gt;: Work closely with Stripe product and engineering teams to rapidly close key product gaps and shape the roadmap based on AI company needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;: Collaborate with AEs to engage deeply with AI founders and technical stakeholders, positioning Stripe as a strategic partner in their monetization journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thought Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: Contribute to shifting Stripe&#39;s brand perception among AI founders and builders through technical demonstrations, hackathons, and meetups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implementation Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Work directly with Professional Services, Partners and Product teams to ensure successful implementation and activation of core payments, Stripe Billing and usage-based billing for AI clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;: Stay informed about alternative solutions in the market and develop strategies to position Stripe&#39;s offerings effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: Act as a bridge between sales, product, engineering, and marketing teams, ensuring alignment on AI-specific billing strategies and customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a passionate, adaptable professional who thrives on innovation and isn&#39;t afraid to challenge the status quo. The ideal candidate combines deep technical expertise in billing systems with a strong understanding of AI business models and monetization strategies. You should be comfortable engaging with technical founders, articulating complex concepts to diverse audiences, and staying at the forefront of AI industry trends. You&#39;re a quick learner who thrives in rapidly changing environments and can adapt strategies as the AI landscape evolves. If you&#39;re excited about shaping the future of AI monetization and have a track record of success in technical sales or pre-sales roles, we encourage you to apply, even if your experience doesn&#39;t exactly match our requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in technical sales or pre-sales roles, focusing on solution architecture and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in pre-sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical acumen in API integrations, real-time data processing, and cloud-based architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage with technical founders and engineers at an API level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills to articulate complex technical concepts to diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments/ billing / invoicing / issuing / banking / Fintech space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for staying at the forefront of AI industry trends and monetization strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25% of the time to engage with key AI accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AI companies or deep understanding of AI business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in usage-based billing models and their application in AI products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of solving complex, ambiguous problems in the billing or AI space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers a unique opportunity to shape the future of AI monetization at one of the world&#39;s leading fintech companies. Join us in defining how the next generation of AI businesses will scale and succeed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach. Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Architecture Team partners with our users to realize their full potential through the adoption of prescriptive solutions that drive their growth and success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work with founders, C-level executives, finance leaders, product design and engineering teams at large global brands and platforms who are building financial services solutions with Stripe.&amp;nbsp; We work closely with Account Executives, Professional Services, Customer Success Managers, Partners, Technical Account Managers Product, and Engineering teams to develop and execute on the account strategy for Stripe in market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to uncover the deepest levels of customer pain and desired outcomes, going beyond surface-level requirements. By truly understanding their strategic business objectives, you will architect and tailor Stripe&#39;s solutions as the definitive answer to their most pressing challenges. You will be instrumental in mapping the customer&#39;s transformation journey, crafting future-state roadmaps and solution architectures that inherently factor in complex third-party integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute meticulous technical discovery, conducting in-depth business analysis and background research on customer operations, industry dynamics, and competitive landscapes to build a foundational understanding that informs every proposed solution. This goes beyond fact-finding; it&#39;s about understanding their &quot;why.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic engagements, guiding APAC and China users through a structured discovery process to align with their core business priorities. You will design compelling, technically sound solutions and master the &quot;technical win&quot; by evangelizing these proposals through executive briefings, comprehensive readouts, tailored presentations, and impactful solution demonstrations that resonate with the customer&#39;s specific challenges and desired future state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and articulate expansion opportunities, strategically extending Stripe’s footprint within existing accounts into new global markets and business units. This involves introducing new capabilities and local payment methods, always with a clear focus on the technical feasibility and the value delivered at each touchpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; within Stripe&#39;s product and engineering teams, meticulously capturing insights, emerging trends, and new opportunities from the field. You will champion these requirements, ensuring they are accurately prioritized and inform future product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the critical technical counterpoint to the sales executive, providing invaluable technical insight and designing robust solutions for both prospective and existing platform users. You will be the expert guide on Stripe&#39;s technical merits and strategic benefits for both platforms and their end-user base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft and deliver compelling technical demonstrations that don&#39;t just show features, but powerfully showcase how Stripe&#39;s platform solves specific business problems, highlighting the unique value proposition, key differentiators, and potential for customization. Crucially, you will illustrate how these benefits cascade directly to the customer&#39;s own user base, driving their success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role such as sales engineer, pre-sale solution consultant or solutions architect for a global software enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills in English and Mandarin as the positions is primarily working with enterprise Chinese merchants based in China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer meetings to gain strategic footing and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle and API architectures. A background in writing code in any of Stripe’s primary deployment languages (Ruby, Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, etc.) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills, presentation skills, and confident in explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion to take on ownership and drive change in a constantly evolving environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel per business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments/ billing / invoicing / issuing / banking / Fintech space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a growth stage internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Commercial Solutions Architecture (SA) team works with technical and business leaders (CTO/ CIO/ CEO/ Founders etc.), payments leaders and product engineering teams in the mid-market segment to evangelize Stripe’s solutions in the market. A solutions architect’s role is to build relationships with decision makers and think strategically about the business needs of Stripe’s customers. Solution Architects identify and propose Stripe solutions to solve complex business challenges and drive growth for our customers. Commercial SAs establish and prescribe best practices around a customer’s strategy, provide business and technical thought leadership and are viewed as a trusted advisor. They work on scaling business processes aligned to maximizing account coverage while working closely with customer and partner resources to deliver a solution that can be adopted quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, the Solutions Architect will build highly consultative trusted relationships with c-level executives and technical decision makers in the customer’s organization to provide business and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges. She/he will architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth for both the user and Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive thought leadership and build executive relationships with key business and technical stakeholders including CIO, CTO, COO, CRO, CDO &amp;amp; Head of Payments. Strive to become their trusted advisor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work to deeply understand the customer’s business objectives and apply Stripe’s payments, SaaS, Banking-as-a-Service and Link Network solutions to customer challenges&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure the technical win for Stripe’s products by delivering demos, responding to RFPs, evangelizing Stripe’s products, and collaborating internally on narratives that align with the customer’s goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with multiple internal stakeholders including go-to-market, product and marketing to deliver impactful EBC briefings for Mid Market accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with professional services and partners to accelerate activations and time to live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with partners to help Stripe scale and reach its Total Addressable Market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 25% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way with users and collaborate internally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An ideal candidate should have experience working for mid-market / enterprise-class software companies (preferably in In payment-tech), focused on identifying business priorities, technology strategy, and solution design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They will have demonstrated the ability to become a trusted advisor to senior executives and facilitate customer success including business value identification(discovery/ demo cycles), road mapping, as well as advising and defining successful execution strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates have external customer-facing experience, have payment expertise (preferred but not required) who can present and architect Stripe’s solutions, and persuade decision makers to leverage Stripe technology to drive business value.&amp;nbsp; Candidates have previous experience in web architecture, enterprise architecture or experience defining and optimizing financial business processes.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role (e.g. solutions architect, sales engineer, customer success, professional services delivery) for a fin-tech/payment-tech / global software enterprise with 7+ years of total relevant experience (software development, enterprise sales/ architecture, business development etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a customer facing roles - presenting and architecting solutions. Domain experience in the payments space is preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding or background in writing code in at least 2 of Stripe’s primary deployment languages (Ruby, Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding oral and written communication skills, presentation skills, and comfortable explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability&amp;nbsp; to understand how a wide variety of technologies and systems interact with each other (ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax, Legacy)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational/time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills to work seamlessly with the broader GTM team to support our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving open ended business problems with a combination of technology and creative thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel per business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

