&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The API Platform team is responsible for empowering teams to build highly reliable and performant services, backing our payment systems, fraud detection, and a multitude of other products. As an infrastructure team, you will build and expand the service frameworks to make complex systems easy to use, resilient, and scalable. We build powerful interfaces for engineers that depend on these systems—deployment, load balancers, web framework, databases, Kafka, and Kubernetes—while keeping them highly available and performant. We&#39;re looking for engineering leaders who drive the technical vision of Stripe&#39;s service infrastructure platform for thousands of engineers to use and build on top of, and thrive in a highly autonomous environment with many moving pieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join as a Technical Lead for one of the most impactful teams at Stripe. You will lead a team of engineers, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering orgs, and advance service-oriented architecture (SOA) adoption at Stripe. By collaborating with the team&#39;s technical leaders, you will ensure the software your team builds meets the needs of Stripe and its customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a highly effective team that consistently delivers high-impact results while genuinely caring for one another. We expect you to bring your curiosity and critical thinking skills to this challenging domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for individuals with a strong background in designing and delivering high-performance infrastructure products for both internal and external customers. We would love to hear from you whether you have spent your entire career in infrastructure or are looking to apply your skill set to the database engineering domain for the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers to create roadmaps that deliver milestones toward a cohesive engineering vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high-quality solutions that meet user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support the Infrastructure&#39;s key engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture and design, vision, direction, and requirements setting, and incident response processes) for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to create and drive toward the longer term vision of Stripe&#39;s services roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g., building internal or external developer products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building infrastructure and products for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adjust conversations from high-level discussions to detailed coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, critical thinking, determination, and a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of people, genuinely caring for each other and contributing to a high level of psychological safety for all team members and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one of the programming languages (Java, Ruby, Python, Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building serverless platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect deep expertise in every dimension above, but genuine curiosity about any of the areas that are less familiar is important to us&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be joining the High Availability and Disaster Recovery team. At Stripe, availability is a core feature of our products. This team designs and builds new solutions to allow latency-critical, stateful applications to survive any type of disaster. We build distributed systems on top of unreliable architecture to provide highly available and resilient customer solutions. This team is creating greenfield solutions which will serve as the basis for Stripe’s architecture 5, 10, or 20 years into the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a distributed team with many remote engineers. You are encouraged to apply if you meet the minimum requirements and are able to work from anywhere in the United States or Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help develop our global architecture by combining less-available components and data centers into a highly available and resilient whole. You will work on latency-critical solutions where every millisecond matters and data redundancy is a hard requirement. You will learn quickly and work on a broad range of problems - one day may be investigating Mongo write concerns, the next may be minimizing cross-region TLS handshakes, followed by developing new systems to automate disaster detection and failovers. Your work will enable Stripe to increase the GDP of the internet by providing uptime and data protection which have historically been impossible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively work with leaders and engineers across the company to understand and identify opportunities to improve Stripe’s reliability&amp;nbsp; posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, implement, and deploy robust distributed services, making appropriate tradeoffs between reliability, throughput, latency, resiliency, engineering velocity and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate, design and implement new products and prototypes to improve service resiliency, engineering velocity and management at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow the next generation of technical leaders at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering strategy, tooling, processes, and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold our high engineering standards and improve our codebase and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 10 years or more of distributed and cloud native software development experience at a highly-scaled or hyperscaler service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a deep understanding of how to build scalable, resilient, distributed systems, cloud native architectures, and mission critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience influencing, planning, scoping, and leading large projects across many teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a collaborative environment involving diverse stakeholders and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a high level of autonomy and responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial, proactive and self-driven&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong history of being a technical lead and mentor across several engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The IAM Control Plane team’s mission is to empower Stripe users to easily and securely manage their access to Stripe products and data. As part of Stripe&#39;s Organizations and Auth Platform, we own the platform for API keys, user roles, and access auditing, ensuring the right people have the keys to the kingdom - and no one else.&amp;nbsp;We are a team of around 10 engineers with an ambitious roadmap, blending deep platform work with direct product impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, build, and maintain the critical systems that control our user’s access to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build the next generation of IAM primitives to securely power AI-driven agentic experiences on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new user-facing permission models, including custom roles and granular access controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement platform features like Account Groups to simplify access management for large organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and operate mission-critical, highly-available backend services that are fundamental to every Stripe user&#39;s experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the stack to ship end-to-end features, from API design and database modeling to frontend components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering standards, tooling, and processes as well as mentor team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Staff-level role, so we&#39;re targeting 10+ years in software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar for engineering quality and a passion for building resilient, scalable distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, building, and operating backend services in a professional environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to navigate ambiguity and solve complex problems with a product-minded approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a modern backend language such as Go, Ruby, Java, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers at all levels, supporting their professional growth and technical leadership development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product, and design teams to define product strategy and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Identity and Access Management (IAM), authentication, or authorization systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with frontend technologies like React and TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on developer platforms or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/link&quot;&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt; helps Stripe&#39;s merchants deliver frictionless and secure checkout experiences by auto-filling customers&#39; payment information, letting customers check out in seconds and pay in one click across the Link merchant network.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Software Engineer to lead the design and delivery of new money-movement capabilities in Link. You will take ambiguous product opportunities and turn them into reliable, scalable, and intuitive experiences for consumers and merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual-contributor role with broad technical and organizational scope. You will own large, cross-functional projects from early product and technical definition through launch and iteration; lead teams of engineers through complex execution; and partner closely with the many Stripe systems and teams that make money movement possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the stack, building services and APIs as well as the user experiences that expose those capabilities. The work may involve modern financial infrastructure—including stablecoin-enabled capabilities—while requiring sound judgment around safety, reliability, compliance, and user trust. You will make the architectural decisions that let the balance model scale globally, and raise the engineering bar for the team as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical strategy, architecture, and execution for large, ambiguous Link initiatives that create new money-movement primitives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end to end: clarify the problem, define an incremental technical plan, align stakeholders, drive delivery, launch safely, and use results to guide further investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build robust, scalable backend services and high-quality consumer-facing experiences across Java, Ruby, and TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a project team of engineers through execution, creating clarity on priorities, decisions, risks, and delivery milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Risk, Infrastructure, and other Stripe teams to build capabilities that are safe, reliable, and useful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate dependencies across Stripe’s payments and money-movement platforms, making thoughtful tradeoffs between speed, user experience, operational reliability, and durable technical foundations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through technical leadership, design reviews, mentoring, and constructive feedback across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the team’s longer-term roadmap by identifying opportunities, technical risks, and investments needed to scale Link’s financial capabilities globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of backend and/or full-stack software development experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical experience leading the design and delivery of large, complex software projects from early definition through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and unblocking a group of engineers on a substantial project as a senior individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in high-ambiguity environments: framing problems, making durable technical decisions, and creating an actionable path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional and cross-organizational collaboration skills, with the ability to align teams with different systems, priorities, and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering judgment around system reliability, operational excellence, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded approach to engineering, with a focus on delivering meaningful outcomes for users and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Java, Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payments, money-movement, fintech, or other regulated financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer products at scale, particularly products that require a high degree of user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on 0→1 products or taking new capabilities from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with stablecoins, digital assets, or the infrastructure that enables global financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appreciation for the importance of good documentation—internal and external—and taking pride in seeing projects through to successful completion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Money Movement teams are crucial in helping Stripe build platforms and product experiences that enables businesses all over the world to move money. We are currently looking for someone who can drive the technical vision for how Stripe moves money at a global scale. This role spans the stack, from the core financial APIs that all of Stripe’s products are built on, like balances, transfers and payouts, to the financial integrations we rely on to move billions of dollars in countries around the world. The teams also run infrastructure that abstracts payment networks globally to expose capabilities for moving money with a variety of characteristics like speed, currency, and cost. We are responsible for ensuring that money gets to its destination quickly, reliably and in a cost effective manner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These systems are extremely central to our plans for the next 5-10 years and building them well will have an enormous impact on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and lead the technical roadmap for Money Movement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure our infrastructure is safely extensible, scalable, reliable and meets SLAs for both external and internal users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape future proof interfaces that are easy to build against and meet the requirements of product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive sound technical decision making within Money Movement and lead technical conversations with other teams across Payments Infrastructure and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run, design, and code review for key components and ships in Money Movement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pair with the engineer manager to mentor and develop senior engineering talent on the teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You may be a fit for this role if you:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have previously been in Technical Leadership roles driving technical work for a large group of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have solid experience in architecting and designing large-scale and complex systems that delivered critical impact to a well-known business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have rich experience in driving, executing, and delivering high quality technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are skilled in gathering and effectively synthesizing users’ feedback and experience with platforms and product offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are skilled in working across engineering teams and other functions in building alignment, driving decision making, and communicating transparently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are effective in giving and receiving constructive feedback to/from peers and team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable in working in ambiguously defined problem spaces, can identify the most valuable areas to direct your energy, and have delivered tangible results, as demonstrated in prior experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, build, and maintain APIs, services, and large-scale systems that reliably and efficiently handle billions of money movement requests.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and solve critical production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack. Mentor engineers to help them grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the company to build new features at large-scale, while improving internal engineering standards, tooling, and processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a distributed and hybrid team, maintaining open communication and strong connections with colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry software engineering experience, with demonstrated impact at a staff or equivalent scope (leading initiatives across multiple teams or systems).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record designing and shipping large-scale user-facing products with distributed backend systems that are both highly available and financially correct.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional engineering projects end-to-end, from requirements through architecture, delivery, and post-launch iteration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong API design instincts and the ability to build simple, developer-friendly interfaces over inherently complex financial and regulatory requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence technical direction and align multiple teams without direct authority, with excellent written and verbal communication across engineers, product, and leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership mindset, such as comfortable with ambiguity, able to define the problem and the plan, not just execute a predefined spec.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, precise communication on complex technical topics for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating real-time transaction processing systems with strict latency and correctness requirements (authorizations, payments, ledgering, settlement).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with card network protocols, BIN sponsorship models, or issuing bank integrations (Visa, Mastercard, or equivalent).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated financial services such as compliance-aware system design, audit trails, financial controls, or KYC or KYB flows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in embedded finance, card-as-a-service, or Banking-as-a-Service platforms. Experience with high-volume event-driven architectures and the reliability and consistency tradeoffs they introduce.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of mentoring senior engineers and contributing meaningfully to engineering hiring and culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payment Intelligence is comprised of multiple product teams building AI-first solutions to some of our customers’ biggest challenges, including fraud/abuse (&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/au/radar&quot;&gt;Radar&lt;/a&gt;), payment optimizations (&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/authorization-boost&quot;&gt;AuthBoost&lt;/a&gt;), Disputes, Authentication, and merchant analytics. We’re a mix of machine engineering engineers and full-stack software engineers impacting ~every Stripe transaction, creating revenue opportunities for Stripe and our customers, and helping protect the broader ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have the benefit and privilege of working on cutting edge technologies with incredible scale and reach while also working directly with our merchants every day to build the right products for their needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on Payment Intelligence, you’ll work across our product portfolio to ensure we’re building in a consistent, efficient, and effective manner. Experience with large, distributed systems on the critical path will help candidates succeed, as will comfort working across the stack and interacting with ML teams and models.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define technical strategy for multiple experiences across the Payment Intelligence portfolio, with a focus on quality and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a quality-first engineering culture - establish standards, tooling, and processes that make it easy to ship high-quality code at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with some of Stripe’s largest merchants to co-build the future of payment-centric intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with product, design, and ML colleagues to ship the very best software possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the stack - contributing to infrastructure and foundational systems, but also FE, API, and ML-adjacent work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, including 5+ years of experience in a strategic technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on Distributed systems, API design, and user facing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive projects at a high-level while also being hands on and contributing directly to technical solutions as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills and a proven ability to work cross-team, cross-org, and cross-functionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments systems and/or fraud detection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ML systems in production: model serving, training pipelines, observability, and evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with 0-1 product builds: you&#39;ve started with a blank page and ended with a production system, and you have clear opinions about what makes that process go well or poorly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across a range of software languages and frameworks; our stack includes Java, Ruby, Python, TypeScript, Kafka, Flyte, Airflow, and Mongo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating ambiguity in a fast-moving organization - you can make confident technical decisions with incomplete information and update gracefully when new constraints emerge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radar helps businesses prevent payments fraud and abuse while enabling legitimate customers to transact with confidence. We combine machine learning and AI with the intelligence of Stripe’s global network to make sophisticated fraud prevention accessible to businesses of all sizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work spans payments fraud detection, protection against abuse beyond the payment, enterprise APIs that bring Radar’s capabilities into businesses’ own systems and payment flows, and the platform that powers it all. We build everything from reliable, low-latency infrastructure to intuitive tools that help users understand threats and control how they respond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud evolves constantly, and so do we. We work directly with users to understand emerging attacks, turn advances in ML and AI into effective defenses, and build products that protect and grow their revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer on Radar, you’ll build products and infrastructure that help businesses understand and stop fraud and abuse. Your work will span backend services, enterprise APIs, and user experiences that put sophisticated prevention capabilities into our customers’ hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own problems from investigation through launch, partnering with&amp;nbsp; product managers, designers, and data scientists. You’ll have opportunities to scale systems that make real-time decisions across Stripe’s global payments network, bring advances in ML and AI into production, and build new products from scratch. Every improvement can have a direct impact on the revenue our users retain and the legitimate customers they serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate reliable, low-latency services that detect and prevent fraud and abuse at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design APIs and dashboard experiences that help businesses investigate threats, configure defenses, and understand how Radar protects them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the shared platform and infrastructure that enable teams to build and launch new Radar capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with users to understand emerging threats and turn those insights into broadly useful products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ML engineers and data scientists to bring new signals, models, and AI capabilities into production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end to end, from technical design and implementation through rollout, measurement, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold a high bar for engineering quality, reliability, and product craft while moving quickly as threats evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of backend and/or full-stack software development experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language, with experience building and maintaining production software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical experience leading the design and delivery of large, complex software projects from early definition through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and unblocking a group of engineers on a substantial project as a senior individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant hands-on coding as a senior IC leader in the last year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across systems and technologies, learn unfamiliar codebases, and make thoughtful technical trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in high-ambiguity environments: framing problems, making durable technical decisions, and creating an actionable path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional and cross-organizational collaboration skills, with the ability to align teams with different systems, priorities, and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of basic data science concepts, like linear models, precision, recall, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer products at scale, particularly products that require a high degree of user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with fast customers, including leading upsell calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of working closely with data science and ML teams to ship products to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on 0→1 products or taking new capabilities from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Java, Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payments, money-movement, fintech, or other regulated financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer products at scale, particularly products that require a high degree of user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with stablecoins, digital assets, or the infrastructure that enables global financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product and Risk Data Engineering is Stripe&#39;s single source of truth data engineering layer for Payments, Risk, and Product — we enable Stripe to confidently run, measure, and grow the business by making accurate information easy to access. We curate and maintain high-quality data warehouses and pipelines that serve as the authoritative foundation for product and financial activity across Stripe, powering analytics, ML capabilities, agentic workflows, and merchant-facing data interfaces. Beyond building data, we act as the internal experts in data technologies and partner with Data Platform to deliver high-quality, low-friction data processing frameworks. We also serve as the bridge between data producers and data consumers — championing best-in-class data engineering practices and guiding product teams on event-driven data API modeling — so that every team at Stripe can build, decide, and grow from a trusted, well-engineered data foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a person who could contribute to the team by solving high-impact, cutting-edge data problems. The ideal candidate will be someone that has built data pipelines for large scale volume, is deeply knowledgeable of key tools including Airflow/Spark/Kafka/Flink, is empathetic, excels at building strong relationships, and collaborates effectively with other Stripe teams to understand their use cases and unlock new capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the technical outcomes for a team of ambitious, talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver cutting-edge data pipelines that scale to users&#39; needs, focusing on reliability and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong subject matter expertise and manage the SLAs of data pipelines and full stack web applications that support critical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and peers across the company to create/improve canonical datasets and data warehouses, use golden paths, and ensure Stripes and customers are using trustworthy data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI/LLM and Agents at scale to produce and analyze high-quality data on ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the opportunity to drive the execution of key data initiatives for Stripe, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Staff-level role — that typically means 10+ years of experience building and operating data systems, pipelines, warehouses, infrastructure, and leading teams to deliver exceptional solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong engineering background and passion for data as well as prior experience with writing and debugging data pipelines using a distributed data framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inquisitive nature in diving into data inconsistencies to pinpoint issues, and resolve deep rooted data quality issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of a backend development language (such as Scala, Java, or Go) and strong SQL experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extreme customer focus, with a commitment to partnering with product, leaders across the business, and other Stripe engineers to understand their use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective cross-functional collaboration, with the ability to think rigorously, communicate clearly, and make or coordinate difficult decisions and trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive with high autonomy and responsibility in an ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to foster and work in a healthy, inclusive, challenging, and supportive work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack is made up of Iceberg, Kafka, Change Data Capture, Flink, Spark, Airflow, Hive Metastore, Pinot, Trino, and AWS Cloud - experience with all or some of these tools is a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing open-source contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining data marts / warehouses to power business reporting needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Product, Go-To-Market, or Sales / Marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine enjoyment of innovation and a deep interest in understanding how things work, with the ability to question and direct architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for various audiences, including leadership, users, and company-wide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk Engineering builds the systems that protect Stripe from fraud, credit losses, and regulatory risk across user onboarding, compliance, financial crimes, and identity verification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial Crimes Engineering builds the systems and controls that let Stripe safely onboard businesses in emerging and regulated industries while keeping Stripe in compliance with sanctions law, anti-money-laundering rules, and financial partner requirements. We keep known bad actors off Stripe, find new through ongoing detection, and build AI-augmented tooling that helps expert reviewers resolve cases quickly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at scale, screening every user, enforcing jurisdictional restrictions across money movement in real time, and automating signal acquisition and synthesis into investigation workflows. We&#39;re now re-architecting our screening platform to make it safe and easy for new Stripe products to launch with the right financial crimes controls, to express richer policy as code, and to serve as a multi-tenant Risk Platform offering across Stripe&#39;s products and subsidiaries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on Financial Crimes Engineering, you&#39;ll own technical direction across our screening, detection, and review systems. You&#39;ll design infrastructure that balances screening latency with accuracy, build the systems that surface emerging risk and collect information to resolve it, and ensure investigators have the tooling they need. You&#39;ll work across distributed systems and policy logic, partnering with ML, Legal, and Compliance to translate regulation into working software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define technical strategy &amp;amp; vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish the multi-year architecture for Stripe’s real-time entity matching infrastructure, policy enforcement engines, and reviewer tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect high-scale systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and optimize distributed screening engines and detection pipelines handling entity- and transaction-level requests at scale with strict SLA and uptime guarantees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build investigations infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Design the systems that surface suspicious activity, collect additional information from users, route cases to reviewers, and augment human judgment with AI to drive faster, more accurate case resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive cross-functional technical alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical voice with Legal, Compliance, ML, and Product leaders to translate evolving global regulatory requirements into technical ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable Risk as a Service:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the architectural evolution toward a multi-tenant screening platform - laying the technical foundation for both internal product launches and external developer-facing APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Set standards for system design, API consistency, and operational rigor across backend and ML-adjacent systems; mentor senior engineers and lead high-stakes design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Own system reliability, observability, and latency, ensuring production systems adapt quickly to sudden changes in global sanctions lists or traffic spikes, and participate in an on-call rotation for these systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, including 5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role on core infrastructure, distributed systems, or platform engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing, building, and operating high-throughput, low-latency APIs and distributed backend systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of defining technical roadmaps and driving alignment across multiple engineering teams and cross-functional domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical depth - comfortable jumping from high-level system architecture down to code-level performance tuning and production debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of articulating technical decisions to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain experience in financial crimes, sanctions screening, AML (Anti-Money Laundering), entity resolution, or high-stakes trust &amp;amp; safety platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with applying LLMs or ML to operational workflows (e.g., case triage, entity resolution, review automation), or experience with fuzzy string matching and NLP for entity matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building investigator/analyst tooling, case management systems, or human-in-the-loop review workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform products or APIs consumed by both internal engineering teams and external developers (e.g., API backward compatibility, client libraries).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience leading 0-1 platform builds or major architectural modernizations from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech stack experience across multi-language environments (e.g., Primarily Ruby and Java) and modern data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity and making high-judgment engineering calls in a fast-moving regulatory environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role can be either based out of the Toronto office with a hybrid work environment, or remote in Ontario with occasional travel to the Toronto office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Service Infrastructure team is responsible for empowering teams to build highly reliable and performant services, backing our payment systems, fraud detection, and a multitude of other products. As an infrastructure team, you will build and expand the service frameworks to make complex systems easy to use, resilient, and scalable. We build powerful interfaces for engineers that depend on these systems—deployment, load balancers, web framework, databases, Kafka, and Kubernetes—while keeping them highly available and performant. We&#39;re looking for engineering leaders who drive the technical vision of Stripe&#39;s service infrastructure platform for thousands of engineers to use and build on top of, and thrive in a highly autonomous environment with many moving pieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join as a Technical Lead for one of the most impactful teams at Stripe. You will lead a team of engineers, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering orgs, and advance service-oriented architecture (SOA) adoption at Stripe. By collaborating with the team&#39;s technical leaders, you will ensure the software your team builds meets the needs of Stripe and its customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a highly effective team that consistently delivers high-impact results while genuinely caring for one another. We expect you to bring your curiosity and critical thinking skills to this challenging domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for individuals with a strong background in designing and delivering high-performance infrastructure products for both internal and external customers. We would love to hear from you whether you have spent your entire career in infrastructure or are looking to apply your skill set to the database engineering domain for the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers to create roadmaps that deliver milestones toward a cohesive engineering vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high-quality solutions that meet user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support the Infrastructure&#39;s key engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture and design, vision, direction, and requirements setting, and incident response processes) for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to create and drive toward the longer term vision of Stripe&#39;s services roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a strategic technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading engineering team(s) working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g., building internal or external developer products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building infrastructure and products for internal or external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering pragmatic solutions that accelerate business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adjust conversations from high-level discussions to detailed coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive writing and in-person communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, critical thinking, determination, and a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with a diverse group of people, genuinely caring for each other and contributing to a high level of psychological safety for all team members and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in at least one of the programming languages (Java, Ruby, Python, Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building serverless platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on-call rotations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t expect deep expertise in every dimension above, but genuine curiosity about any of the areas that are less familiar is important to us&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup Products team builds Stripe Atlas and other products that help founders start and run a company from anywhere in the world. We believe startups are one of the most effective ways to solve the world’s problems, and we want to give founders a running start—and keep them running.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help founders form companies, raise capital, execute critical legal agreements, access the internet’s best tools, and automate their operations while feeling ambitious, smart, and assured. Our goal is to help more startups reach product-market fit, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team comprises high-agency, high-ownership product thinkers who genuinely care about founders. Everyone is responsible for making our products the best they can be and ensuring our roadmap contains the highest-impact work for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a broad and ambitious roadmap spanning global company formation, legal and financial workflows, AI-enabled operations, and products beyond Atlas. Delivering it requires strong technical leadership to shape future investments, de-risk complex initiatives, and build durable partnerships across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on Startup Products, you will shape the technical strategy for the team while leading major 0→1 products from early exploration through launch and iteration. You will turn ambiguous opportunities into clear technical plans, align teams around those plans, and remain hands-on throughout execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across product surfaces, services, APIs, data models, and integrations with internal and external systems. You will partner closely with Product, Design, Legal, Data, Operations, and engineering teams across Stripe to create experiences that make complex and consequential tasks feel simple and trustworthy for founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive technical strategy across Startup Products, connecting near-term product delivery to a cohesive, durable engineering vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large, ambiguous 0→1 initiatives from problem definition and architecture through implementation, safe launch, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain polished user experiences, reliable backend services, APIs, and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks, dependencies, and foundational investments early, creating incremental plans that de-risk the roadmap and accelerate future work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering teams across Stripe, building alignment and influencing their roadmaps and priorities when Startup Products depends on shared capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with founders to understand their needs and translate complex legal, financial, and operational workflows into intuitive products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the team’s engineering bar through clear standards, strong documentation, mentoring, and constructive technical feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product and engineering leadership on emerging opportunities, technical constraints, and investments needed to support the team’s long-term ambitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience defining and delivering large, ambiguous software initiatives from early product and technical exploration through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create technical direction and align teams with different priorities and constraints without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-minded engineering judgment, with a deep commitment to understanding users and delivering meaningful outcomes for them and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to move between strategic discussions and detailed technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high quality bar and attention to detail across product experience, implementation, reliability, and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with early stage startups and a deep understanding of the challenges founders face all over the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building 0→1 products and taking them from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products involving legal, financial, compliance, or other complex and high-trust workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-powered product experiences or platforms that safely automate consequential user tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collecting and filing sales &amp;amp; indirect taxes is a classic area for technology disruption. Companies selling across countries, states, and even smaller jurisdictions have to navigate through a myriad of tax rates, product-level tax exemptions, filing requirements, and registration obligations. The rules are constantly changing, and not accurately calculating and filing tax can have legal ramifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s no surprise then that solving tax compliance is a top user request. We launched Stripe Tax as a new SaaS product in 2021 to make tax compliance as effortless as possible. The Stripe Tax team builds the systems and experiences that help businesses understand where they have obligations, calculate the right tax, and automate reporting and filing. We solve this at a global scale for users ranging from ambitious startups to the world’s largest enterprises, whose requirements demand exceptional correctness, extensibility, and operational rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced technical leader to shape the architecture and technical roadmap for Stripe Tax. You will work alongside leaders across engineering, product, design, operations, and go-to-market teams to turn complex and evolving tax requirements into simple, reliable experiences for millions of businesses. You will lead high-impact, multi-team efforts, make durable technical decisions, and raise the bar for how we build and operate Stripe Tax.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical strategy and execution for Stripe Tax’s most important and ambiguous product and platform investments, from early exploration through production adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work backwards from the needs of complex global businesses and evolving tax regulations to identify high-leverage opportunities and shape the product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, design, operations, legal, go-to-market, and infrastructure leaders to align teams and deliver cohesive tax experiences across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve scalable, resilient systems and data models that meet the exceptionally high standards for correctness, auditability, security, and availability required in tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive interoperability across Stripe products and external tax ecosystems, scrutinizing service boundaries, interfaces, and data contracts to keep the platform extensible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through hands-on technical leadership, clear decision-making frameworks, operational excellence, and mentorship that accelerates other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry software engineering experience building and operating large-scale, distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep software engineering expertise, with a track record of making sound architectural decisions while remaining hands-on in the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex, multi-team technical programs from ambiguous problem definition through successful delivery and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to set long-term technical direction, identify the highest-leverage investments, and make progress amid uncertainty and competing constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and influence skills, with the ability to build alignment among senior technical, product, and business stakeholders without relying on authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to growing other engineers through mentorship, technical feedback, and a culture of rigorous, inclusive, and data-informed decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in tax, financial technology, payments, accounting, financial reporting, or another domain where correctness and regulatory complexity are central&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with large enterprise customers and translating their complex requirements into durable platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing robust integrations with external systems and APIs, or leading platform work that spans backend services, data, and user-facing experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe startups are the future. We work with many of the newest and most innovative companies to help them grow, and we need your help. We&#39;re looking for someone who knows their way around the early-stage startup ecosystem to represent Stripe and share what we&#39;re working on with a broad base of startups and accelerator partners. Our primary goal is to help early-stage founders succeed, and that comes in a variety of forms - mentorship, helping them set up their financial stack, connecting them with investors and mentors, being their internal advocate, and much more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will oversee a portfolio of strategic early-stage accelerator partnerships, including Y Combinator, as we work to educate, attract and retain the most promising startups. You’re an energetic and organized self-starter; you understand the product well and can cultivate trusted partnerships with the right players in the ecosystem. You’re also able to succinctly communicate Stripe&#39;s mission and benefits to investors and startups. You will be on the front lines for evangelizing our product to prospective users and a key driver of our success with startups. You connect dots, constantly soliciting input from users and using that to improve product and GTM strategy. If you’re excited to spend your days interfacing with startup founders and early-stage investors, and find energy in tirelessly helping early-stage founders as they look to start and scale, then we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee our Y Combinator and other accelerator partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the business to ensure that every founder&#39;s experience of Stripe is surprisingly delightful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out and oversee the execution of key programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spin up new initiatives that add continuous value to the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of escalation for partners and top startups to grow Stripe’s brand within the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a product feedback loop to internal teams to ensure that we continue to build for the highest potential businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with key internal stakeholders to advance strategic Stripe initiatives for startup founders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate startup ecosystem insights and prepare weekly / quarterly updates detailing business progress, market trends, and product feedback gathered from startup engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in the startup ecosystem and take up speaking opportunities at key startup events that bolster Stripe as the best platform for founders to start and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage your data prowess (SQL, etc) to build out tools that enable us to better serve founders and demonstrate impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and demonstrated ability to cultivate deep, trust-based partnerships with some of the most consequential venture capitalists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the startup ecosystem with startup or investing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced business or technical founder with a passion for helping other founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the startup ecosystem, founder empathy, and ability to build strong partnerships, particularly within the Y Combinator community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first mindset, anything less than perfect is unacceptable to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally with internal and external stakeholders to get new programming off the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder by nature and are excited to launch new initiatives within Stripe that extend surprisingly delightful experiences to best in class founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communications skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hunger and motivation to operate (and thrive) in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility, and who takes initiative with a “no task is too small” and “I’ll get it done” attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-networked individual who is active in the early stage venture capital and startup ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alumni of Y Combinator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand a technical buyer and key moments in their life-cycle where financial infrastructure decisions are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept public speaker, presenter and moderator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience, understands channel partnerships and the value this channel brings to a GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Data skills - conversant in SQL or Python - and willingness to build tools serve our users and measure business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup Products team builds Stripe Atlas and other products that help founders start and run a company, from anywhere in the world. We believe that startups are one of the most effective ways to solve the world&#39;s problems, and we want to give founders a running start — and keep them running. We help founders form their company, raise capital, execute critical legal agreements, access the internet&#39;s best tools, and automate operations while feeling ambitious, smart, and assured. Our goal is to create more startups that get to product-market fit, fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is composed of high-agency, high-ownership product thinkers, who genuinely care about helping founders and making it easier to start and run a startup. Every person on the team is responsible for making our product the best it can be, and for ensuring our roadmap contains the highest impact ships for founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team member on the Startup Products team, you’ll help us understand and talk about the startups that use our products, turning data into clear internal and external narratives, and use analysis to shape strategy and product priorities. You’ll own high-signal metrics and dashboards while also leading deep dives that explain what is changing, why it matters, and what we should do next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delve into the data to glean new insights about how users use our products and how they are building their businesses on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package insights into external-facing content, driving our public storytelling about our users and the startup market, in partnership with marketing and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze product performance, identify trends and anomalies, diagnose drivers, and translate findings into concrete recommendations and synthesis to share with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead analytical deep dives on strategic questions, new product opportunities, founder segments, growth drivers, and the impact of launches or operational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product and business strategy by sizing opportunities, testing assumptions, evaluating tradeoffs, and helping prioritize the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help us build and maintain a streamlined set of internal dashboards to help us understand user behavior and product usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business analytics, management consulting, or another highly analytical role in a technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment, including the ability to choose the right methodology, pressure-test results, and distinguish signal from noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative and collaborative approach to finding new insights in data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication skills, and the ability to package data into easy to understand content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and extreme attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with startups, founders, company formation, fintech, or products serving small and early-stage businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting or applying user research, shaping product roadmaps, or bringing new products from 0→1.&lt;/li&gt;
