&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; Insights: Wrangle large, highly complex datasets using SQL into actionable insights and become the data expert for your business area. Develop metrics and large-scale dashboards to track the health of our user-facing and internal teams. Perform analyses (using SQL &amp;amp; other analytical tools/languages), identify trends, conduct research, build models, all to deliver objective, critical insights that can inform leadership of opportunities, risks, and strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with executives: Create narratives and documents that tell the story of your business area to influence senior Operations leadership and Stripe executive team decision making. Own executive-facing weekly, monthly or quarterly reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management: Influence and drive cross-functional change by partnering with stakeholders across a wide internal network of globally distributed teams, including Ops, Finance, Data Science, Product/Engineering, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence: Design, optimize and drive operational reviews and rhythm of the business. Guide the planning and goal-setting process for your business area, as well as progress checks throughout the year. Bring and consistently apply a ROI lens to all operational decisions, so we can make better-informed trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct internal knowledge sharing sessions to strengthen the team&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re passionate about solving business problems and making a direct impact on business. You thrive in environments with many moving parts and quickly pick up new domain knowledge and technologies (e.g. AI). We’re seeking someone with excellent communication and advanced SQL/analytics abilities. Strong background in Accounting/Finance or prior AI experience is highly preferred, though these can also be developed on the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in STEM major (i.e. Computer Science, Math, Stat, Engineering, etc.) and 4+ years of prior working experience in data analysis fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical ability, proficiency with SQL (minimum of 3 years advanced SQL) and strong understanding of data relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with extremely large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI tools (Claude Code, etc.) and have demonstrated measurable impact from AI in your role or in others’ around you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication, presentation skills &amp;amp; stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in or with Financial Services, Accounting, GTM/Sales, Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise working cross-functionally and with globally distributed teams to drive business and operational goals using data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect the big picture to minute details, toggling between them to set and operationalize strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced environments (e.g. high-growth fintech/tech company, management consulting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Product Manager and Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success team oversees the post-sales lifecycle for Stripe users, ensuring they realize the maximum value of their investment. This partnership drives user success, increases retention and expansion, and supports mutually beneficial renewal outcomes. Few teams provide such a direct impact on the growth of the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Success Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team sits at the center of how Customer Success operates at Stripe. This role shapes both the function’s day-to-day operating model—from leadership forums and territory and compensation design to the systems and cadences that enable execution—and its long-term direction. You will lead annual planning, OKR development, and engagement-model design to ensure CS is positioned to deliver for users and scale effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a true ‘Business Partner’ role; you will serve as a trusted thought partner to Customer Success leadership—combining strategic insight, operational rigor, and hands-on execution. You will help translate CS priorities into actionable plans, drive cross-functional initiatives, and build the operating mechanisms that enable teams to make better decisions, execute consistently, and scale effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy moving between strategic problem-solving and hands-on execution—and bring a roll-up-your-sleeves mindset—this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The near-term focus of this role is on evolving and scaling the foundations of the Customer Success business. This includes strengthening operating models, processes, business cadences, systems, and reporting infrastructure to support a growing and increasingly specialized organization. As a key business partner, you’ll measure and analyze performance, develop forecasts and dashboards, and lead data-informed process improvements that help the CS team operate more efficiently and deliver greater customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to analyze and troubleshoot system challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define operating models for new Customer Success specialisms, including metrics, processes, and cross-functional ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement AI-enabled workflows that improve CSM efficiency, scalability, and customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct analysis and investigation of system operations and workflow management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs into scalable technical solutions and lead their implementation from requirements through delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable, automated reports and dashboards that meet key business and leadership reporting requirement, and reduce manual effort and operational overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the management of CSM territories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance business processes through data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor annual and quarterly OKRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare materials for QBRs and other leadership meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of work experience, with a significant portion in strategic / operational roles at high-growth tech companies or consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort with ambiguity—you take an undefined operational problem, scope it, design a solution, and drive it to completion with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with and holding a high bar across operational design, strategic planning, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working independently with minimal oversight while holding yourself accountable to deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross functionally with senior stakeholders. You&#39;re comfortable bringing an independent and opinionated perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in AI tools in order to automate workflows as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical rigor—you&#39;re comfortable owning data and metrics directly, running your own analyses, and pressure-testing assumptions without relying on a dedicated analytics partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage technical resources and translate business needs into requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience working with Go-to-Market teams including Customer Success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Proficient in SQL&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global GTM Operations team is responsible for overall productivity and effectiveness of the GTM organization, partnering closely with the sales team and teams across Stripe to drive initiatives. &amp;nbsp;This role will partner directly with the head of the global Solution Architecture, whose team is responsible for pre-sales technical assessment and technical validation of Users in partnership with Sales. This role will be expected to drive the rhythm of business, data insights / reporting, strategic initiatives, annual planning and execution. We advance the sales policies, processes and tools to drive revenue and growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an incredible opportunity that plays an integral role in shaping and executing GTM strategies with Sales leaders. &amp;nbsp;Responsibilities include go-to-market design, resource planning, territory alignment and quotas management, sales process optimization, and business analytics. You will also partner with key cross-functional stakeholders, including Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, adjacent Sales Operations teams, Global Systems &amp;amp; Processes, and the Strategy Planning and Insights team to streamline and optimize our internal processes and deliverables (monthly business reviews, weekly forecasting calls, target setting and planning). We are looking for a self-starter who is passionate about their work, detail oriented, analytical and has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity in a high-growth environment, and solving problems with limited oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solution Architecture team is growing rapidly and is in need of a strong strategy and ops business partner that can help scale the operations and drive strategy of the team. This entails a focus on operational projects (process design, business cadences, systems work) and everything related to planning and running their business, including: org design and planning, sales coverage models, setting SOKRs, measuring and providing insights on performance, and process improvement.&amp;nbsp; In addition to engaging with the Solutions Architecture team, you will also be collaborating with numerous cross-functional stakeholders from across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Solution Architecture leadership and cross-functional stakeholders in developing go-to market strategy, resource plan and key performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage operational processes such as territory planning, quota setting, quarterly compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to investigate and conduct analysis on system and operational issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute initiatives designed to optimize team efficiency and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive rhythm of business (weekly business reviews, monthly / quarterly business reviews) with strong operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights on key performance metrics and priorities (e.g. weekly, monthly, quarterly business reviews), identify key roadblocks to progress, and work efficiently to remove them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide business analytic strength to help drive initiatives critical to ongoing growth and provide key insights for business leadership to support strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive critical projects and initiatives and drive alignment with cross-functional teams across the organization by developing detailed project plans with activity based milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee implementation of enabling systems and tools, working closely with internal systems teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales strategy and operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, or operational experience in investment banking, management consulting, private equity, venture capital, or business insights / analytics roles. Knowledge of sales data such as customer accounts, opportunities and revenue. 11+ years of total work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in a related field (e.g. Finance, Business, Engineering, Mathematics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and ​​distinctive problem solving and analysis skills. Ability to solve complex and diverse business problems (commercial, operational, organizational).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills and a structured approach to solving unique business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL and Excel skills to include experience financial modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large data sets, especially in analyzing large imperfect data sets to solve problems and creating scalable reports and dashboards or ad-hoc analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management experience - with strong communication and influencing skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and comfortable dealing with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly, proactively, and concisely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast-paced and frequently changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality. Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, ambiguous and rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or higher degree in an analytical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company or FinTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in BI visualization tools (e.g. Tableau)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce.com as a user and report developer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy &amp;amp; Operations (S&amp;amp;O) team for Infra is responsible for enabling the continued rapid growth and operational excellence of one of Stripe&#39;s most strategic areas - the infrastructure group. This role sits at the intersection of product, engineering, strategy, finance, data, GTM and day-to-day execution, ensuring the infra organization is well-informed, running efficiently and poised to deliver on the future product needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of this team, you will tackle a diverse array of challenges that underpin Stripe’s technical foundations which will span system scalability, platform reliability, and efficiency. You will provide the analytical rigor and operational pragmatism necessary to scale &lt;strong&gt;Stripe’s infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt; in a way that is both technically resilient and fiscally sustainable. Operating with a high degree of autonomy, you will lead critical strategic projects, translate complex system performance and capacity trends into actionable infrastructure requirements, and drive the high-stakes architectural and resource decisions necessary for Stripe’s long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Infrastructure Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team is a vital partner to Stripe’s engineering leadership and the Office of the CPTO, focused on three core pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setting and Driving the Engineering Agenda:&lt;/strong&gt; We design the organizational structures and operating models that enable our infrastructure to scale ahead of the business. We lead critical technical governance forums and synthesize system-level health metrics such as &lt;strong&gt;utilization, latency, and fleet reliability&lt;/strong&gt; into strategic insights for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Capacity &amp;amp; Infrastructure Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; We deliver objective, data-driven strategies for our platform roadmap. By modeling &lt;strong&gt;future infrastructure needs&lt;/strong&gt; against business growth forecasts, we ensure our global hardware and software investments are proactive rather than reactive, bridging the gap between deep engineering requirements and financial reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program/Process Incubation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; We add structure and clarity to ambiguous problems, leading and influencing large cross-functional teams to stand up and define new programs and processes that simplify how we run the business. We lead cross-functional initiatives to stand up new programs focused on infrastructure efficiency and resource optimization without compromising developer velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Infrastructure leadership to define the long-term strategic vision and build the annual operating plans, ensuring alignment with Stripe&#39;s overall company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a pulse on the financial health/cost of Infrastructure including relevant trends, and proactively surface areas of concern or opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own models for in-depth analyses &amp;amp; benchmark key metrics to help inform our overall strategy and make the right growth decisions for Infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obsess over our top infrastructure efficiency metrics, helping to surface, track, and drive initiatives that will move the needle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional execution across priority projects, ensuring alignment between teams (e.g., product, engineering, marketing, sales, support).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement operational systems and processes (e.g., reporting dashboards, planning forums, decision-making workflows) that help the infrastructure group scale efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategy &amp;amp; operations, data science, finance, product management, or similar roles at technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross functional settings, and in a role that spans strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical and first principles thinking (e.g., ability to question how we are working rather than simply executing), and the ability to zoom out to the most important questions &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for digging deep into data and problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data analytics with demonstrated ability in navigating large data sets and/or SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with the the ability to speak to leaders across different teams, such as partnerships, product, engineering, and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in influence without authority environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good balance of business and technical acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to execute with minimal guidance, and in contexts with a high degree of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in Infrastructure strategy (e.g., Compute, Storage, Networking, IT, Security or Developer Platforms), the Payments ecosystem, or high-scale Fintech is highly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to facilitate large-scale technical forums and planning sessions, maintaining a&amp;nbsp; focus on measurable goals, infrastructure SLAs, and ROI-driven outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving creative solutions for capacity and efficiency bottlenecks, with a track record of effectively influencing the roadmaps of cross-functional engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a senior product strategist-operator to support the Risk team. Risk is central to Stripe’s ability to grow safely: the team protects Stripe and our users while enabling durable, responsible growth. In this role, you will have a front-row seat to high-stakes business and product decisions and a direct hand in helping the team identify emerging risks, prioritize the right interventions, and deliver measurable outcomes. If you are a technical strategist who moves quickly, brings clarity to ambiguity, and stays with difficult problems through resolution, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Risk leaders and cross-functional teams across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Finance, Operations, and Strategy. You will create strategic clarity around Risk’s performance, connect business and product signals, pressure-test plans, and mobilize teams when results are off track. The role combines rigorous analysis with hands-on execution: you will not only identify where Stripe should act, but also help drive the work required to change the trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can connect risk signals, data, financial performance, user impact, and product and business strategy. You can find the signal in the noise, form a clear point of view, and either address the problem directly or convene the right people to solve it quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work across Risk and Stripe’s technical and user-facing teams to improve decision-making, strengthen execution, and help Stripe manage risk while serving users well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the signal: Define and maintain the metrics that matter for Risk’s in-year performance, spanning risk outcomes, business impact, operational health, and user experience. Build a disciplined “morning read”—a curated, high-signal view that surfaces emerging issues and drives timely action beyond standard dashboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deep-dive interventions: Run focused “surge” efforts to diagnose and unblock critical goals at risk. Move from symptom to root cause, align teams on the response, and stay engaged until the trajectory has measurably improved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge Risk, Product, and Strategy: Translate long-horizon company and risk theses into in-year priorities and operating plans. Decompose ambiguous opportunities and threats that cut across Product, Risk, Operations, and go-to-market teams into structured workstreams with clear owners and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize for leadership: Anticipate the questions senior leaders will ask and prepare clear, decision-oriented materials that turn complex and unstructured risk signals into diagnoses, options, and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure-test assumptions: Work closely with Risk, Corporate Strategy, Product, and Finance to test whether plans reflect external market dynamics, changing risk patterns, user needs, and Stripe’s execution capacity. Identify gaps early and help teams adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in product strategy, business operations, data analytics, product management, or strategic business performance roles, ideally in high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in product strategy, product management, or GM-style roles with direct ownership of a P&amp;amp;L or a specific business outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply curious about business models and data, probing into signals, understanding trends and customer usage patterns to uncover novel insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of directly driving business growth through analytical insights and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply AI to improve decision-making and operational efficiency, with sound judgment about when and how to use AI tools without sacrificing rigor or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and the ability to understand the technical mechanics of how software products are built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating ambiguous, cross-functional problems and leading high-stakes interventions with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with fintech products or complex financial systems is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating senior leadership and stakeholder discussions that lead to clear decisions and action on business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in risk, payments, financial services, or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders and CXOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in SQL / Python / R and data analysis; ability to self-serve and perform independent deep-dives into complex datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing creative solutions and influencing the roadmaps of cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate how product launches, policy changes, and go-to-market activity affect risk outcomes, user experience, and support operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the company&#39;s most important strategic priorities is to build great products and experiences for Enterprises—and we are at an inflection point in the growth of our Enterprise business, with significant momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise team is responsible for ensuring all of Stripe&#39;s products and services best fit the unique needs of global, modernizing enterprises. Our Enterprise Product extends beyond our APIs and dashboards—to Enterprise executive engagement, our perception in the market, our partner ecosystem, how we collaborate with our users to bring them live, and our users&#39; day-to-day interactions with our GTM and support teams—they&#39;re all part of the Product experience for these users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We focus on expanding and innovating on Stripe&#39;s platform in ways that help the largest and most complex customers run their businesses. Our work is highly cross-functional—partnering with almost every other team at Stripe—to execute on the priorities that matter most to Enterprises and ensure that they are successful on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Enterprise Strategy and Operations team, you&#39;ll build the infrastructure, processes, and organizational muscle to help our Enterprise business scale:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-cutting company strategy projects and collaborate with teams to implement changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with multiple stakeholders across Enterprise and other Stripe teams (e.g., product teams, marketing, sales, support) to achieve the goals of the Enterprise Engine Catalyst. You&#39;ll need to objectively evaluate teams&#39; competing priorities and align stakeholders on the optimal solution for Stripe and our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with senior leaders and cross-functional teams to accelerate progress, develop new operating models, and incubate new programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish new operating models in collaboration with key cross-functional teams, focusing on roadmap development and context alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate annual and long-range planning efforts across teams contributing to the Enterprise segment, and drive alignment with partner teams to ensure a cohesive approach to planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive projects, timelines, and commitments on internal projects and customer deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in strategy and operations, product strategy, product management, or similar roles at technology companies, including highly cross-functional work spanning strategy, product, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical thinking and first-principles thinking (e.g., ability to question how we work rather than simply executing), and the ability to zoom out to the most important questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills with experience managing end-to-end execution of projects and programs that have transformed their company&#39;s operations and delivered quantifiable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with the ability to speak to leaders across different teams, such as partnerships, product, engineering, and sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in influence without authority environments, execute with minimal guidance, and operate in contexts with a high degree of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments ecosystem or Enterprise software experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to extract the key themes and learnings from a program and build business and investment cases based on these insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL or constructing dashboards and structuring advanced data analysis to measure program success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the implications of Stripe ships such as product features, policy changes, and marketing outreach on the user experience and resulting support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have a significant amount of work ahead, which gives you the opportunity to help put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-strategy-and-transformation-team&quot;&gt;About the Strategy and Transformation team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation team helps Stripe’s largest and most strategic users define and execute high-impact business and technology transformations. We work early in the customer lifecycle, alongside account teams and senior customer leaders, to connect business ambition with a practical path to value on Stripe. The team has established foundational Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation Consultant coverage across regions. We are now adding specialist advisors who bring differentiated expertise to the enterprise conversations where Stripe’s role must be understood not simply as a payments provider, but as an integrated financial backbone within a customer’s broader commerce and technology ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation Advisor, Enterprise Commerce Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be the senior strategic advisor for complex enterprise commerce transformations, Stripe integration engagements &amp;amp; pursuits across AMER. You will support and advise integration teams and our users on the most complex multi product Stripe integration engagements. Additionally, you will help customers develop a clear, prescriptive point of view on how Stripe should integrate into their future-state architecture — and what that means for their commerce platforms, order-management systems, ERP and finance estate, customer and loyalty systems, identity, data platforms, fulfillment operations, and engineering organization. You will partner with broader GTM, Solutions Architecture, and Product teams to increase customer confidence in Stripe’s ability to support consequential enterprise transformations. You will engage senior technical and business stakeholders, including CTOs, CIOs, Chief Architects, VP Engineering, and digital or commerce leaders, translating their strategic priorities into an enterprise commerce architecture, sequenced transformation roadmap, and clear implementation principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the opportunities to define the strategic architectural “what” and “why”: the target state, key design principles, trade-offs, dependencies, and path to value. You will also provide technical advisory support to Stripe’s Integration engineers, Solution Architects and Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation Consultants on the most complex opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-you-will-do&quot;&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead architecture advisory for complex enterprise Stripe deployments&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior post-sales architecture advisor to a portfolio of global enterprise users with complex, multi-product Stripe integrations, helping them evolve from an initial solution vision to durable target-state integration and architecture decisions, supported by transformation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Integration Engineers, Implementation Consultants, Engagement Managers, Account Executives, and Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation Consultants to shape post-sales architecture engagements and provide senior guidance, while detailed solution design and implementation delivery remain with the appropriate Stripe teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise user technical teams on architecture-level decisions across the broader enterprise commerce, finance, and data landscape—including system-of-record boundaries, API and event design, data ownership, reconciliation, operational resilience, security and risk considerations, and organizational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation and thought partner for complex enterprise architecture questions during implementation, expansion, and major evolution of Stripe integrations, translating technical trade-offs across Stripe products into clear decisions, dependencies, and business outcomes for customer and Stripe stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape enterprise commerce transformation strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead executive discovery, strategy and architecture workshops for Stripe’s most strategic enterprise prospects and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess a customer’s current commerce and technology landscape, identifying how payments and financial infrastructure interact with commerce, order management, ERP and finance, CRM, loyalty, identity, data, fulfillment, and risk systems and develop a prescriptive future-state point of view for how Stripe can serve as a financial backbone within that architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives—such as international expansion, omnichannel commerce, marketplace growth, subscription transformation, cost optimization, improved authorization performance, or faster product development—into clear architecture and operating-model implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the enterprise-level principles, system boundaries, ownership models, integration patterns, data flows, and migration considerations needed to support the target state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create multi-phased, dependency-aware transformation roadmaps that connect Stripe capabilities to measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Increase confidence in strategic enterprise pursuits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account teams, enterprise service managers, sales leaders, and senior solutions architects to identify pursuits where enterprise commerce architecture expertise will materially improve customer confidence or decision quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage credibly with executive technical stakeholders as a strategic advisor and peer, not as a product vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers understand the practical trade-offs between their current architecture and a future state that uses Stripe more deeply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear executive narratives, architecture artifacts, transformation roadmaps, and decision materials that make Stripe’s role in the customer’s future state concrete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account strategy, opportunity shaping, and value articulation for complex, multi-product enterprise pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define the path from initial architecture vision to implementation scope, while ensuring detailed solution design and delivery ownership remain with the appropriate Stripe teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inform Stripe’s enterprise strategy and product direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring recurring customer architecture patterns, friction points, and unmet needs back to Product, Engineering, and GTM leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging enterprise commerce trends—including AI-enabled commerce and financial operations, omnichannel experiences, embedded finance, platform business models, and global expansion—and translate them into relevant Stripe points of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Stripe’s differentiated perspective on enterprise commerce transformation through internal thought leadership and selective customer-facing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;minimum-qualifications&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in enterprise architecture, technology strategy, digital transformation, management consulting, or senior technical advisory roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience advising large enterprises on complex technology transformation, ideally spanning commerce, payments, financial systems, or customer-facing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage credibly with C-suite and VP-level business and technical leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of enterprise commerce architecture, including relevant systems such as commerce platforms, order management, ERP and finance, CRM, loyalty, identity, fulfillment, and cloud data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of API-first integration, distributed systems, event-driven architecture, cloud platforms, data flows, and enterprise operational models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of payments and financial infrastructure, including acceptance, acquiring, settlement, reconciliation, fraud and risk, compliance, and multi-party payment models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect architecture decisions to business outcomes such as revenue growth, conversion, authorization performance, operational efficiency, resilience, cost, and speed to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and visual communication skills, including the ability to make complex architecture decisions understandable to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading ambiguous, cross-functional strategic engagements from initial discovery through a practical recommendation and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Stripe or comparable payments and financial-infrastructure platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in enterprise retail, marketplaces, platforms, SaaS, travel, media, mobility, or other complex commerce environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across omnichannel commerce, global payment methods, subscriptions, B2B payments, marketplaces, embedded finance, or platform monetization models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise architecture frameworks and methods, such as capability modeling, value-stream analysis, domain-driven design, and transformation roadmapping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on data architecture, reconciliation, risk and fraud operations, AI-enabled financial operations, or commerce personalization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of coaching senior technical practitioners and influencing cross-functional teams without direct reporting authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External credibility through senior customer advisory work, industry speaking, publications, or contributions to enterprise technology or payments communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Managed Support team enables platforms using Stripe Issuing and Treasury to provide high-quality support to their cardholders and account holders without building the full operation themselves. The team delivers branded and specialized support across areas such as account access, card management, transactions, fraud, disputes, and complaints, while owning the operational readiness and ongoing performance of each program. Working closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, and platform partners, Managed Support provides a scalable, reliable, and compliant customer experience as Stripe’s customers launch and grow their financial products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be managing up to 10 Operations Associates and act as their primary point of contact for performance management, coaching and planning. The Associates under your management are responsible for resolving our users’ most challenging and impactful issues, providing exceptional user experience, and contributing to the overall user satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be a fit, you will have a coaching mindset, proven ability to communicate at different levels, a track record of driving operational performance, possess a deep expertise in customer service, and a passion for inspiring a team to deliver an incredible user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the team in troubleshooting and resolving external user issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance, setting clear goals and driving delivery against individual and team KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage capacity, scheduling, workload allocation, and day-to-day priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure team members have the skills, tools, and resources needed to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process improvements that increase productivity, reduce manual effort, and improve the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement by refining team processes and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor team members through structured career development conversations, continuous feedback, and formal performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an engaged, motivated, inclusive, and welcoming team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recruitment and hiring initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience leading operations teams as a team lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and communications skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary planning and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate effectively with multiple, cross-functional stakeholders to achieve results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience mentoring others and are able to constructively provide feedback to others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to motivate the team and keep them engaged in an otherwise structured process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be subject matter experts in the relevant line of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in customer service or internal/external user-facing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in delivering weekly and monthly business metrics and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in new process launch and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s user base and global footprint grows dramatically, we have distinctly unique support problems resulting from both our type of scale and the type of businesses we partner with. The Product Support Operations (PSO) team plays a key role in efficiently solving our users’ issues. As part of our PSO team, you will be a critical driver in delivering exceptional user experiences. This role goes beyond basic troubleshooting—it&#39;s about using your technical expertise, analytical mindset, and project management skills to strategically improve our support systems, processes, and product quality. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an Independent Business, Startup, SMB, or Enterprise and our mission is to provide all Stripe Users with the best support experience possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Quality team sits at the heart of that mission. We are responsible for defining and upholding the standards that shape every user interaction across our support verticals. We believe that quality is not just a score — it is a reflection of the care and expertise we bring to every user, every time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own quality outcomes at your site, leading a team of approximately 6 Quality Analysts spanning multiple support verticals. Your team plays a critical role in upholding the quality standards that underpin the experience we deliver to Stripe&#39;s users and you will be the person who drives that standard forward at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond your team, you will serve as a key voice in the evolution of our quality program and a strategic partner to vertical leads. To be a great fit, you will have a quality first mindset, the ability to translate data into action, a track record of coaching others to grow, and the cross functional credibility to influence without authority across a multi vertical environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own UIQ quality scores across all verticals at your site, driving teams to meet and sustain a minimum 90% quality score&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the final escalation layer for Disputes at your site, ensuring fair, consistent, and well reasoned outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review quality trends for each vertical at your site, identifying patterns and surfacing risks before they become issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete case work to stay close to the day to day realities of the verticals’ subject matter and maintain subject matter familiarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in calibration sessions across verticals to drive alignment and consistency in scoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help lead rubric updates and contribute to the continuous evolution of our quality framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive projects at the quality program level, contributing to broader initiatives that improve how quality is measured and managed across PSO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-level quality reporting for all verticals at your site, providing leadership with a clear and actionable view of performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and recommendations back to vertical leads, translating quality data into concrete operational guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of ~6 Quality Analysts representing verticals including Payments, Revenue Suite, Account &amp;amp; Connect, Money Management, Enterprise, and Community Ops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals and expectations for individual and team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor individuals through structured career development conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide continuous performance feedback and facilitate formal performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement and psychological safety within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive and own initiatives that make the team an engaging and motivating place to work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recruitment and hiring initiatives as the team evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching or leading teams, with a demonstrated ability to manage and develop individual performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a QA or quality assurance capacity within a product support or customer service organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring others and delivering constructive, growth-oriented feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven subject matter expertise in product support or customer service operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work cross-functionally across multiple teams or verticals to drive results and foster partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills — able to identify trends in quality data and translate them into clear, actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary planning and time management skills, balancing people leadership, reporting, and program-level responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering quality or business performance reporting to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience participating in or facilitating calibration sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to rubric development or quality framework design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with new process launches and continuous improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Stripe is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a significant amount of work ahead. This is an opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Managers work cross-functionally to support Stripe’s largest and most complex users. Through trusted relationships, we offer customized, strategic consultation and proactively identify opportunities to help businesses deliver more value to their customers, optimize their technical operations, and accelerate global growth with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategically support Stripe’s largest and most complex users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide a Gold Standard Experience to key stakeholders at your assigned accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the broader Operations team to share current-state context, resources, and knowledge that support a Gold Standard Experience across teams that interact directly with users through support channels, external documentation, product feedback, and product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build long-term user relationships that increase loyalty to Stripe and its products.&lt;/li&gt;
