&lt;p&gt;P-1336&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about helping data teams solve the world&#39;s toughest problems — from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world&#39;s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Product Manager, you will join a team that works diligently to understand and solve our customers’ most challenging problems. We&#39;re hiring across all of our teams, including AI Platform, Genie, Machine Learning, Unity Catalog,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Databricks SQL, ETL, Streaming, and EDA. As part of our 2027 APM cohort, you will have a dedicated manager and mentor as well as connect with product managers, engineers, designers, account teams, other interns, and leaders from across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring for San Francisco, CA, Mountain View, CA, and Bellevue, WA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand customer problem space and establish the rails for viable solution space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype and test early ideas with customers and engineers to validate direction before the team commits to a build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers and designers to ship features on the Databricks platformWork with a team to build features for the Databricks platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your project end-to-end — design, build, launch, and iterate on feedbackManage your project end-to-end, including design, code, launch and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build with scale, quality, and security in mind from day oneLearn about building a platform that scales quickly while maintaining quality and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will graduate in Fall 2026 or Spring 2027 with a bachelors or masters degree in computer science or related engineering practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursuing a bachelor&#39;s or master&#39;s in computer science or a related engineering field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve used AI tooling for both personal productivity and development projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have some first hand experience with SQL and/or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re hands-on and learn by doing — happy to build, test, and iterate your way to an answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use analytical skills to make data-driven decisions (e.g. analyzing product usage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can make complex topics simple and communicate nuance to partners (engineers, customers, field) in both written and verbal form&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re excited to solve ambiguous problems with a collaborative team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You stay curious and keep learning, whether it&#39;s a new technology, a customer&#39;s domain, or a corner of the product you haven&#39;t touched&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
