&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;(GAQ327R299)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is looking for a strategic compensation leader who likes to build. You&#39;ll be a trusted partner to founders and senior leadership in our Go-To-Market (GTM) organization. You&#39;ll work with them to create compensation solutions that help us attract, retain and motivate world-class GTM talent, and you&#39;ll use AI to build the tools that make those solutions scale. This role reports to the Director of Compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we don&#39;t think of compensation as just a number. It&#39;s how we recognize that every employee is an owner and part of our success. We&#39;re looking for someone with a strong foundation and a track record of doing exactly that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it takes to thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is a deeply technical, fast-moving environment, and our GTM organization is a key engine of our growth. You&#39;ll partner with dynamic, data-driven leaders who value rigorous analysis, clear perspectives, and collaborative problem-solving. In this role, priorities can evolve quickly, and you&#39;ll often navigate multiple important initiatives at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We set high standards for this role to support our fast-paced growth. Successful team members in this environment tend to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trust through analytical rigor.&lt;/strong&gt; You present well-reasoned models and effectively articulate complex analysis to quantitative leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate fast-paced priorities with resilience.&lt;/strong&gt; You maintain focus, sound judgment, and positivity when balancing competing deadlines and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer constructive perspectives.&lt;/strong&gt; You confidently partner with senior stakeholders to propose data-backed alternative solutions and drive alignment to finalize decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embrace feedback as a growth tool.&lt;/strong&gt; You extract actionable insights from feedback and respond with clarity and openness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create order from ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt; When there&#39;s no playbook, you build one, and you&#39;re comfortable acting on 80% of the information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are excited by high standards, technical depth, and collaborative strategic discussions, you will find this work deeply rewarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, high-impact role. Expected time on each area:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM compensation solutions and strategic advice (40%)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with GTM leaders to diagnose talent challenges such as competitive attrition, hard-to-fill roles, rapid scaling and reorganizations, and design attraction and retention solutions that fix them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn vague or urgent requests into clear options with explicit tradeoffs, then help leaders reach a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main compensation advisor on strategic executive hires and high-stakes retention situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-enabled lifecycle compensation (30%)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run merit, refresh equity and promotion cycles end to end for global GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build AI tools and workflows that reduce manual work and improve decisions. Examples include offer modeling, retention-risk analysis, cycle quality checks, and self-serve insights for leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot what&#39;s repetitive or error-prone in today&#39;s processes and automate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise compensation frameworks (30%)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale Databricks&#39; global compensation structure, including market pricing models, pay-for-performance design and equity strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build frameworks that solve today&#39;s problems and anticipate the ones coming as we grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quantitative and technical skill is the foundation of this role. Everything else we look for builds on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Quantitative and technical foundation (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert-level analytical modeling.&lt;/strong&gt; You build compensation models from scratch, including cost-of-program scenarios, pay-positioning analysis, attrition and retention-risk modeling, and sensitivity and tradeoff analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Built with AI.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve personally used AI tools (for example LLMs, AI assistants, or automation and agent platforms) to build compensation tools, models or workflows that others rely on. You don&#39;t need to be a software engineer, but you should be able to explain how it works, what you&#39;d improve, and how you checked that its outputs were accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand RSU and option mechanics, vesting design, refresh strategy, and how grant values and share price movement affect cost and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statistical judgment.&lt;/strong&gt; You know when a market data cut is credible, when a sample is too small, and how to present ranges and market pricing without false precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Compensation expertise (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You know your craft.&lt;/strong&gt; Job architecture, compensation frameworks, market pricing, year-end and mid-year pay cycles, global compensation practices, and pay-for-performance design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You know the competition.&lt;/strong&gt; Deep knowledge of competitor compensation, especially new-hire and refresh equity strategy at high-growth and public tech companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You reason from first principles.&lt;/strong&gt; You balance compensation best practice with what the business actually needs, and you can rebuild a framework from its underlying logic when the standard approach doesn&#39;t fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Strategic partnership (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trusted advisor to senior leaders.&lt;/strong&gt; You have a track record of advising executives on sensitive, high-stakes compensation decisions (offers, promotions, leveling, retention, transfers, org changes) and influencing the outcome through data and judgment rather than authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational excellence.&lt;/strong&gt; You connect the dots between systems, stakeholders and programs to deliver compensation programs end to end, accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; You turn complex analysis into a crisp recommendation an executive can act on in one conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Tableau or other BI tools, or building dashboards for leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting GTM or sales organizations at a high-growth tech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling compensation programs through hypergrowth, IPO, or major organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in a quantitative field (for example finance, statistics, engineering), or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
