&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic and experienced Manager to lead a team of high-performing Executive Assistants in Costa Rica &amp;amp; Serbia. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in developing each EA and building processes that enable them to effectively support executives across the company&#39;s G&amp;amp;A functions (Finance, Legal, People, IT, Operations &amp;amp; Security). This position requires an operational leader with excellent communication skills and previous experience managing a team, preferably of 10+ Executive Assistants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Impact you will have:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and Team Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, mentor, and develop a team of 10-15 Executive Assistants aligned to G&amp;amp;A Executives (Executives in Finance, Legal, People, IT, Operations &amp;amp; Security) to ensure high performance and professional growth, while providing direct executive support to 1 Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a liaison between executives, EAs, and other departments to facilitate effective communication and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the daily operations of the G&amp;amp;A EA team, ensuring efficient management of executives&#39; schedules, meetings, and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning and Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the EA Manager and Corp Ops leadership to align the EA team&#39;s objectives with the company&#39;s strategic goals, while establishing the right framework to operate as a Center of Excellence (CoE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Team Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop a structure for the team to function as a cross-functional unit, supporting multiple departments across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we look for:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5+ years of experience managing a team of Executive Assistants or similar roles, or proven track record of strong leadership in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous Executive Assistant experience (minimum 5 years), Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Marketing, IT, HR, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading cross-functional teams or projects within a corporate environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to engage with senior executives to build trust, solicit actionable feedback, and translate insights into team development and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills with the ability to inspire and motivate a diverse team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and a process-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and maintain professional relationships at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to adjust working hours to accommodate different time zones (primarily U.S.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultural sensitivity and ability to thrive in a diverse, global environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English (C1 level or above) and Spanish, with excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
