&lt;p&gt;Team Lead - Platform Monitoring Engineer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced, hands-on Team Lead to shape the future of platform observability and proactive customer monitoring. This is a high-impact technical role for someone who thrives at the intersection of platform reliability, incident response, and customer obsession.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will balance technical depth with people leadership: driving monitoring solutions, alerting mechanisms, and customer-focused incident detection tools, and raising the bar of the engineers around them. You will partner closely with cross-functional engineering teams to investigate and resolve incidents, drive root cause analyses, and champion solutions that improve customer reliability and stability of the Databricks Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead platform incident investigation, coordinating cross-functional teams through rapid detection, mitigation, and resolution to minimize customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct thorough post-incident root cause analysis across infrastructure, services, and cloud providers to identify systemic patterns and prevent future occurrences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design and implementation of customer-focused alerting pipelines and end-to-end observability workflows that expand detection coverage and reduce mean time to detection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation tools, establish reusable monitoring patterns, and resolve reliability gaps that directly impact customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and help structure the on-call rotation, leading by example during high-severity incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal customer stakeholders to design and execute the customers&#39; reliability plan, focusing on observability and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in growing the local team of Platform Monitoring Engineers, including hiring and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the local point of leadership and a connection to the broader global team, aligning local execution with global goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 6 years of experience as an SRE, DevOps Engineer, CRE, Production Engineer, or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience leading engineers, whether as a people manager or team lead, with clear mentorship and coaching responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production-level experience with at least one major cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP) and proficiency in container and orchestration technologies (Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with monitoring, logging, and alerting tools such as ELK, Prometheus, Grafana, PagerDuty, etc. Ability to architect monitoring solutions that correlate metrics, logs, and traces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Python or similar languages with the ability to build production-quality automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning critical phases of the incident lifecycle from detection through resolution and post-mortem analysis in demanding production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to influence cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS, Master&#39;s, or PhD in Computer Science or Computer Engineering, or a related Engineering field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
